Senior Health Officer: As a doctor, you must respect, love and take care of patients, do not discriminate, rich or poor, think that the patient's pain is our pain
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Oeun Borarath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, said that dentists and dentists must respect, love and take care of all kinds of patients, do not discriminate between rich and poor and think of the pain of patients Is our pain too.
Dr. Oeun Borarath said, "According to the ethics of health professionals, dentists and dentists must respect, love and care for all types of patients, do not discriminate between rich and poor and think of the pain of patients. It is also our pain to improve the well-being, quality of life of our people and cultivate a strong sense of patriotism and national unity.
Oral health is an important part of everyone's general health. Good oral health increases the family economy and society grows better and can contribute to the development of the nation. On the contrary, poor oral health leads to the loss of time, money, resources, and countless other benefits.
In this regard, in order to ensure professional dignity and to ensure the quality and safety of oral health services, the Ministry has prepared a law on the management of the private medical profession, which has already been approved by the National Assembly. At the same time, the Ministry has established the Dental Commission to manage and eliminate anarchy in the health sector.
In fact, in order to increase the quality and capacity, it is essential that all of our dentists continue to strive to learn new technologies from our experienced seniors, as well as to collaborate with international dentists to enhance our capabilities. To be more accurate.
Therefore, the Dental Conference and Exhibition, which is attended by many well-known international speakers to present and share new digital work experiences to our dental students, is to increase the quality and ability to provide services. Dentistry for our people is better.
This is a testament to the fact that the Dental Association of Cambodia has well implemented the education and training to be sustainable every year for dentists in Phnom Penh, as well as from other provinces. According to Dr. Oeun Borarath.
At the same time, Dr. Oeun Borarath also expressed his deep appreciation and gratitude to the professors who came from neighboring countries and reflected the willingness to participate in the development of health and science in Cambodian society, especially in the field of dentistry. At present.
