The 288th Explosive Ordnance Disposal Team carried out its mission without fear of exhaustion under the Sahara sandstorm, hot weather with temperatures reaching 53 degrees Celsius.
The reception ceremony for the Cambodian Blue Hat Forces was held in the presence of Major General Sem Ratana, Deputy Director General, Senior Representative, General Sem Sovanny, Deputy Chairman of the National Commission and Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center, and other Blue Hat Army leaders at VIP Airport.
After the Phnom Penh International Airport, all forces were prepared to be tested for Kovid 19 and malaria, and to continue to be vaccinated against Kovid 19, the fifth dose to ensure that all Cambodian forces are completely safe. From illness after completing its mission.
On that occasion, Major General Sem Ratana, on behalf of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense and Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Chairman of the National Committee and General Sem Sovanny, welcomed the return visit. Of Royal Cambodian Armed Forces fighters from a one-year mission in the Republic of Mali.
Lt. Gen. Sem Ratana stated that the peacekeeping mission of the Cambodian Blue Hat Forces in Mali is the eighth year and the 288th Explosive Ordnance Disposal Squadron is the eighth to successfully carry out its mission. Brilliant that has brought honor and prestige to the motherland of Cambodia.
In addition to the busy operation of the above mission, the 288th Explosive Ordnance Disposal Squadron has actively contributed to a number of humanitarian activities in its area, such as: Donating medicine to three local hospitals, sending a team of female doctors. One medical examination and treatment for the people, one time distribution of study materials, clothes and food to more than 300 orphans.
Mr. Chea Chanto Celebrates the 44th Anniversary of January 7 Victory Day in Kampong Thom Province
(Kampong Thom): Dr. Chea Chanto, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee and Chairman of the Kampong Thom Provincial Party Working Group, participated in the celebration of the 44th Anniversary of the Victory Day on January 7, 1979 - January 7, 2023 in Kampong Thom Province on January 9, 2023
On the occasion of celebrating the 44th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day in Kampong Thom province, Mr. Chea Chanto quoted and read the speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party to the commemoration ceremony. 44 of the Victory Day on January 7 as well.
The CPP aims not only to lead the country for 40 or 50 years, but to lead the nation forever.
Dr. Chea Chanto stated that for the past 44 years, no political party has been able to compete with the People's Party. Some political parties have developed from small to large, while others Leading the nation, but not yet able to control its own members, how can it be left to lead the Mexican nation?
In which, Mr. Chea Chanto called on all people to be ready to go to the polls in July 2023 to elect Samdech Techo Prime Minister to lead the country in peace, economic and social development.
Preah Vihear Provincial Administration Celebrates the 44th Anniversary of the Victory Day on January 7, Senior Minister Meas Sophea calls for joint protection of the achievements of the January 7 spirit
(Preah Vihear): In the morning of January 9, 2023, Preah Vihear Provincial Administration celebrated the 44th Anniversary of the Victory Day on January 7 (January 7, 1979 - January 7, 2023) at Preah Vihear Provincial Hall. Senior Minister Meas Sophea called for joint protection of the achievements of the spirit of January 7 for the benefit of future generations.
This morning's "January 7" Victory Day celebration was attended by Mr. Prak Sovann, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, Mr. Long Sovann, Advisor to the Royal Government, Ms. Chak Heng, Senator, and Provincial Leaders, Commander-in-Chief Borders, commanders of the three forces, civil servants in departments, units, district and municipal authorities, teachers, students and many other people.
Mr. Meas Sophea called on the people to work together to maintain the achievements born from the spirit of Victory Day "January 7" and to protect the peace in order to maintain the opportunity to build a more prosperous society.
He also sent a message of greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party and other leaders in the Royal Government of the Cambodian People's Party to send to the students present. In this whole ceremony.
He said that January 7 was the day that the Cambodian people escaped the brutal massacre led by Pol Pot. At the same time, he also recalled the grief, hardship, desolation of the Cambodian people, as well as the brutal massacre, as well as the devastation and destruction of the nation, causing the entire national economy to fall to zero.
In addition to commemorating the difficult situation of the people and the devastation of the national economy in the genocide of 3 years, 8 months and 20 days, the Senior Minister also highlighted the resistance movement of the national leaders, including: Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Samdech Thamma Pothisal, Chea Sim and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as well as many other heroes, heroines and patriots, sacrificed their lives to liberate the country from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Thai health minister says his country has decided to lift restrictions on foreign travel. The 19-year-old Kovid, who announced last weekend the requirement for foreign travelers, has been shown proof of vaccination. This was released by the AFP news agency on Monday, January 9, 2023.
The decision replaces a new policy announced last Saturday by the Thai Civil Aviation Authority before China reopened its borders on Sunday. The policy stipulates that all foreign passengers must be presented with 19 vaccinations or given a certificate that they have been cured of the virus in the last six months.
