Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport announces the opening of 50 outstanding students and offers 100% scholarships
(Phnom Penh): The good news for students and the public who are looking for a study in a profession that is in the market in Cambodia can apply for the competition to have the opportunity to become an outstanding student to receive a scholarship 100% free study period 4 to 5 years according to each major from Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport for the academic year 2022-2023.
In the announcement of Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport received by Fresh News on January 9, 2023, said that the Institute is opening opportunities for students and the general public who are looking for scholarships to continue their studies. Bachelor. Currently, the institute has opened the application process for the third generation of students in the academic year 2022-2023, with a total selection of 200 students to enroll.
Out of 200 candidates who will compete for admission to the institute, 50 candidates who pass the exam with the highest score will receive a 100% scholarship for free study for 4 to 5 years, depending on the specialty. On another occasion, the Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has given priority to women by providing 50% scholarships for the 200 female candidates who pass the exam.
It should be noted that Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport is a public higher education institution that is training students in 6 majors, including: Road, Highway, Bridge, Railway and Port Construction, Sewage System, Skills Economics and land transport management, logistics and supply chain management skills, cruise skills and ship engine skills.
The Chinese military said it was conducting military exercises around Taiwan on Sunday, the second such exercise in less than a month. In late December 2022, Taiwan claimed that 43 Chinese warplanes had flown across the central line of the Taiwan Strait, an unofficial buffer zone between Taiwan and China.
China has led nearly regular military exercises near Taiwan after former US House of Representatives Speaker Nancy Pelosi visited Taiwan in August 2022.
Russia's Defense Ministry says 50 Russian soldiers have returned to Moscow for medical and psychological treatment. "Under an agreement reached on January 8, 50 Russian soldiers have been released from territory occupied by the Kiev regime," the Russian Defense Ministry said in a statement.
The Ukrainian government has acknowledged Russia's claims and said 50 Ukrainian soldiers have also been released under the agreement.
This morning, Samdech Techo and Chinese Ambassador Preside Over the Groundbreaking Ceremony for the National Road from Skun to Kampong Cham
On the morning of Monday, January 9, 2023, the infrastructure development process has begun for the welcome of early 2023. The work to expand and improve the quality of National Road No. 7 from the roundabout of Cheung Prey district town to Kampong Cham provincial town will start. The ceremony will be presided over by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Vinthean.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that the project to expand and upgrade the quality of National Road No. 7 has a total length of more than 45 km from the roundabout of Skun town, Cheung Prey district to the roundabout at the base of the Kizuna Bridge in Kampong Cham. Construction of 9 cm thick AC concrete pavement and widening of the road body from 2 lanes to 4 lanes, each lane is 3.75 meters long and the park is 1.5 meters wide.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, the reconstruction of National Road 7 is in response to the current progress of the country, especially the volume of traffic and the growth of transportation, which has increased dramatically from day to day. To one day.
This section of national road also contributes to the promotion of tourism in Kampong Cham province, which has ancient temples, natural resorts and historical culture.
In addition, this section of the national road will facilitate the connection of the transportation of goods and products of Kampong Cham and the border provinces to the Tonle Beit port, which is under construction for export to local and international markets. Waterway.
