The Civil Aviation Authority of Thailand (CAAT) said in a statement on Saturday that from next Monday morning, all foreign arrivals must confirm that they have been vaccinated or provide a certificate of identity. Healed from Kovid-19 in six months.
Passengers who have not been vaccinated must present a medical certificate that explains why they were not vaccinated.
The Thai Civil Aviation Authority (CAAT) said the airline would be responsible for reviewing documents before boarding, and also posted a list of required vaccines on its website.
Vaccination requirements were lifted in October last year, but were reinstated when China reopened its borders following the easing of its zero-Kovid policy.
The new measures do not apply to Thai passport holders or passengers passing through Thailand.
