(Kampong Speu): A baby calf was rescued by the Wildlife Alliance (WA) on January 6, 2023 after the team received information that a calf was trapped. In the Oral Wildlife Sanctuary, Kampong Speu Province. The cub injured his right front leg.
At this time, the baby was sent to the Phnom Tamao Wildlife Rescue Center to save lives and treat diseases. If not rescued in time, the calf that separates the herd from its owner may die. The calf was trapped at the same location where a calf was trapped and rescued in June 2021, but died.
On behalf of the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, thanked the WA Wildlife Rescue Team for its efforts to save the world's rare wildlife, as well as other wildlife.
He said that WA, together with the Cardamom Mountain Protected Area Communities, has been actively involved with the Ministry of Environment in protecting and conserving natural resources and wildlife in the Cardamom Mountains Protected Areas. .
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra noted that communities that have seen trapped animals seeking intervention to save animals have shown an understanding of the importance of biodiversity and participation in wildlife conservation. The Ministry of Environment and conservation partners will continue their efforts to launch a zero-trap campaign to increase public awareness and participation in protection and conservation.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that traps and rifles are the hidden killers of wildlife in Cambodia every day, which needs to be prevented and suppressed from being taken into protected areas. Tens of thousands of traps have been removed from protected areas, and hundreds of firearms and ammunition have been confiscated in recent years.
In order to participate in the protection and conservation of wildlife, especially rare wildlife in the world that is present in Cambodia, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment called on all people to stop eating wild animals and do not believe that eating wild animals provides Good health. At the same time, the relevant authorities will enforce the law against the perpetrators of animal slaughter without exception.
