(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, led professional officers to visit all night to solve the problem of the collapse of the second dam of Anko Kbal Chhay Water Supply Company, which caused damage and collapse of the water pump to bring water. Go to 3 water purification stations as well. In this regard, the Governor of Sihanoukville confirmed that the supply of clean water to the people of Sihanoukville as a whole will be disrupted by about 50 percent.
He said that normally there are two machines that have to run every day, but due to this problem, only one machine is running wastewater. Although not enough, but not at all.
Four teams are divided to deal with this task urgently, including:
Team 1: A team of mechanics must repair the pump head damaged by the dam collapse as soon as possible.
Task 2: Electrical experts who will deal with the damage caused by the power outage during the dam collapse to prepare for the pumping of water to be filtered to produce clean water when the first team is ready to repair the dam Once clean water is produced, the supply to the city will resume. Currently, some transformers and light poles have collapsed.
Task 3: Dam repair team, including the team of 3 existing company mechanics, and the provincial governor also instructed the Department of Public Works and Transport to bring 3 more machines and vehicles. Transport 3 more land units to support this work as soon as possible.
Team 4: Pipe connection team to pump water from the first station to the filter at the second station and continue to clean the filter at the third station as well.
On that occasion, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun also appealed to the people not to worry about the lack of water, even though the second dam collapsed, but the first pool, the third pool and the fourth pool with water. Much to supply the people in the future, just some difficulties today, tomorrow or maybe tomorrow, that is, within 3 days.
He said that there is still one machine that can supply 50% clean water. He called on people to save water in these three days. For unnecessary use, it should be temporarily suspended, such as watering grass, watering the garden and so on.
