Understand business: Falling shipping prices and reopening China as an opportunity to boost Cambodia's agricultural exports
(Phnom Penh): Prices of inland waterways and land transport from Cambodia to China have fallen back to normal after rising sharply after China implemented the Zero Kowit measure and during last year's fuel surge. Let Cambodia's exports to this country face obstacles.
Experts in the field of transport and export of agricultural products understand that the decline in transportation prices and the announcement of China's easing of measures 19 measures are an opportunity for Cambodia to increase exports of goods, especially agricultural products.
Mr. Chea Chandara, President of the Association of Freight Forwarders and Supply Chains, told Fresh News that the current price of water transport from Sihanoukville and Phnom Penh to China has dropped to more than $ 200 to $ 400. In the past, shipping costs have risen by about $ 600 to $ 800 per container.
He added that China's reopening of the country will help revitalize Cambodia's transport sector by transporting, exporting and importing various goods.
"I also note that Chinese investors have bought Cambodian agricultural products, so I think Cambodia's agricultural exports will increase after the reopening of China," he said.
He said it was not the shipments to China that reduced the cost of shipping from Cambodia to the United States and Europe, which had previously risen from more than $ 10,000 to $ 20,000, to between $ 1,000 and $ 2. Thousands of dollars per container today.
"I have high expectations for the export of Cambodia's agricultural products as well, especially before the traditional Chinese New Year in the Chinese market, there is a high demand for agricultural products such as lentils, bananas, durian, etc." .
