It should be informed that the River Festival has been organized 6 times, including in 2015 in Kratie, 2016 in Stung Treng, 2017 in Kampong Cham and Tbong Khmum, 2018 in Kandal, 2019 Made in Kampong Chhnang province and in 2020 made in Battambang province. However, due to the spread of Kovid 19, the government also suspended the tourism event for two years, in 2021 and 2022.
On the afternoon of January 6, 2023, the Ministry of Tourism and Administration of Kampong Thom Province also chaired a meeting to prepare for the 7th River Festival, chaired by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province. Leaders of civil servants from relevant ministries and institutions at Kampong Thom Provincial Hall.
On that occasion, Minister Thong Khon said that with the improvement of the situation of Kovid 19, the Royal Government has decided to organize the 7th River Festival in Kampong Thom Province from March 8-10, 2023. Face and can continue to the 11th and 12th because Saturday and Sunday.
The Minister said that the organization of the river festival in Kampong Thom province is due to the Stung Sen flowing down to the Tonle Sap Lake, especially in Kampong Thom is in the middle of the road from Phnom Penh and Kampong Cham to Siem Reap and Preah Vihear. An important tourist destination.
He also stressed the need to organize exhibitions of local products produced by local people. For this local product fair, he would like to encourage as many agricultural handicraft products as possible to be sold at the event to boost exports on the spot.
He added that in addition to showing the cultural potential of historical sites to show to the people as well as tourists understand that Cambodia has a long history and culture, "Cambodia is the Kingdom of Culture, the Kingdom of Water."
The director of the department added that Kampong Thom is halfway between Phnom Penh, Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Siem Reap, Preah Vihear, so tourists will be able to visit the River Festival before continuing to visit Siem Reap and other destinations.
He added that Kampong Thom province also has many tourist destinations, especially the heritage area of Sambor Prei Kuk temple, or can connect tourist destinations to Preah Vihear and Preah Vihear temples, and other destinations such as ecotourism, agriculture, tourism, tourism, etc., which are all Potential for tourism.
At the same time, Mr. Nguon Rattanak, the provincial governor, also committed to co-organize this river festival well, because he also had the experience of co-organizing the river festival in Battambang province once in 2020 when he was the governor of Battambang province before moving Come to Kampong Thom province.
