(Phnom Penh): Under the initiative of Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, this morning, January 7, 2022, the Ministry of Justice organized the 2023 Voluntary Blood Donation Program under the theme "Give Blood, Give Hope" to join the celebration. Celebrate the 44th anniversary of the Victory Day on January 7 and to participate in social and humanitarian activities.
This voluntary blood donation program is organized under the auspices of the Ministry of Justice in collaboration with the CPPCC. Justice Sector, National Blood Transfusion Center and Justice Club, as well as voluntary blood donations from leaders, advisors, assistants and civil servants of the Ministry of Justice, as well as students of the Royal Academy of Judicial Professions and professionals in the field of justice. A total of more than 300 people.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, said, "This blood donation is for the sole purpose of saving lives. "The need for blood is a real need at the forefront, as there are many patients who are hospitalized and in need of blood to save their lives."
"So far, despite the advancement of health technology, no developed country has been able to produce artificial blood, that is, blood is only produced by the human body itself," he said. If there is no blood donation, there is no blood to save the lives of those who are in need of blood.
