UPDATE: Traffic Police in Takeo Province Target National Road No. 3 in Tram Kak District to Stand Up for Investigation After Criticism of Fines and Violence Against Chinese Men
(Takeo): The traffic police force of Takeo Provincial Police, targeting National Road 3 in Tram Kak district, has been removed to investigate after being fined for arresting a foreigner. Exceeding the legal limit and leading to the use of violence until it is shared on social media.
Speaking to Fresh News on the afternoon of January 7, 2023, Brigadier General Chheng Rattanak, Deputy Police Commissioner of Takeo Province, confirmed that the target police officers on National Road 3 in Tram Kak District are currently conducting additional interrogations. Temporarily wait for the results of specific investigations to report to the leadership and take action or enforce force discipline.
Brigadier General Chheng Rattanak claimed that through this case, the leadership of the Takeo Provincial Police has decided to stop the purpose of enforcing the law in this place to avoid prejudice with the people.
Please be reminded that a Chinese person who is likely to be an investor in Cambodia posted a harsh message on a traffic police officer on National Road 3, km 68, in Tram Kak district, Takeo province (km 68). He was initially fined up to $ 100 for speeding, which he claimed was not illegal and led to violence, injuring the Chinese man.
In addition to narrating the story of the target police on National Road 3 in Tram Kak district, Takeo province, who was fined for no reason and did not issue the bill, the Chinese national also pointed out that the actions of this police officer seemed to tarnish Cambodia's image. Even more so.
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, this morning, January 7, 2023, accompanied by Dr. Yuk Sambath, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Health and Health Technical Officer, with the participation of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor Phnom Penh and all construction teams inspected and accelerated the work at the "Techo Santepheap" National Hospital.
Dr. Yuk Sambath continued that under the highest guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the National Hospital will be ready for completion by the end of June and will be able to receive patients from both districts. 6 as well as other districts in Phnom Penh and bordering provinces.
In addition, Dr. Yuk Sambath stated that in the face of the uncertain situation of 19 global Kovid infections and the evolution of new viruses, some parts of this hospital will have to be prepared. As soon as possible to prepare for any bad situation that may occur, so for Cambodia under the strict and prudent leadership of Samdech Techo, we are ready to withstand the spread of this vicious virus.
Please note that this large national hospital is an initiative by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
