The movie "Tuk Srey Pdey Prat" will be screened this evening
(Phnom Penh): The movie "Tuk Srey Srey Pdey Pratt" shows the sad and tragic real life story of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross will be screened on Saturday evening. This is January 7, 2023.
The song "Touk Srey Pdey Prat" describes the real life story of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who had to face hardships and distance from Samdech Techo Hun Sen. He was about 5 months pregnant with Hun Manet.
For the cause of the nation and the people, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, along with four other comrades, on June 20, 1977, fled from the Koh Thmey Village Command, Memot District, to Vietnam, seeking support to overthrow the regime. Genocide of Pol Pot.
The distance for the cause of the nation and the people is the most difficult and sad time for Samdech Techo Hun Sen, because this distance does not know what the fate is? Do not know whether to die or live? In particular, this separation has to leave his beloved wife who is pregnant with a 5-month-old baby.
Samdech Techo's departure is already a hardship and a torture of the heart. But Samdech Kittipritthbandit, the wife living in the district, is even more difficult. As a woman with an unfaithful husband, the Khmer Rouge had to live a secret life to ensure the safety of her life from the Khmer Rouge regime. In addition, weak, pregnant women are subjected to harassment and forced to work without food or shelter.
These are the contents highlighted in the song "Tuk Srey Srey Pdey Pratt". The content of the song also highlights the patience and overcoming all obstacles of Samdech Kittipritthbandit in giving birth to a child and trying to take care of the child in a difficult situation until reuniting with Samdech Techo on February 24, 1979 .
The song "Touk Srey Pdey Prat" was filmed by the Association of Friends of Voluntary Arts to Help Society, combining scenes with modern recording techniques to create a more attractive music film. In particular, a higher interest was incorporated into the reality of the struggles and hardships of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit during that struggle.
Mr. Heng Long said that the movie "Tuk Srey Pdey Pratt" was carefully produced for about nine months at a cost of about 130,000 US dollars.
