Victory Day "January 7" is a day that people across the country cheered because it was the day their lives were liberated from the abyss of the Pol Pot genocide. But Victory Day was not celebrated by politicians opposed to the ruling CPP. They tried to distort and sow that the day of victory "January 7" was the day that Vietnam invaded Cambodia.
At the inauguration ceremony of a pagoda in Chhlong district, Kratie province, Dr. Hun Sen, a permanent member of the Cambodian People's Party and the next prime ministerial candidate of the Cambodian People's Party, presented some aspects to discuss whether "January 7" is Liberation or the day when Vietnam invaded?
Dr. Hun Manet questioned that before the liberation on January 7, 1979, did the Democratic Kampuchea regime or the Khmer Rouge regime stop killing people?
According to interrogation of people who witnessed the regime, until the end of 1978, the Khmer Rouge regime continued to kill people, there was no policy to stop killing people. Therefore, without the liberation movement, the Cambodian people would still be slaughtered or tortured during the regime.
Dr. Hun Manet emphasized that "the overthrow of the Khmer Rouge, the end of the genocidal regime, the end of Pol Pot's rule in 1979 drove the Khmer Rouge to stop killing, equal to saving more than 5 million lives." This is true. ”
"Wanting you to be angry is your right," he said. But ask if the result of the overthrow of the genocidal regime by the United Front for National Salvation, backed by the Vietnamese Volunteer Army, was to banish the killing of 5 million people? "If the result is to save the lives of 5 million people, it is the success of our nation."
Dr. said that the overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot would not have been possible without the support of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army, because at that time the Cambodian resistance movement, which had a circle of more than 10,000 people, could not. Can not defeat the Khmer Rouge regime.
At the same time, international organizations do not have a policy of overthrowing the Khmer Rouge regime, even though they are aware of the suffering of the Cambodian people through refugees. This is according to a foreign diplomat who confirmed to Mr. Hun Manet.
Mr. Hun Manet said that at that time, Cambodia had no choice but to rely on Vietnam or Thailand to help defeat the Khmer Rouge regime.
Mr. Hun Manet also said that the day of victory on January 7, because the movement led by the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party, but for the benefit of all Cambodians.
