Ministry of Agriculture and Ministry of Environment issue joint notice on forest fire prevention and control measures
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Ministry of Environment on January 6, 2023 issued a joint statement on measures to prevent and prevent wildfires after the Ministry noticed that every forest fire The year has caused problems for the loss of forest resources, flooded forests and natural resources in protected areas.
In a statement obtained by Fresh News, the two ministries noted that the main causes of the most frequent wildfires in the dry season were deforestation and planting of agricultural crops. Nomadic agriculture, encroachment on forest land for illegal settlement, illegal encroachment on state land, burning of forests to catch animals, arson in the forest by human negligence and so on.
Seeing all these factors, the Ministry of Agriculture and the Ministry of Environment have introduced eight important measures for the relevant ministries, institutions and agencies to implement together.
