General Vong Pisen Celebrates the 44th Anniversary of January 7 Victory Day in Pearang District
(Prey Veng): This morning, January 7, 2023, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, presided over the celebration of the 44th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day. January 1979 - 7 January 2023) in Pearang district, Prey Veng province.
In front of the ceremony, which was attended by more than a thousand members, General Vong Pisen read a speech by Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and President of the Cambodian People's Party, on the meaning of the historic Victory Day over the Pol Pot genocidal regime. Who saved the nation and the people of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech also highlighted the memory of the great merits of countless cadres, female soldiers, patriots and soldiers of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army who sacrificed their lives to liberate the Cambodian people from genocide and defense. The revival of the people.
General Vong Pisen emphasized that for the past 44 years, starting from the January 7 victory, the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen has worked hard to rebuild and develop the country from scratch to everything, including the process of democracy. Respect for human rights, national economic development to grow every year, especially to make the society peaceful, ensure political stability, security throughout the country.
On the basis of this great sacrifice and achievement, General Vong Pisen instructed the whole program to clearly evaluate the selection of leaders who are patriotic, capable of seeking peace, defending peace for the peace of the people. Samdech Techo Hun Sen not only liberated the nation from the Pol Pot regime, Samdech Techo also saved the people from the waterfall of Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "The spirit of January 7 is immortal in the hearts of all Cambodians and all generations to come. We are all committed to keeping the spirit of January 7 stronger and brighter." . The past 44 years have been 44 years of unity, 44 years of heroic struggle and 44 years of victory for the Cambodian people. ”
Samdech Techo emphasized that our struggle has transformed the homeland from the land of the dead to the most proud land, which has increased our faith and strengthened our commitment to achieve new achievements in socio-economic development and development. Building a glorious future for future generations without the recurrence of wars, national divisions and genocides like in the past.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister added that a nation with national unity, decisive defense of its independence and freedom can not be defeated by any external force, so must work together to preserve all the noble achievements of the society to survive and Strong in all circumstances. In this spirit, we are all determined to safeguard the peace and national unity that we have achieved with the utmost difficulty, so that it will remain stable and not be destroyed by any person or power.
US targets supply of Iranian drones to Russia in new sanctions package (Video inside) (Washington): The United States on Friday announced new sanctions targeting Iranian drone suppliers, Washington claims That was used by Russia to attack Ukraine's civilian infrastructure. This was released by the AFP news agency on Saturday, January 7, 2023.
The US Treasury Department said in a statement that it had sanctioned the division director as well as a total of six board members of QAI, which the ministry described as one of Iran's major arms manufacturers, with the role of design and manufacture. Drones. The company itself has been under US sanctions since 2013.
"We will continue to use the means we have in place to try to prevent Putin from using the weapons he was using in the brutal war in Ukraine," said US Treasury Secretary Janet Yellen. Friday's move would freeze US assets of those sanctioned individuals and bar American citizens from doing business with them.
The United States has in the past sanctioned companies and individuals accused of producing or transferring Iranian drones to Russia for use in the war in Ukraine. Tehran has acknowledged sending drones to Russia but claimed it preceded the war of aggression that erupted in February 2022, while Moscow has denied using them in Ukraine.
