Minister Thong Khon warns students in New Zealand to help promote Cambodian tourism
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, instructed Cambodian students studying in New Zealand, in addition to striving to excel in their studies, also to help promote national tourism as well as peace and development in the country to contribute to attracting visitors. Tourists from that southern country.
Minister Thong Khon's remarks were made to allow 16 Cambodian students who have received scholarships from the New Zealand Government to pay a courtesy call and receive recommendations on January 6, 2023 at the Ministry of Tourism.
On that occasion, Mr. Put Sopheak, a representative of the above students, reported that the scholarship was obtained through the assistance of the Government of New Zealand for the development of human resources, society, sustainable economy in developing countries.
Mr. Put Sopheak continued that the 16 winning students are officials working in public, private and non-governmental organizations such as the National Bank of Cambodia, General Department of Taxation, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Office of the Council of Ministers, ACE School, Asia-Pacific Development Bank. World Vision, Asia Foundation and the Pioneers of Cambodia.
At the same time, Minister Thong Khon instructed all 16 Cambodian students studying in New Zealand to help promote tourism, peace, and development in Cambodia in order to contribute to attracting tourists from the southern countries.
Mr. Thong Khon continued that Cambodia is now ready to receive international tourists, especially the Royal Government has managed the situation of Kovid 19 well, the people are friendly and have many tourist destinations while the tourism movement. Domestic is continuing to rise, which is a credible sign from tourists from abroad.
Minister Thong Khon advised students that even if studying in the country, Cambodian students must take into account the development of the country to contribute to the building of the nation, while the country has a lot of human resources, but still not enough. That, too, is always needed.
He continued to advise everyone to take part in maintaining peace and the achievements that the Royal Government has worked to build, because this peace has given people the opportunity to build socio-economic status, students have the opportunity to continue their studies, build human resources, such as the opportunity that students have Continuing to study abroad also depends on peace factors.
