This front then formed on December 2, 1978. With the support of the Vietnamese side, the Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation, with its greatest and sharpest resistance, completely overthrew the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime throughout the country on January 7, 1979.
At the same time, Dr. Kim Sandepheap stressed that because of the Cambodian People's Party, the people and the country were saved from the abyss of death, continue to live in freedom, peace, territorial integrity and development forever. That is why the Cambodian people have named the Cambodian People's Party as the angel of salvation, protection and development of the people and the country.
The forum was attended by Mr. Kao Kosal, Director General of Trade Promotion of the Ministry of Commerce, Mr. FU Jinming, Deputy Director General of the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region Department of Commerce of the People's Republic of China, as well as investors from both countries.
The forum on "Promoting Trade and Investment between Cambodia and China (Guangxi Province") was organized during the visit of the delegation of Jiangxi National Chamber of Commerce to Cambodia and the purpose of the meeting was to discuss the feasibility study and cooperation. Investment opportunities to strengthen and expand trade cooperation by linking the two countries.
He said that in the last 10 years before the Kovid 19 crisis, Cambodia had achieved high economic growth of around 7% per year, as well as significantly reduced poverty and social inequality. Became a low middle income country in 2015.
Mr. Kao Kosal said, "All these achievements have pushed Cambodia to set a long-term vision and aspirations to become a high-middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country in The coming 2050. "
"In terms of bilateral trade, I would like to inform the forum that the total trade volume between Cambodia and China in 2021 will reach approximately 11.194 million US dollars, of which Cambodia can export to China," he said. "More than 1.510 million US dollars and imports from China more than 9.684 million US dollars, an increase of about 38% compared to 2020."
He added that Cambodia has continued to cooperate with China on many trade-related issues, such as the establishment of nine Cambodian private business centers in some major cities in China to promote potential products. Cambodia promotes Cambodia's tourism culture and trade and investment policy, as well as boosts exports to the Chinese market.
Cambodia and China recently signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Strengthening Trade Cooperation between the General Department of Trade Promotion of the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia and the Department of Commerce of the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, China. The goal is to promote Cambodia's potential products to the Chinese market, which will boost the export of 400,000 tons of Cambodian cassava to China in 2022-2023.
He added that Cambodia-China trade cooperation has been continuously strengthened and expanded under the visionary and cooperative leadership of the top leaders of the two countries, Cambodia and China under the regional framework of the two sides. Establish the ASEAN-China Free Trade Agreement and push for the achievement of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP).
Under the bilateral framework, Cambodia and China signed the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement on October 12, 2020, which came into force on January 1, 2022, paving the way for Strategic partnership and promote economic, trade and investment cooperation between Cambodia and the People's Republic of China.
