Over the years, economic and trade cooperation between China and the Philippines has shown great vitality. China is the Philippines' largest trading partner, largest source of imports and second largest export destination. The two sides identified four key areas of cooperation: agriculture, infrastructure, energy and human culture.
China's "Belt and Road" initiative has been effectively linked to the Philippines' "Build more, build better" concept, and has implemented nearly 40 intergovernmental cooperation projects. This time, Philippine President Marcos visited China, leading a large-scale trade delegation, which can fully confirm that the Philippine side attaches great importance to expanding cooperation with China.
