(Phnom Penh): In the 44 years since January 7, 1979, after the fall of the Khmer Rouge regime, Cambodia has walked the most difficult and dangerous path, but it is the right path to ensure long-term progress. Long and prosperous for the motherland of Cambodia.
Under the reign of the King of Cambodia and under the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister, he has led Cambodian ships to many important achievements in recent years, especially in preventing Successful Kovid 19 outbreak, reopening of the country and rapid economic recovery.
The Cambodian-Vietnamese relationship has developed in many areas, bringing tangible benefits to the people of each country, and is not just a traditional relationship, but also a brotherhood and comradeship. Join the battles that have been shared in the cause of national liberation and national reunification, as well as in the construction and development of their respective nations.
On September 22, 2022, the UN-backed Khmer Rouge Tribunal held its final session, rejecting the appeal of the last surviving Khmer Rouge leader (Khieu Samphan). Of the brutal regime that ruled Cambodia from 1975-1979 and was the only one of three men convicted of genocide during the Khmer Rouge regime that lasted 16 years.
The Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC) has sentenced Khieu Samphan to life in prison based on the atrocities committed against humanity during the Khmer Rouge genocide. It is a final decision and closes the way for protests. This means that the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime has come to an end.
Thus, 44 years after the opening of the new era after the overthrow of the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime, the Kingdom of Cambodia has become a country that adheres to the principles of democracy, the rule of law, peace, political stability, socio-economic development and National unity.
Cambodia has achieved high and sustainable economic growth over the past two decades, moving from a low-income country to a low-middle-income country, and is striving to achieve the vision of a high-income country. The average high in 2030, based on the living standards of the people, continues to grow steadily and on an equal footing with countries around the world.
