(Phnom Penh): January 7, 2023, this year is the 44th anniversary of the Victory Day over the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime. In the context that Cambodia is on the path of liberal democracy, pluralism, multi-party issues on issues also follow. The meaning of January 7 seems to be determined based on political views and positions rather than the value of historical truth.
If we find it difficult to compare the progress of the nation as a whole, let alone compare within our family circle, we can also know what changes have taken place in the family society from 1979 to the present. Body?
Today, we have all kinds of freedoms, from the right to obey all kinds of religious traditions that were not available in the Khmer Rouge era, not even education. Our education is available from early childhood to primary and higher education. All of this is what we have seen about the shift in mental rights.
As for the physical, what we see now, including bridges, roads, schools, hospitals, pagodas, small and large buildings, mushrooming, civilization of people's lives, etc., is not a gift from God. But it comes from the efforts of the government.
In the past, when we wanted to travel from one province to another, from one region to another across the country, or even from home to school, how long did it take us? Travel to all provinces across the country is now possible in the evening. Bridges, roads, schools, hospitals, pagodas, buildings, buildings are irrefutable evidence of achievements after January 7, 1979.
Cambodia, formerly a siege country and politically and economically isolated, is now a country that is actively integrating into regional and global structures and structures and is playing an active role. Equality and equality in all regional affairs and on the international stage.
These are measurable indicators of the growth and development of Cambodia after the liberation on January 7, 1979. Therefore, January 7 is a historical fact and a lesson to remember, to remember the founder of January 7, the angel of national liberation and the people, the restorer of nation building and development, to remember the philosophy of unity, national reconciliation and unity, to remember the father of the founder of peace And engrave a long-lasting culture of peace.
At the same time, the heirs of the 7th of January must continue to maintain the achievements of the 7th of January, but they must not be satisfied with the current achievements of the 7th of January and pray for the 7th of January. The successors of January 7 must set out new perspectives, new strategies and visions in line with the evolution of globalization to create more legacies and achievements for the next generation.
