The gifts of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit were handed over by Mr. Seng Teang, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, to the 395th family of three twins on the morning of January 6, 2023.
The family, who received this precious gift, was born on December 9, 2022, the first of three children, a father named Hak Lyhay, 41 years old, a civil servant and a mother named Am Kunthy, 42 years old, a teacher. Residence: Prek Yeay Hay village, Prek Thmey commune, Koh Thom district, Kandal province.
Mr. Seng Teang said that from 1999 to the present, more than 23 years ago, 395 families gave birth to 3 twins or 4 twins and received a generous donation from Samdech Techo. And Samdech Kittipritthbandit to support the hardships in daily life, especially to raise three twin babies, to be the grandchildren of both Samdech after giving birth.
In addition, Mr. Seng Teang continued that all these donations are not gifts from the Royal Government, donations from the Cambodian Red Cross or donations from parties that serve political activities, instead, these gifts are born gifts. Out of the sincere and thoughtful spirit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who realized the real difficulties for people who have given birth to three or four twin babies.
Due to the poor health of the mother and baby and the fact that the baby is kept in a nutritional bottle, Mr. Seng Teang advised the medical team to continue to monitor the health of the family of three twins. That with a high sense of responsibility and continue to stay in the hospital for a long time before leaving for home.
At the same time, he also instructed the families of the triplets to bring all these gifts, nurture and strive to keep the triplets healthy and have a good future in the future.
Mr. Seng Teang urged the families of the three twins to continue to adhere to the Royal Government's "3 Doom and 3 Defenders" measures so that Cambodia can overcome all 19 cases of Kovid.
