Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara thanked Sokha Hotel for actively developing the Bokor resort. What are the special features of the 108-meter-tall Buddha statue that you should know?
She continued that at the same time, the construction of hotels, resorts, residences and a number of service buildings has also appeared in accordance with the master plan and permission from the Ministry of Taxation, and in addition, the company has also established a fruit and vegetable farm. And pets as well.
Currently, the company has been focusing on the development of a vision for implementation in the area of more than 81,000 hectares, which the Royal Government has given the company the right to invest and develop.
Lok Chumteav Oknha Sok Chantha continued that at the same time, the company is also implementing another project to build a main road, which the Royal Government has allowed to connect from National Road No. 4 at km 158 + 291 to the development area in On Bokor Mountain, which is more than 60 kilometers long.
In addition to investing in the development of infrastructure, construction and services, the company has also focused on the field of faith and religion, which is the culture and traditions of our people for a long time.
The company built a 5-meter-tall statue of Preah Pisnouka at the entrance to Monivong National Park "Bokor", a large statue of Grandma Mao on the hill at km 22, 23.87 meters high and a Neak Ta monument A mountain on the ridge for happiness, prosperity and a place of worship for the people and tourists who come here.
This Buddha statue is the largest and tallest in Cambodia and also among the tallest Buddha statues in the world.
He took the form of the Maravijaya Buddha or the Demon Defender of the Bayon style, the supreme design of Buddhism during the reign of Jayavarman VII in the 13th century.
This Buddha statue was built on the ridge of Bokor Mountain, which is 962 meters above sea level in the five hundred rice fields of Monivong Bokor National Park.
Lok Chumteav Sok Chantha confirmed that this statue will be built of gold-colored concrete, facing east, 108 meters above the ground level to the top of the pillar, which represents his 108 blessings. Perched on a circular pink throne (representing the field of Wat Sangkha, the design of the throne follows the pattern of a part of the diamond pillars of the Elephant Krab Temple of the Kulen style during the reign of King Jayavarman II in the 4th century.
On the ground floor, 248 meters long and more than 100 meters wide, there are four large stairs accompanied by dragon handrails representing the four directions in the style of Angkor Wat in the reign of King Suryavarman II in the 12th century.
On the first floor, there is a board or porch in front of the Buddha statue for religious ceremonies, and there are seven Buddha statues and five ascetics, a total of 12 (representing only 12 months and years) placed around the Buddha. The statue is large and has eight steps (representing the eight directions and the eight nobles) for ascending to the shrine of the Buddha.
For the interior of the ground floor, there will be small Buddha statues on the walls, a place for religious gatherings, a museum, a hall, a lamp post, a place for Vipassana, etc.
The company is currently studying to develop a design for this huge Buddha statue project to become one of the largest Buddhist tourism centers in Cambodia and the world.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara also thanked Sokha Hotel for its active development on Bokor Resort, while the Deputy Prime Minister attended the groundbreaking ceremony for the tallest Buddha statue in Cambodia and the world in his style.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara thanked Sokha Hotel for its active contribution to the development of the Bokor resort area and for initiating the construction of the statue, which will become a major Buddhist tourist center in the Kingdom of Cambodia. And in the world.
