(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism on January 5, 2023 issued a press release on Cambodia, warmly welcoming Chinese tourists, which confirms that Cambodia is ready to welcome Chinese tourists with hospitality. The warmest as the Chinese government will reopen the country on January 8, 2023, just two days away.
China is a large, densely populated country, the largest tourism market in the region and the world, and one of the countries in the region not far from Cambodia. Good transportation, in particular, is a strong strategic partnership, a common destiny, which further demonstrates that the Chinese tourism market is the highest priority market for ASEAN as well as Cambodia.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has been steadily implementing travel facilitation, removing health barriers since 2022, when Cambodia announced the reopening of the country.
Please be informed that Cambodia is the warmest tourist destination because Cambodia is a country that has been evaluated by the World Health Organization as a leading country in providing vaccines to people, both the basic dose and the most boosting dose created. Gain good community immunity and re-open the country, the first socio-economic activity in the region, adhering to the principle of "learning to live with Kovid-19 in a new normal path."
The Ministry of Tourism, relevant institutions and the private sector in the tourism sector are pleased and welcome and ready to welcome Chinese investors and tourists with the warmest hospitality.
According to the daily reports of the Ukrainian military, most of the Russian soldiers were killed in the fierce fighting in the eastern Donetsk region of Ukraine. If the above figures are verified as true, it would be the loss of a large number of Russian troops in just one day.
Meanwhile, the Ukrainian military claimed that one Russian military plane, one helicopter and three tanks had also been destroyed in the past day. Airstrikes by Russian missiles and rockets on Bakhmut and two other cities in the Donetsk region have killed and wounded civilians, but no exact number has been confirmed.
