Cambodia's rice export data for the last 10 years released by Hean Vannhorn, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that in 2022, Cambodia exported more than 200,000 tons of rice to Europe, an increase of 32.1% Compared to the same period in 2021, which accounted for 35% of total exports.
The senior official noted that in the last 10 years, from 2012 to 2022, exports to the EU market have been declining year by year from 66%. 25% of total annual export volume, but will increase slightly again in 2022.
He said the decline in rice exports to China in 2022 was related to exchange rate issues. In the past, the Chinese yuan had a higher purchasing power when the exchange rate was weak, leading to a drop in orders. Another factor is that in 2021, China bought more food in reserve, leaving more rice in stock, thus delaying rice orders in 2022.
He expects that in 2023, rice exports to China will increase after China reopens trade.
At the same time, he confirmed that the agreement or quota for exporting 400,000 tons of rice has almost been implemented and the two sides will start talks in the middle of 2023 to request a new rice export quota.
