In the current context, when international markets do not place orders for long-term textiles and garments, businesses can switch to low-cost goods. In 2022, when they began to diversify, the market and product growth remained stable.
For the last quarter of 2022, the economy grew 2.2 percent from a year earlier, down slightly from 4.2 percent in the third quarter.
On a seasonally adjusted basis, the economy grew 0.2 percent in the fourth quarter, compared with 1.1 percent in the third quarter, according to MTI data.
All sectors except manufacturing increased in the fourth quarter from the same period in 2021.
