Phnom Penh's first toilet waste treatment plant project is 70% complete, today the authorities inspected the progress of construction
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of January 5, 2023, Mr. NUON Pharath, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh Capital City, led a working group to inspect the progress of the construction of the toilet waste treatment plant located in Sangkat Pleung Cheh Roret, Khan Kampoul, Phnom Penh. Phnom Penh.
The first phase of the toilet waste treatment plant project in Phnom Penh has achieved about 70% of the results, which will be completed by the beginning of May.
This project will contribute to improving the well-being of the people in Phnom Penh by providing three main benefits, including:
* First: Environmental benefits through proper wastewater management, which will improve the quality of sewage in the city * Second: social benefits through job creation and recycling of toilet waste Organic fertilizers reduce the use of chemical fertilizers * Third: The economic benefits through the sale of organic fertilizers produced in the agricultural market, or in other words, "waste management."
The construction of the treatment plant is in line with the "Toilet Waste Management Strategy for Phnom Penh 2035", which was started in 2018 through a technical assistance from AIMF.
