This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Dith Tina's participation in the press conference on "Concepts in the field of agriculture in Cambodia" organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia at the Office of the Council of Ministers on the morning of January 5. This year 2023.
"In the overall view, the Ministry will have a new responsibility to set up a more efficient agricultural production system, ensuring that prices do not rise or fall by dividing profits," he said. "It's the same for consumers and producers and distributors."
Mr. Dith Tina said that the Ministry wants the same growth for all actors in the production chain, and that leaving or not giving importance to any one character will lead to the whole production chain stuck and Problems.
In addition, Mr. Dith Tina said that the Ministry's concept is to extract agricultural potential that is in line with the favorable conditions of Cambodia to distribute equitably to the entire production chain from production to you. Consumers or end users.
In this sense, the Ministry of Agriculture has a heavier burden because it has to weigh the common interests rather than the interests of any group in the entire production chain. In the past, we promoted productivity to ensure food security. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Dit Tina.
"Currently, we need to balance and set up an agricultural production system that responds to market demand," he said. For the domestic market, we need to ensure price stability at a reasonable level for all, both producers and consumers. "Therefore, the profits of all the players in the production chain must be at the same reasonable level."
"Apart from the price aspect, we have taken into account the quality and safety of agricultural products for consumers, which is also an additional burden for the ministry," he said. "For the export market, based on this concept, the ministry's strategy is to promote the export of high quality and high-priced products, which we call key products or luxury products."
At the same time, Mr. Dith Tina also said that Cambodia can not and must not compete with neighboring countries based on quantity and low prices due to high costs in both production and transportation. Cambodia has high excellence in quality, so Cambodia should focus on strengthening this excellence for its competition.
Mr. Dith Tina emphasized that in order to achieve this goal, the Ministry of Agriculture is responsible for setting up a highly efficient agricultural production system and responding to the actual needs of the market in both quantity and quality.
