Kratie Coalition Forces Crack Down on Fishing Offenses in Kampi Dolphin Conservation Seizure and Burn Various Illegal Fishing Equipment
(Kratie): A joint force of Kratie province has launched an operation to crack down on illegal fishing in the Kampi Dolphin Conservation Canyon in Sambok commune, Chit Borei district, Kratie province, confiscating and burning various types of illegal fishing gear.
The operation took place on the evening of January 4, 2023, led by Mr. Phuong Tina, Deputy Director of the Mekong Fisheries Administration Inspectorate, led by the River Guard, Dolphin Conservation, Kampi and Chroy Banteay.
According to Mr. Mok Ponlok, Kratie Fisheries District Chief, during the crackdown, the police confiscated evidences of fishery crimes, including: confiscation of fishing gear in the canyon, Chroy Banteay and 6 gems, 180 meters in length and 2 square meters. 7-15 cm, confiscated a 100-meter-long rope, 50 fruit of No. 9, and these artifacts were burned at the riverbank behind the Kampi guard post.
The Director of Fisheries also urges all people, especially fishermen, not to use the wrong fishing gear that the sub-decree on the management and protection of dolphins has banned, including: fishing nets. Fishing tackle, which is a danger to the lives of dolphins from day to day.
He added that although this is the fishing season, the equipment is strictly prohibited by law. If committed, will be punished according to the law on fisheries.
At the same time, he requested the local authorities to help guide the dissemination of the benefits of the Mekong River dolphins, which are Cambodia's precious living treasures, and how to protect the Mekong River dolphins. Mekong dolphins survive for the present and the future.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's recommendation follows reports of an endangered species of dolphin due to fishing nets and some illegal fishing in the Mekong River dolphin area.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed the two provincial governors to set up a permanent core area for conservation by banning fishing, nets and other disturbances to ensure that the dolphin area is 100% safe, including Other core areas depending on tidal conditions.
