3. Vehicles traveling from Kampong Cham to Phnom Penh must divert traffic on Road 270 through Kang Meas district to the intersection of Roka Kong, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province.
4: For vehicles traveling from Kampong Cham City, Chamkar Leu District to Phnom Penh, the traffic direction must be diverted at the intersection of Prey Toteung Market, Chrey Vien Commune, Prey Chhor District to Street 70, through Kang Meas District to the intersection of Kar Kong, Muk Kampoul District, Kandal Province. Commentary: What role did the RCEP play over the past year in promoting regional and global economic recovery in the face of repeated crises?
In this regard, negotiations to reach the implementation of this agreement is not easy, from the first negotiations in May 2013 until the official signing in November 2020, negotiations have been going on for more than 8 years. But despite the difficulties, the reserve member states have made every effort to negotiate a consensus.
The old saying goes, "Get tired first, get tired later." Under the close cooperation and efforts of the parties, an agreement has been reached to establish the largest free trade area in the world today, covering 30% of the world's population and 30% of the world's economy. The world will account for 28% of the world's trade volume, with a steady influx of member states.
In early 2022, the political crisis between Russia and Ukraine escalated to the point of an armed conflict. The wave of conflict has affected global commodity prices, especially oil and gas prices. After that, some countries began to face the pressure of inflation. On the other hand, the spread of Kovid-19 is not over.
The RCEP, born in a context where the world is facing such a recurring crisis, is under greater pressure than ever before. As a result, RCEP member states have exploited regional superiority by promoting a series of trade and investment facilitation coupled with the reduction or abolition of tariffs between each other, increasing the volume of exports and imports. Order.
In addition, the RCEP environment has also been highlighted. The agreement takes into account the different levels of development of member states by setting out preferential or transitional provisions for less developed countries, ie setting out a transitional mechanism for about 20 years to achieve the gradual abolition of tariffs. 90% of imported products.
China has played a prominent role in implementing the RCEP. For example, in 2022, many ASEAN fresh fruits, including Vietnamese durian, Cambodian gourd and Lao passion fruit, were approved for import to China for the first time in accordance with sanitary and phytosanitary inspection standards. China's food safety is also the first time that China has approved the import of many kinds of fresh fruits directly into China.
Over the years, the gradual removal of trade barriers between RCEP member states has brought dividends to the countries concerned, becoming a model of the world's free trade. The coherence and complementarity of the national policies and strategies of the RCEP member states has not only helped to stabilize the regional economy in the midst of the global crisis, but also contributed to the stabilization of the industrial and supply chain. The world, too.
We can be confident that in line with the capacity building of member states, the RCEP will mature, which will be an important driving force for contributing to regional and global economic growth.
