Airfare from Cambodia to China drops to $ 500 as China shows trend of reconnecting flights (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Round-trip airfare between Cambodia and China used to jump to tens of thousands of dollars during The Kovid 19 epidemic has been steadily declining. To date, airfare from Cambodia to China has been just over $ 500, about the same as before the Kovid 19 epidemic.
She pointed out that the price may not continue to fall even if China announces the easing of the Kovid 19 rule from January 8, 2023, because the price is similar to the normal price before the Kovid 19 outbreak.
"Prices may go up a bit if flights are not added because demand may increase," he added.
The National Health Commission of China announced on December 27, 2022 that it will end the requirement for travelers to enter the country from January 8, 2023, which is an important step towards It has reopened its border since closing most of it in early 2020.
Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for Civil Aviation, also told Fresh News that after China announced the opening of the country from January 8, 2022, some Chinese tour companies have shown the trend of connecting flights. However, it is not certain because they have not yet requested a specific landing.
He added that Cambodia welcomes Chinese flights to Cambodia and hopes that the relevant authorities will facilitate various measures to open up to Chinese businessmen and tourists upon arrival in Cambodia.
According to a senior civil aviation official, there are currently 15 flights from Cambodia to China and 15 flights from China to Cambodia per week.
Labor Minister Raises Historical Truths After January 7 Liberation Day
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, spoke about the historical truth and the achievements of nation building that occurred after the day of liberation on January 7, 1979, and disseminated to unions as well as workers in Cambodia.
The commemoration of this historical truth was made on the occasion of Mr. Ith Sam Heng presiding over a meeting with the leaders of the Union of Trade Unions and about 300 members and members to celebrate the 44th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day. 1979-2023) held in front of the headquarters of the General Confederation of Trade Unions of Cambodia (CGCU) in Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh on the morning of January 4, 2023.
On that occasion, Ms. Tep Kim Vannary, President of the General Confederation of Trade Unions of Cambodia, expressed her gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who made all kinds of sacrifices for the cause of the nation and the people and as an outstanding guide of the Cambodian people. Has led the country through difficult stages and achieved great success for the nation and its people.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that the day of liberation and Victory Day on January 7 is the historical truth of Cambodia, which all people consider today as their second birthday, especially the opening day of building the country, building people's lives. Build peace, build infrastructure and achievements for the nation and the people, continuously enhance the national prestige on the international stage, lead Cambodia to enlightenment under the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party.
"January 7 is not only the day of national liberation, but also the important day in saving the lives of the people from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, which ruled the country for three years and eight years," he said. The 20-day month caused more than 3 million people to die unjustly and to destroy infrastructure.
He added that what is a memory and a lesson in history needs to be reminded so that all can work to prevent this genocide from happening again.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng recalled that after the day of liberation on January 7, 1979, until now, the Cambodian people have received justice through the establishment of a hybrid court (Royal Government of Cambodia and the United Nations) that tried the genocidal leaders. And completed its mission in the past. In particular, the court acknowledged that the government of Democratic Kampuchea had set up a genocidal brothel.
The Minister called on the unions in Cambodia, together with the workers, to work together to prevent this atrocity from happening again in Cambodia and to remember what is historical truth as well as the achievements that came after the 7th day of liberation. January, especially to remember the spirit of Victory Day January 7 always in my heart. Achievements after January 7 are worth more than anything.
