Dr. Mao Havanal expects that KOICA will continue to support the National Institute of Civil Aviation for the development of the Cambodian aviation sector
The delegation was welcomed by General Dr. Mao Havnall, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation (SSCA) and Mr. Lim Kao, Director of the National Institute of Civil Aviation and leaders of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation and the National Institute of Civil Aviation.
Mr. Lim Kao stated that the purpose of the visit was to review the achievements in the National Institute of Civil Aviation, such as: construction of school buildings, study materials and office furniture.
The National Civil Aviation Institute (NICA), a former Civil Aviation Training Center (CATC), was built by KOICA under a grant from the Republic of Korea of US $ 10.1 million, which includes the construction of school buildings, study facilities and training facilities. Training of trainers as officials of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation by Korean instructors.
