Mr. Nguon Rattanak made this remark when he and his team inspected a concrete road built by the community in Kamreng village, Srayov commune, Stung Sen city, Kampong Thom province on January 4, 2023.
During the inspection and meeting with the people, the provincial governor also thanked the people who sacrificed their energy to develop the villages and communes to contribute to the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, this is a united force. One to achieve the goals we want.
At the same time, the provincial governor also called on the people to continue to participate in the development of villages, communes and to maintain long-term peace, which the Royal Government is difficult to find.
On that occasion, Mr. Nguon Rattanak and his team donated 60 tons of cement and 100 cubic meters of black stone, and the owner of the plot of land Soksan also donated 20 tons of cement.
He said that this is the first step in supporting the people who have sacrificed both money and energy.
According to Mr. Som Thy, Srayov commune chief, more than 1,700 meters of concrete road, 6 meters wide and 1.5 meters thick, is the budget of the commune fund, while the concrete road of nearly 400 meters is the participation of the people. Dedicated money and energy to build this road.
