The United States and South Korea will take action if North Korea uses nuclear weapons (Video inside) (Washington): Washington and Seoul are planning to coordinate an effective response if North Korea dares to launch an attack. By nuclear weapons. This is a warning from the White House, quoted by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, January 4, 2023.
A spokesman for the White House National Security Council on Tuesday (Washington time) confirmed that South Korean President Yoon Sok-yul and US President Joe Biden have tasked the two countries' working groups with planning. Coordinate an effective response to all scenarios, including a nuclear attack from North Korea.
The White House warning comes amid a flurry of reports in recent days over response to Pyongyang's nuclear threat. Earlier on Monday, Biden denied that the United States was in talks with South Korea over joint nuclear exercises after the South Korean president confirmed the progress of the talks.
A White House National Security Council spokesman reiterated that joint nuclear exercises were not an option because South Korea does not have its own nuclear weapons. Even so, the United States remains fully committed to protecting its allies from attacks.
