Philippines: More than 33,000 people evacuated by floods as they remain in temporary shelters
MANILA (Reuters) - More than 33,000 people were displaced by floods that killed 51 people in the Philippines last week while in temporary shelters, the government said on Tuesday. No. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Tuesday, January 3, 2023.
The Department of Social Welfare and Development said the evacuees came from five areas badly affected by the floods that hit the archipelago on Christmas day.
The National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council said in a new report on Monday that the death toll had risen to 51 and that authorities were still searching for 19 missing people.
The floods have forced the government to evacuate nearly 600,000 people in 10 regions across the Southeast Asian country to safety.
