Mak Ngoy, Director General of the General Department of Higher Education of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, told Fresh News on January 3, 2023 that the inclusion of insurance in the undergraduate program will help students gain a sense of knowledge. On the real skills and skills of the insurance industry that drive their performance better.
He said that currently, the General Department of Higher Education in collaboration with the Cambodian Insurance Regulator has visited universities in Phnom Penh and other provinces to give lectures to students and professors to make them understand the importance of the field. Insurance and the size of job requirements in the sector.
He hopes that when it is widely disseminated, universities and students will understand the importance of this insurance subject, which will lead to the inclusion of insurance subjects in the curriculum, as well as to attract students to start studying the subject. This.
He added, "We have been discussing in higher education institutions and with the Cambodian insurance regulator so far, some higher education institutions have this subject, such as the Royal University of Law and Economics." "And the National High School of Management until he has a bachelor's degree and we want to expand this program."
He said that according to the insurance regulator of Cambodia, there are currently more than 3,500 full-time employees in the insurance sector and more than 10,000 part-time insurance agents, and is expected within 10 years. The number of full-time workers has increased to about 30,000 and the number of part-time workers has increased to 100,000.
