After a total of 145 days off Earth, the Danuri spacecraft is now orbiting the moon at 1.62 kilometers per second. Danuri will officially launch a lunar exploration mission in February, and it will also find a suitable landing location for South Korea's future lunar mission. Commentary: RCEP continues to provide a strong impetus to the regional and global economy.
The RCEP, initiated by ASEAN with 10 member states and China, Japan, South Korea, Australia and New Zealand, is the largest population-free and largest free trade agreement . Since its inception one year, it has entered into force in 13 of the 15 member states in a row.
In terms of the RCEP, China's accession is very important. As the world's largest developing country and the world's second largest economy, China accounts for nearly 60 percent of the RCEP. China has continuously provided new opportunities to the world through its new developments and continues to replenish the vitality of the regional and global economy.
By 2022, China and regional free trade partners "have boosted mutual trade", the flow of goods will be smooth. More than 90 percent of trade in goods will gradually achieve zero tariffs, significantly reducing trade barriers and promoting regional economic integration.
By 2022, the enterprises of the countries in the region "benefit from each other" to share the benefits brought by the favorable policies set out in the agreement. In the case of ASEAN countries, one of the major benefits brought by the RCEP is the reduction of import costs and the increase in export opportunities caused by the reduction of customs duties.
Immediately after the RCEP came into force, the zero-tariff ratio between China and ASEAN exceeded 65 percent, greatly boosting ASEAN's import and export trade. In the first 10 months of 2022, China's exports and imports to ASEAN reached 7.98 billion US dollars, an increase of 13.8% over the same period in 2021. .
Since the implementation of this agreement, one year has yielded remarkable results. At the same time, the Member States continue to write new chapters on mutual benefit and win-win, and continue to provide a strong impetus to the regional and global economy. Mr.
Svay Chrum District Authorities Detain a Suspect in Drug Trafficking Case and Confiscate Some Evidence
(Svay Rieng): Police in Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province, arrested a suspect in a drug trafficking case and confiscated some exhibits.
The arrest took place at 6:10 pm on January 2, 2023, in front of the Krous pagoda gate, at Krous village, Krous commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province.
Mr. Som Sophorn, Police Inspector of Svay Chrum District, said that his forces detained a 54-year-old male suspect with an unspecified occupation, residing in Krous Village, Krous Commune, Svay Chrum District, Svay Rieng Province. The confiscated items include: 13 large packages of white crystalline powder, 1 large package of drugs, 3 mobile phones, 1 motorbike and some drug paraphernalia.
The district inspector said that in front of the police, the suspect confessed that he had bought 14 packages of drugs from Phnom Penh and packed them in a taxi and sent them to him.
Mr. Som Sophorn stated that after receiving information from the people that he was involved in drug trafficking, he led the anti-drug crime force of Svay Chrum district in cooperation with the police force of Krous Administration to search and arrest the suspects at In front of the gate of Wat Krous and will be interrogated.
The district inspector continued that the police checked the water to find drugs as a positive result, so the competent authorities to build a case according to the law.
