(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation on January 3, 2023 organized a consultative workshop on updating the cooperation agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam on standard operating procedures. In identifying and repatriating victims of human trafficking.
The senior official of the Ministry of Social Affairs said that, of course, this document (standard procedure for identifying and repatriating victims of human trafficking) has existed since 2009 until now. It has been more than 13 years since the SOPs were required to be updated by both sides.
He said that human trafficking and human trafficking have occurred and are spreading everywhere, most of them transnational organized crime, and this crime has affected the national, regional and global.
In this context, he strongly hopes that the participation of his technical team (practitioners) will make this workshop meaningful to participate in various input comments for the benefit of victims of human trafficking and abuse. Sexual abuse, especially of women and children, victims of human trafficking and sexual exploitation in Cambodia or in any target country.
In addition, Mr. Nhek Vannara expressed his strong hope that this document will be a means for the implementation of practical work with high efficiency and as a support to the provider of care for victims, especially the initial identification of services and Facilitate the repatriation of victims of the two countries, Cambodia and Vietnam.
