Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara to Preside Over the Groundbreaking Ceremony for a 108-Meter Buddha Statue on Bokor Mountain Tomorrow
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of a 108-meter-high Buddha statue on a hillside. Bokor in Monivong "Bokor" National Park, Kampot province on January 4, 2023 tomorrow.
The Royal Government has in principle authorized Sokha Hotel to build a 108-meter-high Buddha statue on the ridge of Bokor Mountain in the 500 rice fields of Monivong "Bokor" National Park, in accordance with the master plan and style provided by the inter-ministerial working group. Agreed with the support of the Board of Directors of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The construction of this Buddha statue will contribute to the promotion of Buddhism in the Kingdom of Cambodia as well as create another new tourism potential of Monivong "Bokor" National Park.
