(Phnom Penh): On the morning of January 2, 2023, at the Office of the Mine Action Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chief of the Mine Action Authority, handed over demining equipment to the Army Engineering Corps Command and the Bodyguard Command, including: 160 mine clearance machines. 160, 40 body armor and 85 explosive devices, totaling $ 785,125.
Demining equipment is divided into the following:
* Army Engineering Command received 150 mine kits, 150 kits, 40 body armor and 85 explosive devices, totaling $ 745,775, received by Lt. Gen. Ouch Vantha, Deputy Commander of the Army Commander of the Army Engineering Corps, Lieutenant General Dr. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army Command.
