The Chinese government has announced that it will end the requirement for entry into the country from January 8, 2023, which is an important step towards reopening the country. Since closing most of the international gates in early 2020.
This welcoming announcement was made on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, together with Mr. Wang Vinthean, Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia, inaugurated the construction site of a bridge across the Mekong River in Kratie Province on the morning of January 2, 2022. .
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced in advance to welcome Chinese tourists who want to visit Cambodia when the Chinese government allows people to go abroad easily in the near future.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is an attractive, safe, warm and ready tourist destination for Chinese tourists.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, this year, Cambodia received only 2.2 million international tourists, but also expects to receive 2 million Chinese tourists after the government of the People's Republic of China reopened its people abroad.
Samdech Techo said, "This year, Cambodia received 2.2 million tourists, and if Chinese tourists start to open dozens of flights a day, then we will receive 2 million Chinese tourists." "People equal to 19 before Kovid will increase the number of tourists in Cambodia."
Samdech Techo continued that some important sectors are starting to grow again, such as agriculture, industry, services, etc., but in the service sector, there is still tourism services, which increased at a low level because before 19 Kovid, Cambodia received 6.6 million people. Now get only 2.2 million people in 2022.
At the groundbreaking ceremony for the bridge across the Mekong River today, Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao also confirmed that the Chinese government will soon allow its people to travel abroad again. Will be a major tourist destination for them.
According to a study by the Ministry of Tourism, when the Chinese government reopens the outbound population, Cambodia will receive about 2 million tourists from this country with the introduction of attractive strategies and readiness to Welcoming Chinese tourists as well as other tourists.
The Minister of Tourism, Mr. Thong Khon, said that according to the current situation, Cambodia expects to receive as many international tourists by 2026 as before the Kovid-19 crisis.
