Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Groundbreaking Ceremony for the Construction of a Bridge Across the Mekong River in Kratie Province
(Kratie): New Kratie, Peace Land, Roads, Bridges, Highlights. It is a great joy for the people of Kratie province at the beginning of 2023, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, giving a sacred bond, a bridge across the Mekong River to solve the difficulties of daily travel. This is an unprecedented historical achievement for the people of Kratie.
The construction of the bridge across the river and the road connecting the bridge was opened this morning, Monday, January 2, 2023, under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Wang Vintian, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's opportunity to open the construction site of the bridge across the Mekong River in Kratie Province:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the achievements of the Mekong River Bridge in Kratie Province are the result of the efforts of the Cambodian people and the contribution of the Chinese government.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Chinese government has already helped build four bridges across the Mekong River. So far, China has helped build a total of 11 bridges across the river.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the achievements of the bridges and roads that China helped were a demonstration of the Cambodian-Chinese friendship and the achievements of the Belt and Road policy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was seeking credit from China to build infrastructure.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was also seeking credit to build a road west of the Mekong River in Kratie to Kampong Thom.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that throughout his life, one hand strives for peace, protects peace and the other hand strives to develop the country to meet the needs of the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that after the bridge was put into use, the difficulties of the people must be reduced. The cost of childbirth is eliminated and time is saved.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Chinese government and people for helping to build this bridge.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expects that Samdech will pay a visit to China in the near future. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that his visit to China will decide on a number of other infrastructure construction agreements, including the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Kratie is a province to be estimated for the new year in terms of infrastructure.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the people of Kratie for voting for the CPP in June 2022. Samdech Techo strongly hopes that the people of Kratie will continue to vote for the CPP in July 2023.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the election in support of the CPP is in support of the peace process.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the opposition is not a partner of the CPP and has no opportunity to lead the government.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen welcomes all Chinese tourists to Cambodia. Samdech Techo Hun Sen expects that Cambodia will receive 2 million more Chinese tourists after China allows people to go abroad.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expects that the construction of a bridge across the Mekong River will receive attention from construction companies as well as authorities.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that nothing will interfere with the construction process of the bridge across the Mekong River and will be completed as planned.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen commended the Ministry of Public Works and Transport for its efforts in the construction of the Mekong River Bridge in Kratie Province.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requests the people's understanding on the impact of various construction projects.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen congratulates teachers and students who started the new school year today.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded the authorities to pay attention to vaccinating the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the governors of Kratie and Stung Treng provinces to pay attention to the conservation of dolphins without exception. Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends the establishment of a permanent core area for dolphin conservation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that peace has made people enjoy the New Year. Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for joint protection of peace because there are still people trying to destroy.
Opening day of the 2022-2023 school year, Mr. Eang Sophalleth: Students can learn in a clean classroom and a good environment under a peaceful roof
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Oreang Ov District, said that education and the environment must be linked. In addition, students can study in a clean classroom and a good environment under the roof of peace led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth made the remarks while presiding over the opening ceremony of the 2022-2023 school year at Peam Jiang High School in Preah Theat commune, Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province on Tuesday, January 2, 2023.
On that occasion, Mr. Eang Sophalleth stated that the students will be model youth who participate in not creating waste, especially plastic waste (using environmental bags, using water bottles or reusable materials, etc.) to manage waste well. Participate in environmental clean-up at home, school, pagoda and public place and can help spread the word about environmental hygiene that leads to a healthy and clean and green environment.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth said that education is the key to development and one of the four priorities of the Royal Government (people, water, roads, electricity) No country can develop and prosper without capable and knowledgeable human resources. .
In addition, he shared eight basic points that focus on learning to achieve good results and success by encouraging hard work, diligence, respect for the law, morality, virtue, participate in vaccination against Kovid 19 Doses set by the Royal Government Participate in social activities, do good deeds, continue to protect the heritage left by our ancestors and previous generations, and participate in keeping schools clean, villages clean and healthy.
It should be noted that the opening ceremony of the new school year at Peam Jiang High School was held with the organization of an environmental sanitation campaign under the theme "Our motherland, our duty, we are clean and green".
Mr. Eang Sophalleth distributed study materials and budget to the school management, teachers and students who won the annual winners from 1st to 5th in all levels and more than 700 students participated.
Separately, the head of the Oreang Ov district field team encouraged two students of Peam Jiang High School who had just passed the high school diploma (Bak Dop) A level, each with $ 500 and some study materials, and distributed Trash and cleaning materials to schools and local authorities.
