Many global companies are looking at China Plus One, a strategy to diversify investment outside of China to avoid supply chain constraints, as China, the world's second-largest economy, is on the rise. Kovid-19 infection.
Reuters reports, citing India's local broadcaster CNBC-TV18, that the international company intends to seek production in India but wants to continue its existing joint venture in China.
According to the report, Apple, the maker of the iPhone, wants Chinese company BYD to get permission to sign a joint venture with an Indian company to shift production of the iPad to India, and the Indian government may. Consider this change.
The Indian government may allow joint ventures with Chinese companies in areas where India does not have technical expertise, the statement said.
India and China have maintained quiet relations after the worst border clashes between the two neighbors since 1962 in June 2020.
After the clashes, India blocked Chinese companies from participating in Indian government tenders, required Chinese companies investing in India to gain approval, and banned dozens of Chinese programs. According to Reuters.
Indonesia tightens palm oil exports from January 1 to strengthen domestic supply (Video inside) (Jakarta): Indonesia will tighten palm oil export rules from January 1, allowing Less exports to ensure adequate and affordable domestic supply of cooking oil. According to Reuters.
According to new officials and regulations obtained by Reuters, exporters will be allowed to export six times the export volume of the exporter, down from eight times the current level.
Indonesia earlier this year tried to keep cooking oil prices from rising beyond control and introduced export measures on palm oil products to try to increase supply and keep prices down.
The short-term ban on palm oil exports has shaken markets and raised concerns about existing global supply, but the ban has also led to an increase in domestic inventories. According to Reuters.
The Ministry of Finance said in a separate statement that the current import tariffs will continue to apply to seven types of coal until March 31 next year, and tariffs will be applied to the most favorable countries. From April 1.
