New dream achievement! This morning, the construction of the historic bridge across the Mekong River in Kratie province began under the presidency of Samdech Techo and the Chinese Ambassador
The Mekong River, which flows through Kratie province for about 150 km, although it provides many benefits to daily life, such as water for irrigation, farming, fish to support life and livelihood, but this long river has become An obstacle for their daily travel as well, especially people living on the west bank of the river.
The longing and dreaming of seeing a bridge across the river facilitates travel for many months. At this time, the hopes and dreams have come under the shadow of peace and thought of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that the bridge across the Mekong River in Kratie province is 1,761 meters long. The bridge is located on the east bank of Talus village, Bos Leav commune, Chit Borei district, and on the west bank of Thmor Reap village, Prek Prosop commune, Prek Prosop district.
According to the Senior Minister, the bridge will be built with a diameter of more than 13 meters, with two lanes for vehicles, two lanes for bicycles and two lanes for pedestrians. 1 meter long and the railings of the bridge on both sides.
The Senior Minister said that the project to build a bridge across the Mekong River in Kratie province, along with the connecting road, is an important strategic project to connect the relationship and hope between the people living on the east coast and the people living on the west coast, including Connect remote areas in the Northeast to the town as well.
The senior minister said that this project is part of National Road No. 60B connecting Kratie to Kampong Thom, which is connected to the main national roads and provincial roads, such as: West Coast, connected to National Road 6 straight. The Kampong Thmor junction, Kampong Thom province, continues to Siem Reap and connects via National Road 71A along the Mekong River to Stung Treng in the upper reaches and to Kampong Cham in the lower reaches of the Mekong River.
On the east side, it connects to National Road 7 to Stung Treng, Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri provinces and connects to National Road 73 through Chhlong district, Tambor district to Tbong Khmum province and then to National Road 7. Go to Kampong Cham or Prey Veng and continue to Phnom Penh.
At the same time, this bridge and connecting road will facilitate the various trips of the people in daily life activities, the journey of the children, students to school and your trip to the hospital, especially in Emergency or late night without ferry crossing, free of charge and safe.
The people of Kratie province, who have been waiting for this presence for many years, were overjoyed to hear the news of the construction of this bridge.
The presence of the bridge will make it easier for them to travel without wasting time waiting for the ferry and reduce the daily budget while traveling.
The people of Kratie province have expressed their gratitude and gratitude to Samdech Techo forever for providing this precious bond.
