Interior Ministry Spokesman: 43 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on December 31
(Phnom Penh): At least 43 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on December 31, 2022 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on January 1, 2023.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 59 suspects, 14 were arrested in 11 criminal cases and 45 were arrested in 12 drug cases.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on all parties to fight against sexual abuse and trafficking of women and girls, especially men, to stop immoral activities (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia this morning On January 1, 2023, we called on the people to unite in the fight against abuse and sex trafficking for women and girls, especially for men to stop immoral activities.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's appeal was made on the occasion of Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen visiting children victims of sexual abuse and trafficking and officially inaugurating a three-story building. With 40 rooms, which was assisted by both Samdechs at Asexip Cambodia, located in Sangkat Prey Sar, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expects that AFSIP will not receive more girls and girls who are victims of sexual abuse or trafficking, stating that the construction of this new building is not aimed at increasing the number of people, but Only to make the girls who are staying more comfortable.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Today, Lok Chumteav Chou Bun Eng, who is responsible for the fight against human trafficking, is also here. We must start together to fight against abuses, especially "Animals that have grown because of some man created."
Please note that AFSIP Cambodia was established in 1996 by Ms. Mam Somaly. This organization was established to combat human trafficking and sexual exploitation of women and girls.
AFSIP Cambodia has a total of 32 staff members (18 females) and a total of 148 young men and women who are receiving support from AFP Cambodia Cambodia, including health care and scholarships and vocational training. Since 1996, the organization has helped a total of 10,000 girls and girls who have been sexually abused and trafficked.
Key Remarks by Samdech Techo HUN SEN Opportunity to Visit Girls and Girls Victims of Sexual Abuse and Trafficking at AFSIP Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): With the opening of the New Year 2023 this morning, Sunday, January 1, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, visited the affected girls and young women. Victim of sexual abuse and trafficking at AFSIP Cambodia in Sangkat Prey Sar, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
In addition to visiting Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, a three-story building with 40 rooms was officially inaugurated, with the help of both Samdechs in this organization.
The following is the content of the main speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech was happy to meet with the girls and young women who were emotional about the problems they were facing.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit are proud to support for the benefit of the girls and young victims at AFSIP.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on men to stop their immoral activities.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expects that AFSIP will not receive more girls and girls who are victims of sexual abuse or trafficking.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that the construction of the accommodation building at Asexip is not to receive more girls and young victims.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for joint action to combat sexual abuse and trafficking for girls.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked all the philanthropists who provided support to AFSIP. Samdech Techo considered this support to be a place that should be supported.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pride and joy that the girls and girls victims at AFC's stand up to their problems and get a higher education.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends giving priority to scholarships for girls at AFSIP.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces the principle that girls at Afsip must graduate from higher education. Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces to guarantee the education of the victim girl at Afisip.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen is proud of the girl victims in Afesip who passed the police and military exam.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that there is no society that hates girls who are abused, only encouragement and compassion.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to increase the financial support for AFSIP from 10 million Riels to 20 million Riels (for food). This installation starts from January 2023 and will continue to provide 100,000 Riels to the girls at Afisip.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also decided to donate $ 50,000 per year to AFSIP to solve various problems in the organization.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this support will take place in the long run. But this is not to support the abuse of girls.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expects that the decision to support this time will improve the support of the organization and the food at AFSIP.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen receives a request not to bring a girl victim of abuse under the age of 5 to court. This request was made at the request of Ms. Mam Somaly, Director of AFSIP.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodians celebrate the New Year with joy and without fear. Samdech Techo stated that this is a peace achievement that is hard to find.
(Phnom Penh): With the opening of the New Year 2023 this morning, Sunday, January 1, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, visit the affected girls and young women. By Abuse and Sex Trafficking at AFSIP Cambodia in Sangkat Prey Sar, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
In addition to visiting Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, a three-story building with 40 rooms will be officially inaugurated with the assistance of both Samdechs in this organization.
On March 10, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit have already had a face-to-face meeting with young women and girls who are receiving support in the rehabilitation center of AFSIP Cambodia. .
The two Samdechs have provided compassion, warmth and encouragement to the young women and girls victims at AFSIC Cambodia by donating a car with 1,200 kg of rice on a monthly basis. 10 million riels per month and a budget for a young girl / girl 100,000 riels per month.
AFSIP Cambodia combines all forms of human trafficking and preventive measures aimed at reducing the needs of victims of trafficking through the fight against violence against women and girls (gender inequality) as violence against women and girls It is part of a human rights issue.
AFSIP Cambodia works to help young women and girls who are at high risk of being trafficked, sexually abused, raped, enslaved, or exploited in collaboration with their families to provide security and provision Strategies for Sustainable Leaving.
AFSIP Cambodia works closely with government officials, NGOs, local authorities and international partners to provide relevant solutions to relevant issues.
AFSIP Cambodia aims to provide care and guarantee the rights of young women and girls vulnerable and enslaved by slavery through successful rehabilitation, education, training and integration, return to society with financial independence, sustainability and resilience. Fiction. We do this by helping and training them about financial independence through business sustainability. Then encourage them to become part of a network of former victims.
AFSIP Cambodia helps women and girls at high risk of being trafficked, abused, harassed and sexually exploited by providing safe shelter in mental health care centers, physical health, legal aid, lower secondary education And higher education, skills training, economic development with a small business start-up package, or finding a job for them at the end of each major.
After the integration of young people and girls to reunite with their families in the community, AFSIP Cambodia continues to monitor and continue to provide excellent spiritual, counseling and financial assistance to promote their stability and dignity. We encourage victims to become ex-victims and encourage ex-victims to contribute to society by building a network to promote ex-victims.
AFSIP Cambodia has an office and rehabilitation center located in Village 24, Sangkat Prey Sar, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh, and our rehabilitation center of AFSIC Cambodia is named "AFS Tum Di Rehabilitation Center". "Tum Di" is the name of one of the victims of AFSIP Cambodia, but he died of an infectious disease.
AFSIP Cambodia has a total of 32 staff members (18 females) and a total of 148 young men and women who are receiving support from AFP Cambodia Cambodia, including health care and scholarships and vocational training.
Out of 148 people, 119 received a high monthly stipend from Samdech Cho and Samdech Kitti, each of whom received 100,000 Riels for out-of-pocket money when going to school and some savings for the purchase of toiletries as well as support. Support their families as well when they have a need.
Ms. Mam Somaly said that since 1996, the organization has helped a total of 10,000 girls and girls who have been sexually abused and trafficked.
