The following is a message from General Vong Pisen: A fire completely engulfed two houses in Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon
(Phnom Penh): On December 31, 2022, a fire completely burned two houses on Sothearos Street, Village 9, Group 50, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon. This is according to the report of the Fire Police Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
According to the fire brigade, in addition to the two houses, the fire continued to spread to about 20% of the three neighboring houses.
According to the report, 23 fire trucks from the fire brigade used 115 fire trucks, equivalent to 460 cubic meters of water. Until 1:30 pm on the same day, it was completely extinguished.
(Kampot): There are at least 34 entertainment events organized throughout Kampot province, especially in Kampot, Bokor and surrounding areas for national and international tourists on the occasion of the Global New Year 2022 to 2023 . This is according to Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Kampot Province.
He said that in Kampot and surrounding areas, authorities have organized New Year's Eve with two concerts, Khmer boxing, traditional martial arts, traditional boat races (fishing boats). Not only that, there is also a market for tourists and a fireworks display to celebrate the Global New Year.
The provincial governor added that the 34 locations are all organized with different features, such as next to the beach, along the canals, mountainous areas, agro-tourism areas, which are luxurious for national tourists. And internationals wishing to visit Kampot.
Separately, on Bokor Mountain as well as Bokor City, Kampot Provincial Administration and local authorities have also organized a lot of tents for tourists with beautiful scenery, weather and unique natural potential. In addition, the mountain also has hotels to meet the accommodation needs of tourists, as well as many other tourist destinations.
Soy Sinol, director of the Department of Tourism, said that so far, hotels, guesthouses, boutiques and accommodation services in the province are booked almost 100 percent out of a total of more than 4,700 rooms, however. There is no shortage of accommodation, which is still enough to meet the needs of tourists.
As noted by the Director of the Department of Tourism, tourists flocked to Koh Smao beach (from the provincial town to the tourist port), a newly prepared beach, where there is a traditional fishing boat race. Traditional Khmer martial arts, while some people are sitting for leisure, some are also traveling there because there are entertainment events both day and night.
