(UN) - The United Nations General Assembly has voted to adopt a resolution calling on the International Court of Justice (ICJ) to comment on the legal implications of Israel's illegal occupation of the Palestinian territories. This was released by the AFP news agency on Saturday, December 31, 2022.
In an election on Friday (New York time), the UN General Assembly passed the resolution by a vote of 87 to 26, while 53 other countries voted against. The election also highlighted differences among Western nations and a majority of support among Muslim nations, including Arab states that have signed peace agreements with Israel.
The Palestinians on Saturday hailed the adoption of the resolution as a reflection of a victory in Palestinian diplomacy.
Donors Donate Nearly $ 3 Million for "Son Under the Full Moon"
(Phnom Penh): The benefactors of the Duke, Duke, as well as senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia have donated a total of nearly 3 million dollars for the licking of the film "Son under the full moon".
