Putin expects Xi to pay state visit to Russia during spring 2023
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russian President Vladimir Putin on Friday said he expects Chinese President Xi Jinping to pay a state visit to Russia next spring between March and June. One that would be a show of solidarity from Beijing to Moscow in the face of Russia's war in Ukraine. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, December 30, 2022.
"We expect our friends to pay a state visit to Moscow during the spring of 2023," Russian President Vladimir Putin said during an online video conference on Friday. "This visit will show the world how close Russia-China relations are."
In the brief discussion, which lasted more than 10 minutes, Putin added that Russia-China relations were growing in importance as a stabilizing factor, and he aimed to further deepen military cooperation between the two countries. Both. In response, the Chinese president said Beijing was ready to step up strategic cooperation with Russia against the difficult situation in the world.
JAKARTA: Indonesian President Joko Widodo said on Friday that Indonesia had decided to repeal all remaining measures to control the spread of Kovid 19 because of the systematic majority of the population. Immunity against the disease already. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Friday, December 30, 2022.
Nearly 75 percent of Indonesians over the age of six, or 174.7 million, have received two doses, and about 68.5 million have received at least one booster dose. Prior to the announcement, restrictions on most social activities had already been lifted for those who had received at least one dose of Kovid 19 vaccine, but authorities still required the wearing of masks in public places and use. Kovid 19 Tracker when accessing public places.
"There will be no more restrictions on mobilization and social activities, and this decision is based on the latest cross-border figures," Widodo told a news conference.
The world's fourth most populous country recorded a total of more than 6.7 million cases of 19 Kovid cases, with 160,583 deaths.
