Russian tourists flock to Thailand as tourism recovers
BANGKOK: Thailand is experiencing a surge in Russian tourist arrivals, with data showing a doubling of monthly arrivals in November and a nearly seven-fold increase in September, far surpassing other countries in the country. This peak travel season. According to Reuters.
Reuters reports that Thailand is seeing a boom in tourism, with 1.75 million visitors in November, four times the number received for the whole of 2021 when flights and arrivals arrive. Arrivals of foreign tourists are hampered by epidemics.
Russia was Thailand's seventh-largest tourism market in 2019, ahead of the outbreak with 1.48 million visitors, but ranked eighth in monthly terms in November. It lags behind Malaysia and India with 108,985 visitors, up from 44,314 in October and 15,900 in September.
Russian arrivals in November accounted for about 60% of the total number of visits to the country in the same month in 2019.
