China urges US to suspend arms sales to Taiwan
BEIJING (Reuters) - China on Friday urged the United States to suspend arms sales to Taiwan and military ties with the country, as well as stop creating new factors that could lead to tensions across the Taiwan Strait. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Friday, December 30, 2022.
He stressed that China has always strongly opposed US arms sales to China's Taiwan.
Wang said China urges the United States to adhere to the one-China and three-China-US principles, which are joint statements and sincere action on commitments made by US leaders who do not support "Taiwan independence." "
A total of 11,448 traffic accidents occurred in Vietnam in 2022, killing 6,364 people and seriously injuring more, according to the Vietnam Traffic Police Department. 4,215 people and 3,613 people were slightly injured. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Friday, December 30, 2022.
The number of traffic accidents and minor injuries decreased by 0.3 percent and 12.1 percent, respectively, while the number of fatalities and serious injuries increased by 9.9 percent and 7.8 percent from the same period last year. .
On average, in 2022, Vietnam was hit by traffic accidents 31 times a day, killing 17 people and injuring 22 others.
In 2021, a total of 11,454 traffic accidents occurred in the Southeast Asian country, killing more than 5,700 people and injuring nearly 8,000, according to the country's statistics bureau. People.
