Ministry of Tourism recommends all capital-provincial departments to increase the promotion of women in tourism by 2023
(Phnom Penh): Pursuant to the policy of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Tourism has instructed the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism to strengthen the management mechanism for women in the tourism sector and to promote the rights, roles and values of women for the upcoming action plan for 2023. .
This instruction was made at the meeting to review the work of women and gender in the tourism sector in 2022 and the direction of implementation in 2023 on December 30, 2022 at the Ministry of Tourism under the chairmanship of Ms. Hun Dany, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism Minister Thong Khon.
The meeting was held to review the progress of women and gender work in tourism at both the national and sub-national levels, discuss challenges and set out the implementation direction for 2023 to strengthen the management mechanism for women in tourism and promote Promoting the participation of women in rights, roles and values, as well as empowering women in the tourism industry.
During the meeting, the Secretary of State stated that in accordance with the policies and political programs of the Royal Government, especially the recommendations of the Prime Minister, which requested all relevant ministries and institutions to pay attention to women working in the economy. Informal and entertainment services.
She said that the Ministry of Tourism, as a staff to the Royal Government, always pays attention to the group of women who work in restaurants, restaurants, karaoke, bars, discos, beer gardens, massages and spas, and Minister Thong Khon always gave guidance and assign duties. To Secretary of State Hun Dany, lead a working group to visit and find out about the needs and challenges of women in the private sector in the tourism sector.
As a direction for further implementation in 2023, Secretary of State Hun Dany provided the following five key recommendations:
1. Continue to strengthen the mechanism for managing women in the tourism sector and participate in building a workforce that serves the informal economy in accordance with the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
2. Continue to organize training courses and orientation workshops to strengthen and build the capacity of women in tourism.
4. Continue to strengthen and expand the network of women in the tourism sector, especially to build more private women's groups in all tourism services to facilitate management, share their experiences and solve their challenges.
5. Continue to visit and talk to women in the business community as much as possible. Experts advise students who are stuck or failing should take a clear basic skill along with 4 other skills to become a qualified employee or entrepreneur.
(Phnom Penh): Economic and financial experts have given some advice to students who have just passed or failed in 2022 should have a clear skill along with 4 other skills to develop into a quality employee or entrepreneur at the moment. Ahead.
Mr. Nget Chou said that students who have just passed the exam or failed should have a clear basic skills that are skills for life to easily get a job or run a business for a living. However, they also need to have four accompanying skills, which are important for them to help them work effectively and have a better life as well as financial freedom.
He explained the four accompanying skills:
1. Entrepreneurship skills are skills that are creative and create business ideas to solve problems in society. First, young people can use basic skills to work, earn a living and family, and use entrepreneurial skills to help the company they work for grow. Then you can start your own business if you have a clear desire and ability.
2. The skills of managing personal finances and investing are from now on. Knowing how to work or run a business to earn a living for the family alone is not enough, it is required to know how to manage money and hard-earned assets. Effectiveness. In particular, know how to use the money earned to create extra money through investment to ease the burden to support family life and educate children well.
3 - Communication and teamwork skills: No matter what the job, as an entrepreneur or an investor, everyone should have good communication skills and the ability to work in a team effectively. . Otherwise, there is no chance of success in the job.
4. Foreign language skills: This skill is used for study, research and job communication, etc.
At the same time, he also mentioned the skills that the Cambodian market is in need of that young people should consider to acquire skills to meet the needs of the labor market in Cambodia, while currently facing a shortage of manpower in these areas.
Students who have gone bankrupt should study for an associate's degree in engineering or other technical skills such as electrical construction, electronics repair or agriculture, and advance to a bachelor's degree.
