The G7 foreign minister on Thursday called on the Taliban to "immediately change" the ban on women working in Afghanistan's humanitarian sector. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Thursday, December 29, 2022.
The ministers said they were "deeply concerned" that the Taliban's careless and dangerous regulations that bar women women of national and international non-governmental organizations (NGOs) from working could put the Afghan people at risk. Millions depend on humanitarian aid for survival.
"We call on the Taliban to immediately change this decision," they said in a statement issued by the British Foreign Office.
The ban is the latest attack on women's rights in Afghanistan since the Taliban seized power last year.
Less than a week ago, these extremist groups claiming to be Muslims also barred women from attending university, sparking outrage and protests in some Afghan cities. .
The statement came after six aid agencies suspended operations in Afghanistan in response to the ban.
