(Kampot): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, emphasized that the factors of complete peace and strong political stability and high economic growth provide great opportunities for environmental protection, biodiversity conservation and sustainable development. Unprecedented for Cambodia.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra's remarks were made on the occasion of presiding over the meeting to review the work results of 2022 and the work direction for 2023 of the Department of Environment of Kampot Province, with the participation of Mr. Nei Kong, Deputy Governor of Kampot And a total of 300 relevant officials on the morning of December 29, 2022.
Taking this opportunity, the senior official of the Ministry of Environment said that December 29 is the 24th anniversary of the end of the civil war in Cambodia through the implementation of the win-win policy submitted by Samdech Techo Hun Sen ended the civil war and brought complete peace to the nation and the people of Cambodia.
"Peace, political stability and development in all areas are indispensable preconditions for the protection of natural resources and the conservation of biodiversity in Cambodia, and provide opportunities and resources for the Kampot Provincial Department of Environment to work for the cause of the environment and natural resources." This is an additional statement of Mr. Net Pheaktra.
The Secretary of State added that after Cambodia recovered from the ashes of the sea, blood, tears and bones of the Cambodian Civil War, under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen re-established protected areas in 1993 with Lay the signature of King Norodom Sihanouk and the establishment of an institution in charge of the environment, which is a reflection of the long-term strategic thinking in building a new progressive society.
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra continued that due to the complete peace factor has improved the management and conservation of natural resources, and now Cambodia has changed a turning point from a logging country to earn economic income. A country that is fully capable of maintaining forests to generate income for society through the sale of carbon credits and eco-tourism creates jobs and income for its people.
