Mr. Chay Borin brought a message from Samdech Techo, President of the Party, Samdech Chakrei, Honorary President of the Party, Samdech Vice President of the Party, party leaders at all levels, along with Dr. Hun Manet to General Phan Nguon and his family.
General Phan Nguon was very excited and thankful and expressed his deep gratitude to the party leaders at all levels, especially Dr. Hun Manet, who appointed Mr. Chay Borin as his representative. The General and his family arrive at the house, making the General and his family feel warm and an honor for the family.
The General also expressed his clear support for the candidacy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister forever and the support of Dr. Hun Manet as the successor full of knowledge, ability, morality, virtue and merit as the successor to lead the country. The future.
General Phan Nguon also described his work history that after the liberation in 1979, he joined the Ministry of Defense in the Air Force and was promoted to Deputy Director of the Air Force Department, Deputy Commissioner of Aviation Defense, Undersecretary of State, Secretary of State of the Ministry. National Defense and advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen (currently an advisor to the Ministry of National Defense).
The General also said that the younger generation used their lives as capital for the cause of the people and the nation for peace and to develop the country to develop day by day to make the country rich. Reputation is equal to other countries in the world, so the younger generation, in addition to continuing to maintain the achievements of the previous generation of leaders, must adhere to two important points:
1: Must strive to continue to study, pay attention to research in order to acquire skills and knowledge clearly, which is to build a strong foundation to achieve success in fulfilling the functions, roles and tasks. The future.
2: Strengthen the will of patriotism and national unity of the younger generation.
The General also wished the Cambodian People's Party a landslide victory in the upcoming 7th National Assembly Election 2023 to continue to lead the country in maintaining peace and development for decades to come. .
On this significant occasion, members of the delegation handed over souvenirs and funds donated by Dr. Hun Manet to General Phan Nguon and wished him good health, strength and longevity.
DC-Cam: The Khmer Rouge Regime Commits Serious Human Rights Violations in the Twentieth Century
(Phnom Penh): The Khmer Rouge regime committed serious human rights abuses in the 20th century, killing more than two million Cambodians. This is the saddest tragedy in human history.
Cambodia has suffered directly from this regime, but Cambodia has sought to restore its country from scratch to this day. Cambodia will continue to improve day by day for the next generation and be a part of a brighter world.
DC-Cam is proud to document this difficult history for the cause of justice, remembrance and reconciliation for its nation and the world. DC-Cam Holds Exhibition on Genocide and Resurrection of Cambodians
(Phnom Penh): To Celebrate the 24th Anniversary of the Victory Politics Day, Celebrate the 24th Anniversary of the End of the Cambodian Civil War and the Successful Implementation of the Victory Politics (December 29, 1998 - December 29, 2022) and the 5th Anniversary of Victory Monument The Documentation Center of Cambodia allows for a three-day exhibition on the genocide and resurrection of the Cambodian people from December 29 to 31, 2022 at Victory Monument.
An exhibition on the genocide and resurrection of the Cambodian people contributed to a win-win policy to end Cambodia's civil war. Content is a common theme of the Khmer Rouge History Exhibition to show the origins of the Khmer Rouge rise to power, the fall of the Khmer Rouge, the struggle in the civil war after the fall of the Khmer Rouge regime in 1979 until a win-win policy. Victory and revival of Cambodia.
In the whole exhibition, there are 3 main parts:
* First: The Khmer Rouge organization, which features images from 1975 to 1979 of top Khmer Rouge cadres, photographed at airport locations and departments in Phnom Penh during the Khmer Rouge regime, depicting the presence of The Khmer Rouge was there as regime leaders evacuated people from Phnom Penh for fear of bombings. These are lies.
* Second: Genocide crimes that show the work of people in cooperatives, dam construction, digging canals and other irrigation systems, all of which are forced labor and evidence of what happened. The same section also shows the location of crimes such as the exhumation of victims of the Khmer Rouge massacre in villages in Cambodia in the mid-1980s.
Overall, this section is about the revival after the fall of the Pol Pot regime and the gradual rebuilding of society until Cambodia has progressed under the umbrella of peace as it is today.
The exhibition also features photos of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on his journey across the X-16 into Vietnam for help. In this photo, the Documentation Center of Cambodia shows a slogan that reads, "Between the sky and the earth is the victorious monument of humanity, born from the path to the overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot."
Ministry of Economy and Administration of Kampong Cham Province Organizes Training Course on Capacity Building and Procedures for Obtaining ACSEP Credit in Agriculture
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Mey Van, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, this morning, December 29, 2022, presided over a seminar on capacity building and training on access processes and procedures. ACSEP Project Loan Component 1.
The ceremony was held at Phnom Pros Hotel, Kampong Cham, with the participation of representatives of Kampong Thom Provincial Administration, Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration and Kampong Cham Provincial Administration, as well as 10 district governors, community representatives, development partners and other stakeholders.
On that occasion, the Governor of Kampong Cham Province said that currently short-term crops are actively involved in promoting the family economy can be produced two to three times a year, such as all kinds of vegetables, beans, potatoes and tobacco. Cultivated on 67,920 hectares and produced 679,801 tons in 2022. Long-term crops such as bananas, cashews, mangoes, coconuts, etc. were planted on 39,183 hectares and produced 211,165 tons in 2022.
Mr. Un Chanda stated that Kampong Cham is one of the six target provinces of the project to compete on the value chain and improve agricultural safety, a project of the Royal Government that will contribute to strengthening the value chain of agricultural products. Some of the competitions are cassava, mango, cashew nuts, vegetables and local chicken.
Therefore, in today's workshop, representatives of communities and agricultural production and processing enterprises in the three target groups will receive specific information about the ACSEP 1st component loan scheme for agricultural enterprises and communities and better understand the procedures. Can get loans to manufacturing enterprises and their communities. Pursat Provincial Administration to Celebrate the 44th Anniversary of January 7 Victory Day and Global New Year
