So far, Cambodia has imported about 30,000 tons of salt from India to meet domestic demand.
Speaking to Fresh News on December 28, 2022, Mr. Bun Barang, a salt producer, confirmed that "according to the plan, the import of salt will be about 60,000 tons to meet market demand, but so far Cambodia has imported about salt. "Only 30,000 tonnes of the 30,000 tonnes have also been suspended because we are selling and waiting for the Kampot salt harvest."
He added that Kampot salt will be harvested during February 2023 in case the weather is favorable, but the harvest is not very productive because so far the salt has not been harvested yet. Also depends entirely on the weather, if the weather is not favorable, the amount received accordingly.
He added that the salt supply is about 7-10,000 tons per year. Last year, salt production reached 100,000 tons, but in the last 2-3 years, salt production did not seem to be very productive due to the rainy weather, so the production was only Only 3-50,000 tons, therefore, can not supply enough and require the import of salt from abroad.
Please be informed that due to the weather problem, the salt production in 2022 will be less compared to 2021 with the production of only 30,000 tons, so the Royal Government of Cambodia decided to import salt to meet domestic demand of about 6 Ten thousand tons.
Kampot and Kep provinces are the main sources of salt in Cambodia, with salt production from the end of December to May, while the area for salt production in Kampot province is 3,726 hectares. In 2019, Cambodia faced a shortage of salt and imported about 30,000 tons of salt from China.
