Nearly 5,000 people gathered to celebrate the 24th anniversary of the end of the war under Samdech Techo's win-win policy
General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, confirmed that 4,688 people attended the celebration of this historic day. In total, 272 national and international guests, 7 monks, armed forces, including 19 scouts, equal to 2,315 people, youth plans from the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, 894 Red Cross scouts, 1 population plan, 200 people.
General Ith Sarath said that this anniversary celebration is very important to be held every year so that the people can understand the win-win politics, support all the activities of the win-win politics, be grateful and grateful to the heroes, especially the founders and operators. Win-win politics that sacrificed its life for the cause of the motherland until the end of the war.
Along with the celebration, there will be the inauguration of some newly built achievements at the Win-Win Monument. Achievements inaugurated include the achievements of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, National Security, including the Royal Gendarmerie and the National Police, the CMAC Park and the Victory Monument Park.
In this event, there will also be an exhibition on the implementation of the win-win policy of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in 19 booths. Among them, there are 12 booths under the Ministry of National Defense and 7 booths of the Commander-in-Chief, and fireworks were fired at night.
It should be noted that Cambodia experienced a tragic fire crisis for about three decades after the illegal coup d'état of March 18, 1970. The flames of war that erupted on March 18, 1970, engulfed the Cambodian ship, destroying it almost to ashes.
The flames of war, which erupted in a single day but burned for up to three decades. The flames of war were completely extinguished on December 29, 1998, the day the Khmer Rouge leaders came to join the Royal Government.
The flames of war were extinguished under a win-win policy founded by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. With the end of this war, it was time for Cambodia to find peace, to find national unity and territory again after the fall of the Angkorian Empire, which lasted for at least 500 years.
Win-win politics is a strategy and principles that will bring about the guarantee of social security, national unity, national unity, peace, the guarantee of territorial integrity, sovereignty and sustainable economic, political and social development.
Ending the war by win-win politics is the philosophy of peace and strong political commitment of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia. The end of the war is not a miracle or a coincidence, the process of ending the war requires highly talented and scientific leadership together, as events vary greatly.
Win-win politics in Cambodia has a broad meaning, that is, it covers all areas of society as a whole. Thus, win-win politics is the strategy and principles that bring about the guarantee of social security, national unity, national unity, peace, the guarantee of territorial integrity, sovereignty and sustainable socio-economic and political development.
In 2018, the Royal Government of Cambodia began to celebrate the end of this war to commemorate the heroism of the founders and operators of win-win politics, as well as to make the Cambodian people aware of the value of win-win politics as a cause. Bring peace, end the flames of war and bring development for the society as it is today.
To celebrate the win-win political day in January 2022, the Royal Government of Cambodia has issued a circular to designate the win-win political day on December 29 in the annual calendar without a break.
In that circular, the Royal Government instructed all ministries, institutions, capitals, provinces and private public institutions to prepare banners and slogans to celebrate the win-win political day with the message, "Thank you, peace!" Thank you, win-win politics! "Thank you to the founders, guides and political operators, win-win that brings peace and complete national unity!" Summary of important news events for December 28, 2022
