(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works, stated that the introduction of a new type of civil servant ID card to be used as an identity card and an ATM card (ATM) to pay salaries from the bank, as well as for other functions. The other is to reform public administration in line with the program for implementing digital government policies.
Mr. Prum Sokha said this evening, December 28, 2022, presiding over the official launch of the new type of civil servant ID card held at Cambodianna Hotel and with the participation of bank representatives. Including many other relevant professional officers.
Mr. Prum Sokha added, "The announcement of the launch of Smart Card confirms that we have achieved a breakthrough as a result of the efforts in the program to implement the digital government policy of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia. "Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the head in the use of modern technology in the era of the era of technology 4.0."
Minister Prum Sokha also stated that the announcement of the introduction of this new type of civil servant ID card is also a step in the reform of public administration in order to develop and build human resources, also build institutional development and publication. The card is also keeping pace with technological developments.
Mr. Prum Sokha added that the process of using the new type of civil servant ID card is to change the dream into reality by changing from a civil servant card to a civil servant card and can be used to open Salary through partner banks, as well as access to a number of other means.
He also claimed that the ministry will also start developing other issues, including the ministry's plans to support the welfare of civil servants, including a number of other issues.
According to the report, the introduction of this new type of civil servant ID card in response to the process of the fourth industrial revolution coincided with the spread of Kovid 19, the Cambodian Digital Economic and Social Policy Framework 2021-2035 has been prepared. Established in 2021 as a common framework and a roadmap aimed at promoting the process of digital transformation on all actors in the Cambodian economy and society as a whole.
This policy framework has three pillars: (1) building a digital government, (2) building a digital citizen, and (3) building a digital business. In accordance with the above policy framework, the Royal Government has set out the Digital Government of Cambodia Policy 2022-2035, focusing on the vision "Building a Digital Government to Improve the Quality of Life and Confidence of the People through Better Public Services". .
The printing and issuance of new types of civil servants' ID cards clearly reflects the new efforts and responses of the Ministry of Public Works to contribute to the building of digital government through modernization and innovation in public administration. Ministry of Land Management starts experimenting with construction materials
