(Banteay Meanchey): A huge fire has been burning at Grand Diamond Casino Kandal, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Sithi Loh said that the fire started at 11:30 pm on December 28 and had not been extinguished until dawn on December 29.
About 300 joint police forces and 11 fire trucks were operating at the scene, the commissioner said. However, due to the high and narrow location, the size of the fire spread throughout the location, making the firefighting operation difficult and not yet extinguished.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, vice chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, told Fresh News this morning that several casino staff had been evacuated from the building. He has now sent helicopters and commandos to the scene to evacuate personnel from the roof.
The senior minister emphasized that so far there was no information related to the deaths or injuries in the incident.
Meanwhile, the intervention force of the 711 Disaster Search and Rescue Operations, 70th Brigade, by helicopter to the scene in Poipet to rescue.
