Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor Inspects Car Tire, Solar Panel and Furniture Factory
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, on December 28, 2022, inspected the construction site of the car tire factory, the production process of the furniture factory and the solar panel factory in the special economic zone of Preah Sihanouk City. Sihanouk is located in Bit Trang Commune, Prey Nob District, Preah Sihanouk Province.
During the inspection, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun visited the project to establish a car tire factory which is under construction on 28 hectares, the first step is to build on 10 hectares, build 60 percent and install the engine 5 percent, equipped with 5 rows of engines. Three rows are automatic machines that do not require people and the other two rows use labor.
At present, the factory needs 1,500 workers, the first phase can produce 15,000 small car tires per day in one wheel can take 38 seconds, while the big car can produce 2,500 tires per day can take 60 seconds per tire . The raw material can use 300 tons of rubber, raw materials imported from Thailand and Malaysia.
The company currently has factories in China and Thailand that produce and export tires to the United States. After that, the provincial governor inspected the solar panel factory and continued to inspect the furniture factory.
On that occasion, the Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province also thanked the Director General of the Special Economic Zone and the factory owner for facilitating the technical working group of the provincial administration to inspect the tire factory, solar power plant and furniture factory in Economic zone.
The provincial governor also urged young Cambodians to study hard to work in Sihanoukville, which has a factory that employs technical workers using robots to make tires. This factory can not only have ordinary workers, so we are ready to fill Development needs and can also signal farmers who produce to supply the factory.
He said that, for example, rubber growers in Cambodia, when there is a tire factory, need up to 300 tons of rubber per day to supply the factory, so do not want to import raw materials from abroad because Cambodia As an agricultural country, we have the potential and some lands need to be changed from farming to rubber cultivation.
