Ministry of Tourism mainstreams domestic tourism promotion policy for new year
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism expects an increase in tourists in 2023, but in order to attract these growths, the Ministry has also organized a training course on policy measures to promote the internal tourism movement in 2021-2023 at the end of 2022 again to prepare Characteristics and best practices in promoting tourist excursions.
The training course lasts for 2 days from December 27-28, 2022 at the Ministry of Tourism, while the parties who received this training include officials from the relevant departments of the Ministry of Tourism, officials from the 25 Departments of Tourism. Provinces and the private sector in the tourism sector to participate in the implementation of policy measures to promote the internal tourism movement in 2021-2023, a total of about 70 people.
Mr. Kim Sereyroth, Director of the Department of Management of Accommodation and Food Services of the Ministry of Tourism, said that the Ministry of Tourism, together with the Royal Government and the private sector to restore and promote tourism in Cambodia during and after the Kovid-19 crisis, has prepared and requested approval by The Royal Government on October 23, 2021 on policy measures to promote the internal tourism movement in 2021-2023.
He said that the policy measures to promote the internal tourism movement focus on five policies, equivalent to 35 measures, including: First, to enhance the confidence and trust of domestic tourists, and second, to promote the process. Business - Tour operators in the new normal trajectory, 3-Facilitate domestic tourists, 4-Develop tourism products to serve the internal tourism movement, and 5-Promote and mainstream public awareness.
Mr. Kim Sereyroth continued that the purpose and goal of the policy measures to promote the internal tourism movement is to encourage more domestic tourism movement, especially in 2023, because the implementation in 2021 and 2022. Satisfactory results with a recovery of more than 13 million domestic tourists in 2022.
By 2023, Cambodia is projected to receive 3-4 million international tourists and 12 million domestic tourists. According to the current situation, Cambodia expects to receive international tourists at the same level as before the Kovid-19 crisis in 2019 at the latest by 2026. China: A new aspect of the rural consumer market presented through the package
BEIJING, Dec. 1 (Xinhua) - As of Dec. 1, the latest data from the China Post Administration's fast-track big data platform shows that China has achieved more than 100 billion packages of rural shipments in 2022, which was achieved 7 days earlier compared to last year.
At the same time, along with the acceleration of the construction of rural express delivery system in recent years, the coverage rate of express delivery into the village has been steadily increasing. Now every day, more than 100 million packages go in and out of the countryside, reflecting the potential of the rural consumer market.
Constantly replenished and intensified express delivery network makes package traffic more convenient, more and more agricultural products are sold directly to the whole country through the express delivery network, many of which are brought Going abroad. Small packages have helped increase farmers' incomes and paved the way for rural industrial development.
Khmer Civilization Expert: "Peace" is the Kingdom of God
(Phnom Penh): Khmer civilization expert Mr. Rath Sandab said that December 29, 2022 is the 24th anniversary of the "peace" of Cambodia, which ended the war in 1998 and made the motherland and Our whole Cambodian nation has this wonderful peace and happy life.
"Peace" is really in the hearts and minds of all of us Cambodians who are hungry to live in harmony.
Because in the past, our motherland has been in the flames of war and national division for about 500 years and almost lost its name from the world map, especially the war that erupted from the coup d'etat that overthrew His Majesty the King from 1970-1979. Caused devastation and catastrophic loss of more than 2 million lives during the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Therefore, in order to preserve this precious heritage of "peace", we need to work together to maintain "peace" and eliminate war. Because there is no peace without caution. Therefore, we must make the strongest and strongest contribution to the defense of this "peace" because it is a problem and a blessing for all of us.
Mr. Rath Sandab continued that in this context, we, the Cambodian people, are the pillars and solid foundations for sustaining "peace" to avoid war. Therefore, we must have a high responsibility to protect the building of our beloved homeland, because this poor land and nation has gone through the sufferings of innumerable chronic wars.
In this spirit, the sacred duty of all of us is to oppose the deceptive policies of corrupt politicians, who often incite and push society to the brink of war. In this case, if we drown without considering all the rhetoric or irresponsible politics, it can bring great danger to the whole society in the blink of an eye.
Therefore, we, the Cambodian people, must be wise, strive to learn and understand the sad historical lessons from the past to the present, in order to achieve "peace", national unity and complete harmony as today, especially to understand the actions and political ideas of the kingdom. "War" against the kingdom of God "Peace". Commentary: China's epidemic prevention work adheres to pragmatic, scientific goals
