(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ing Phirun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Permanent Vice-Chairman of the Tobacco Products Control Committee, said that smoking or cigarette smoke has caused many diseases and seriously affect the health, please call people should stop The smoking.
This statement was made by the doctor at the 27th meeting of the Tobacco Products Control Committee held at Sokha Hotel on December 27, 2022.
According to Dr. Ing Phirun, scientific studies have found that smoking causes a wide range of diseases, including cancer, cardiovascular disease, heart disease, lung disease and diabetes.
"People need to be aware of the dangers of secondhand smoke, not just those who smoke, but also those who inhale or inhale secondhand smoke," said Dr. Ing Phirun. "If a family has a husband who smokes, his wife and children help educate him to stop smoking so that those around him do not endanger him, especially pregnant women and children under the age of two."
Currently, tobacco use throughout the country is declining and some of our people have also changed their behavior, especially in public places such as restaurants, hotels, etc., is declining, according to the doctor.
The doctor said that the decrease in tobacco use is due to the fact that our people are more aware of the community when our professional officers go to health education and legal action. He added that for legal action, the ministry has filed lawsuits against four cigarette manufacturers and the court has already issued verdicts and fines.
