Kampong Speu Provincial Governor: Many investment projects have moved to Kampong Speu (Video inside) (Kampong Speu): Peace factors and the clear development policy of the Royal Government have made Kampong Speu a potential investment destination. Help the lives of the people of Kampong Speu to change a new face, especially to escape from the past as a poor and ignorant.
If one remembers the past, Kampong Speu province, although not far from Phnom Penh, but this province is considered to be a province that seems to be far and far away. There is even an impression on some people when they mock and joke with someone who does not understand the way of civilization or city dwellers, etc., they are drawn to that person from Kampong Speu province.
In an interview with Fresh News, Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu, highlighted that the situation in Kampong Speu as well as the people of Kampong Speu today is not the same as in the past. The province of Kampong today has changed its face, has improved a lot, and the lives of the people have improved, unlike the words of the past.
The provincial governor underlined, "Under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Kampong Speu province, which was a war zone from the time of the war to the present, has become a large industrial area, which is obvious to this day." In Kampong Speu province, there are factories that have opened and are in contact to open many places.
Mr. Vy Samnang added, “Currently, many factories and projects are ready to open. "There is no need to worry about the lack of factories for workers to work, only the fear of lack of labor to return to work."
According to the current provincial governor, Kampong Speu has a total of 381 factories. Through these factories employed nearly 160,000 people, most of whom were citizens of Kampong Speu province. Through the presence of factories, these enterprises have become workplaces and sources of income for people and help their lives better.
"In the past, people in Kampong Speu did not have the opportunity to work in our province. We had to pack rice, pack rice and pack pots to go to work in other provinces. "Currently, our factories here provide jobs for people to work close to home, have an income and have a better life." This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Vy Samnang.
With the increase in investment to establish more factories in the province, the governor also called on the people in the province to continue to work hard to give confidence to investors not to cause any phenomena that lead to investor resentment. Loss of investment confidence in the province.
Another important factor that the provincial governor called on the people of Kampong Speu to keep together is the peace factor. The provincial governor said that the hard-won peace achieved by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party is very important and necessary. Without peace and stability, no investor will come to invest in business.
