(Phnom Penh): December 29, 2022, marks the 24th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian war and the restoration of peace and territorial integrity after at least 500 years of division in Cambodia's history.
The win-win policy set by Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a great legacy for the nation and the people of Cambodia. Through this win-win politics, it brings a new light of life and society full of development, prosperity and happiness.
* Session 1: Cambodia in the process of ending the armed conflict through peaceful means and to achieve national unity
On January 14, 1985, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was unanimously elected by the National Assembly as the Prime Minister at the age of 37, while Cambodia was in the midst of a full-blown civil war. When Samdech Techo Hun Sen took office as Prime Minister, he immediately laid down many more policies to bring peace to the country and its people, including:
First, build the military forces of the People's Republic of Cambodia to grow and grow in both quantity and quality.
Second, make the tripartite coalition government gradually separate because the three forces have different substances and are easily separated.
Third, to attract the royalist forces led by Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk to return to live with the society, as well as the forces of Samdech Son Sann.
Fourth, the Khmer Rouge forces were isolated from the forces of the tripartite coalition government, isolated from the international arena, especially from the countries that used to help them. This is an important starting point for the emergence of a political strategy that Samdech Techo Hun Sen put forward to dissolve the Khmer Rouge from Cambodian politics. The strategy that Samdech laid out during the 1980s was called the "Defensive Strategy".
1. The Cambodian conflict needs to be resolved through a political solution.
Second, the Cambodian issue needs to be resolved by the Cambodian people themselves through negotiations between all parties in the conflict to end the bloody war and to rebuild a peaceful, independent, democratic, territorial, neutral and non-partisan country. Coalition.
Third, when an agreement is reached between all Cambodian parties, an international conference will be held to ensure that this agreement guarantees Cambodia's independence, peace and stability in Southeast Asia.
Phase 1: On February 21, 1990, signed between Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Techo Hun Sen in Bangkok, Thailand.
This proposal was approved by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Samdech Techo Hun Sen once said that Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk had repeatedly said to Samdech: "Whether or not there is a political solution, he must return with His Excellency Hun Sen because he can not be with the Khmer people. "Red did not continue."
- His Excellency Hun Sen agreed to hand over to Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk as the Chairman of the Supreme National Council without the need for the Vice-Chairman of the Supreme National Council and to keep the number of members in the Supreme National Council to 12.
To fully fulfill his role as President of the Supreme National Council, Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk has decided to resign as President of the Cambodian Resistance Movement and President of the Cambodian National Government, and he remains neutral as Mediate without being in any party or in any political party from now on.
In this case, Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk decided that his successor in the Cambodian resistance movement and in the Cambodian national government depended on the resistance movement and the Cambodian national government.
