The meeting was held at the Peace Palace in Phnom Penh in order to strengthen and expand the cooperation between Cambodia and Algeria.
Dr. Osman Hassan expressed his happiness and gratitude to the Ambassador of Algeria to Cambodia for his recent efforts to facilitate the Cambodian delegation to pay an official visit to Algeria. Many positive fruits should be proud.
On that occasion, Dr. Osman Hassan briefed the Ambassador on peace, political stability, economy, development, progress, harmony, ethnicity and religion in Cambodia under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
He added that for the Muslim community in Cambodia, the government has provided opportunities and opportunities on an equal footing with the general population. The Cambodian Muslim community has the opportunity to serve in the Senate, the National Assembly and in the government, from the national, sub-national to the grassroots level.
In 2015, the Royal Government provided the Cambodian Islamic community with 1,678 state and contract teachers, and more recently, the Cambodian government has appointed Muslims as Deputy Governors. 12 12 and 50 Deputy Governors of 50 districts.
At the same time, Dr. requested the Government of Algeria to provide scholarships to Cambodian students in order to provide opportunities for the younger generation to have a wider opportunity to strengthen their capacity and have a high potential to participate in the development of the country in the future.
The Ambassador continued that he would like to support all requests from the Cambodian side regarding the development of the Cambodian Islamic community. He commended the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia for his efforts to harmonize the nation and lead the country to peace, non-violence and non-discrimination, which is a good example for the whole world.
Please be informed that the bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and Algeria dates back to 1962. During 1973, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk also paid a royal visit to Algeria.
