Tycoon Tuy Ky was elected as the new President of the Provincial Chamber of Commerce by the old and new members of Pursat Provincial Chamber of Commerce for the first time.
(Pursat): Mr. Kim Meas Sok Seiha, Under Secretary of State, on behalf of Mr. Mao Thora, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, Mr. Nguon Por Seng, Deputy Governor of Pursat Provincial Board of Governors, on December 27, 2022, presided over the election ceremony. Pursat Chamber of Commerce for the first third mandate.
The ceremony was held at Pursat Provincial Kindergarten in Peal Nhek 1 Village, Sangkat Phteah Prey, Pursat City, Pursat Province, organized by the Ministry of Commerce, Provincial Administration and Pursat Provincial Chamber of Commerce with the participation of Ms. Seng Somon, Director of Communications Provincial and Municipal Chambers of Commerce represented HE Oknha Nguon Meng Tech, Director General of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and leaders of some provincial departments and units.
After the two-station ballot counting process, there were 159 voters, equivalent to 71.62% of the 222 registered voters, 12 candidates, of which 8 were elected. As a result of this election, 15 members, both old and new, elected Mr. Oknha Tuy Ky as President of Pursat Provincial Chamber of Commerce for the first third term.
After Tycoon Tuy Ky, the new president of the Pursat Chamber of Commerce, vowed to work hard to attract investors for development in Pursat, Deputy Governor Nguon Po Seng and Kim Meas Sok Seiha The Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce congratulated the new members of the Provincial Chamber of Commerce and elected its good leader for the first time for the first time.
The two leaders said that the election of members of the Pursat Provincial Chamber of Commerce in accordance with the instructions of the Ministry of Commerce, because the President of the Provincial Chamber of Commerce is an important engine in helping to develop the business sector. To be more prosperous, especially to help boost the economy in the province by attracting investors to invest or do business directly to create jobs and increase income for the people in the province.
The two leaders also confirmed that for the first election of Pursat Provincial Chamber of Commerce for the third mandate, it went smoothly. Voters complied with the conditions and principles set by the Ministry.
Ministry of Land Management issued a press release on the direction set by Samdech Techo Hun Sen for the Ministry to implement in 2023
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction has issued a proclamation on the results of the meeting to review the work results in 2022 and set the implementation direction for 2023.
The meeting to review the work results in 2022 and work direction in 2023 of the Ministry of Land Management, a total of 2,000 participants, held under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo's introduction was made on the occasion of closing the meeting to review the work of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction on the afternoon of December 27, 2022.
Samdech said, "We must continue to implement the policy of providing social land concessions to people who lack real land, and we must set targets for providing land so that they can have real land to build their livelihoods." On the other hand, we will continue to build houses for our armed forces stationed along the border, and we will continue to build houses for veterans so that they can have a home The best place to protect the border is "There are people living there."
Samdech Prime Minister instructed the Ministry of Land Management and relevant authorities to promote conservation in the Angkor resort area in line with the development in the Run Ta Ek development area and related areas for people who volunteer to leave the Angkor resort area to settle. New in that area, consistently implementing the social and infrastructure support policies set by the Royal Government.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed the Ministry of Land Management and relevant authorities to continue to solve problems for the people living as villagers around the Tonle Sap Lake by updating the map in each province, adjusting the boundaries of Area 3, the boundary of Area 2 and cut Clear the land where people have lived for a long time in Zone 3 and Zone 2 by the end of May 2023.
Samdech Techo emphasized, "The provinces that I have visited all the provinces , each province must make a plan where the people, including the people in the three areas to find a way. Cut the skewer so he has to make it smooth. "I set a limit, do not procrastinate, because this year I issued an order on this issue in May, now I set a deadline of May 2023 to be completed in all provinces and across the country in the Tonle Sap."
Samdech Techo stated that solving the problem for the people living as villagers around the Tonle Sap Lake is in the interest of the people who can solve both directions, with one side maintaining the Tonle Sap Lake and the other side being the people who Live long and get the right to occupy their land.
