Lok Chumteav Mao Chamnan Donates Nearly $ 30,000 to AFSIP Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Lok Chumteav Mao Chamnan and her family visited the girls and young women of AFSIP Cambodia and donated some funds and study materials.
Lok Chumteav Mao Chamnan, wife of Duke Kith Meng, brought her sons, daughters, employees of the Royal Group and other philanthropists to meet and learn about the challenges that girls and young women face and the support that AFSIC Cambodia provides They.
Ms. Mam Somaly, Founder and Managing Director of AFSIP Cambodia, shared the organization's history and efforts to help children get a better education.
During the visit, Lok Chumteav Mao Chamnan expressed her deep gratitude for the efforts that AFSIP Cambodia has contributed to the community.
She said, "I would like to thank AFSC Cambodia and all its staff for their efforts to help children in need. These activities are very meaningful to our community and set a good example for others to do good deeds. Children are an important pillar for the development of our nation. "They need our care and a good education."
Lok Chumteav Mao Chamnan encouraged the girls and young people in Asexip Cambodia to study hard to get a good job in the future and be able to support their families as well as contribute to the development of Cambodia.
Mrs. Mao Chamnan and her family donated US $ 10,000, US $ 12,000 in scholarships and study materials to AFSIP Cambodia to celebrate the New Year with girls and young people and to encourage They.
At the end of the visit, Lok Chumteav Mao Chamnan prepared lunch from KFC for girls and young women.
Ms. Mao Chamnan, Chief Operating Officer of Wing Bank and Royal Group, is also a strong advocate for gender diversity in the workplace and has done a lot to build a corporate culture of equality and mutual respect. .
242 candidates continue to compete in the 10th Kramakar Student Recruitment Competition, 120 finalists were eliminated
(Phnom Penh): The Royal School of Administration of the Ministry of Public Works on the afternoon of December 27, 2022 started the second written test in the 10th Kramakar Student Recruitment Competition with 242 candidates to participate. Only 120 finalists were eliminated.
As of December 27, this is the second writing test, a lecture and a short quiz, combined with a foreign language (English or French) lasting 1 hour and 30 minutes. The examination center is in the Royal School of Administration.
This morning, Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of the Council of the Royal School of Administration, with the participation of Mr. Youk Bunna, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Public Works, Director of the Royal School of Administration and Chairman of the examination center, together with relevant leaders. Participate in the selection of quizzes on this second writing test for the 10th Kramakar Student Selection Competition.
In the afternoon of the same day, at the beginning of the competition, 242 candidates out of 242 candidates will be shortlisted for 120 years for one year training in 2023 at Royal School of Administration. Before the start of the competition, Permanent Secretary of State Youk Bunna, a representative of Minister Prum Sokha, cut the test subjects for the candidates.
On that occasion, Mr. Youk Bunna stated that in this exam, the Ministry of Public Works, especially the Royal School of Administration, paid the most careful and accurate attention by organizing a meeting on the decision on the appointment of district chairpersons and sub-committee chairs. For this exam.
At the same time, during the examination process, there were also observers from the Anti-Corruption Unit and representatives of relevant ministries and institutions and from universities and institutes. The preparation of the discipline is to be prepared immediately, without any prior preparation.
He advised all candidates to disclose all the knowledge they have and to check all the questions clearly before starting to answer each question. In particular, for candidates who fail the exam, do not despair, make an effort to learn more about the lack of their knowledge to be ready to participate in the exam next year at the Royal School of Administration and other ministries, institutions and units.
The director of the Royal School of Administration also confirmed that the current exam is conducted in accordance with the basic principles of the Royal School of Administration to be transparent, fair and quality, so candidates with real knowledge and ability are successful.
