573 overweight trucks found in Preah Vihear province, the director of the Department of Public Works ordered all trucks to be weighed
(Preah Vihear): 573 vehicles were found to be overweight by the O Po-Preah Vihear station overweight vehicle inspection team.
Mr. Samleang Try, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province, ordered the officers to have all the trucks enter the scales. If it is found that there is a vehicle that does not enter the station without weighing, the officer stationed at the station will be responsible or ask to be removed from office.
If there is evidence as he stated above, he will ask to remove the official who committed the crime immediately without disturbing the leadership of the Ministry.
At the same time, Mr. Samleang Try also instructed all station officials to pay attention to fulfill their duties with a high sense of responsibility, that is, not to be involved in any illegal acts, and to have Beware of falling into any corrupt tactics to ruin our reputation as officials who have served for many years.
Please be informed that for one month from November 16th to December 15th, 2022, the inspection team of overweight vehicles of O'Po-Preah Vihear station of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport Inspected a total of 3,706 vehicles, of which 573 were found to be overweight.
Oknha Huot Ieng Tong, President and CEO of Hattha Bank, told Fresh News on December 27, 2022 that after the banks raised interest rates, the number of depositors increased significantly. In 2022, most of the increase will be in dollars, while the riel will increase slightly.
He said that for Hattha Bank in 2022, deposits will increase by about 25%, the bank offers a similar interest rate between the dollar and the riel, from 8% to 8.5%, depending on the amount and Period of deposit.
In the past, some banks and microfinance institutions have announced higher interest rates on their deposits, including more than 8 percent for riel deposits and more than 7 percent for dollars. The increase was due to the US Federal Reserve raising interest rates to reduce inflation.
Kaing Tong Ngy, spokesman for the Cambodian Microfinance Association, said that by the third quarter of 2022, deposits at the five deposit-taking microfinance institutions had reached 4,686 million US dollars, an increase of 20 US dollars. .1% compared to last year, with customers depositing a total of 2.66 million accounts.
