According to the report of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, in 2022, the Ministry has issued 315,441 land titles to the people and distributed 264,805 cards to the people. Myanmar court to announce final verdict in Aung San Suu Kyi case this week
Myanmar court, now under military rule, is set to announce its final verdict in the case against former military coup leader Aung San Suu Kyi on Tuesday. This Friday. This was released by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, December 27, 2022.
Suu Kyi, now 77, was arrested after a military coup on February 1, 2021, which ended Myanmar's Provisional Democracy era and pushed the Asean country into a state of disarray. Unrest.
A Myanmar court will rule on the last five corruption cases against Suu Kyi, each of which carries a maximum sentence of 15 years in prison. She is currently being held in a prison compound in the capital, Nay Pyi Taw, while previously under house arrest at a location that has not been made public.
In the last 12 months, the Nobel Peace Prize laureate has been sentenced to a total of at least 26 years in prison for a variety of offenses, including violating the anti-Kovid 19 restrictions. Illegal possession of radio communication equipment to the point of inciting violence, violating national secrecy and trying to influence the Myanmar Electoral Commission.
Ministry will train hospitality for 255 tour operators and 50 trainers in Banteay Meanchey
(Banteay Meanchey): From the beginning of 2023 to the middle of 2024, the Ministry of Tourism, in collaboration with Swisscontact, will provide capacity building training for tourism professionals to 255 tourism workers and 50 trainers in Banteay Meanchey Province.
This training project was disseminated at the Hoka Hospitality Training Workshop to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Tourism, tourism business owners, tourism service staff, staff working in tourism and many tourism stakeholders on the 26th. December 2022.
It should be informed that the HoKa Project Management Committee of the Ministry of Tourism has launched Hoka Hospitality Training Projects in 5 provinces around Tonle Sap Lake, including Battambang, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey and Pursat Provinces. 2023 to mid-2024. The training focuses on food and beverage service, hospitality and front office, housekeeping, chef, coffee making and more.
Mr. Chuob Ratana, Director of the Department of Tourism Development Planning, Ministry of Tourism, told Fresh News that for Banteay Meanchey, the Hoka Project Management Committee plans to provide training to 255 tourism staff and 50 tourism trainers. He said that this number is able to meet a reasonable level for job needs in the tourism service business in Banteay Meanchey.
The director of the department said that the organization of this workshop is to disseminate to the Department of Tourism and tourism business establishments in the province to be ready to recruit staff to work in tourism and to prepare them for the upcoming training courses. The Hoka Hospitality Training for Banteay Meanchey will be held from the beginning of 2023 to the middle of 2024.
Mr. Pak Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, also said that the current seminar on hospitality training is very important to support tourism in Banteay Meanchey, because in the past two years, professional staff Those who used to work in the tourism sector have turned to working in various fields that are not their specialties and have severely affected the human resources in the tourism sector in Banteay Meanchey province.
The Secretary of State continued that through this outreach workshop also reflected the full readiness of all stakeholders to receive tourists who will visit Banteay Meanchey, especially in 2023.
Mr. Chhoeun Sereyvuth, Director of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Tourism, stated that the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration is currently encouraging investors to invest in tourism in the province, especially the development of new tourism products to attract tourists. And stay at new resorts in the province.
The Director of the Department of Tourism continued that along with the gradual recovery of the tourism sector for Banteay Meanchey province, it is necessary to train the skills of staff working in the tourism sector, which is a strategy to improve the quality of services and services. Satisfied with tourists, especially to increase productivity, strengthen competitive excellence, promote innovation and high creativity for each employee.
Commentary: Why did China decide to abolish strict Kovid-19 disease prevention and control measures?
Since the outbreak of Kovid-19, China has taken strict measures to prevent and control the spread of foreign diseases and cases of infection imported from abroad. These measures have protected the safety, life and health of the people. Chinese and foreigners who have been living in China for the past three years.
However, from 2022 onwards, countries around the world have lifted a series of strict measures for the prevention and control of Kovid-19, based on the actual situation of their respective countries. However, it is observed that China still has stricter control measures than other countries.
In addition, in the past, vaccination rates have not been able to create a "immune barrier" in society, which is justified by the abolition of strict preventive and control measures. On the other hand, the experience of the first case of the rapid spread of Kovid-19 in Wuhan is a practical lesson that should not be neglected in the prevention and control of infectious diseases.
Second, we look at the evolution of the Kovid-19 virus. Since Kovid-19 spread globally, the virus has undergone a series of mutations, bringing with it difficulties and complications in prevention and treatment. Medications and vaccines may lose some of their effectiveness when exposed to a new mutation virus. Therefore, measures to prevent and control infectious diseases must look at the actual development of infectious diseases.
First of all, through the most thorough scientific study, it is found that the new type of Kovid-19 mutation that is spreading in China is no longer a serious danger to the life of the people, that is, more than 90% of cases are infected. If there are no symptoms or mild symptoms that do not need treatment or just take medicine for 5-6 days will be cured.
The second is the right time. Currently, the vaccination rate across China is more than 3.4 billion doses, which has become a shield to protect people's health. On the other hand, the ability to respond to Kovid-19 is also very mature, and the treatment is also effective and efficient, so it is the right time for "relaxation".
The facts show that the subject of China's measures to prevent and control infectious diseases, which "puts the life of the people at the core, puts the health of the people first", protects the lives and health of the Chinese people and foreigners who Stayed in China for 3 years.
For the past three years, the world has been united in the fight against Kovid-19, a global pandemic that has borne fruit. We can be confident that under the joint efforts of the countries of the world, in the end, China's initiative to jointly establish a common human health community will be achieved.
Senior Health Officer: Drug use severely affects health, safety, society, economy, family and society
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hok Kim Cheng, Director General of Health Technology of the Ministry of Health, said that according to the United Nations report on drugs and crime (UNODC) shows that in the last 10 years, the trend of use Drugs do not decrease. The consequences of drug use have had a profound impact on health, safety, the economy, the family and society.
His remarks were made at a consultation meeting on the draft Strategic Plan on Drug Abuse 2023-2033, which took place at the Phnom Penh Era Hotel on December 26, 2022.
Dr. Hok Kim Cheng said that the drug problem is a public health problem, drug addiction is a chronic mental illness. Drug addicts are victims, we do not want them to lose their ability to work, have mental health problems and chronic, so our strategy involves fighting, preventing, educating and treating drug addicts in the community as well.
Therefore, this is the second consultation meeting after the first online consultation. He strongly believes that this meeting will receive more important input for the development of the draft plan. The drug abuse strategy is more comprehensive, clear, effective and effective to implement the Cambodian health development agenda in the coming years.
Dr. Hok Kim Cheng emphasized that in order to be successful in this work, it is not only in one institution, but in the overall response. The Ministry of Health has also cooperated with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. In public and private schools, with the participation of teachers and parents of students to give him a clear understanding of this drug addiction to educate his children and students.
According to Dr. Chhit Sophal, Director of the Department of Mental Health and Substance Abuse of the Ministry of Health, health services for drug addicts are available in all 25 provincial hospitals and referral hospitals. 72 districts and also in more than 300 health centers, but now more than 100 places.
"Before the 19 19 outbreak of Kovid, drug addicts came in for treatment and increased every year, but during the Kovid 19 epidemic there was a decrease," he said. However, he continues to educate more about drug treatment and get closer to the community, hoping that more people will come to receive services. Regulation of Public Administration Maintaining Awareness of Public Administration in Cambodia to Students of the University of Economics and Finance
