Chinese Ambassador: Nearly 3,000 Tons of Cambodian Longan Exports to China
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Wang Vintian's participation in the handing over of 1 million animal vaccines donated by the Chinese Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs to the Cambodian Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries this morning. December 27, 2022.
On October 27, Cambodia and China celebrated the inauguration of Cambodian fresh lentil exports to China, opening the door for Cambodia's agricultural exports to China.
According to Wang Vintian, fresh Cambodian longan has appeared in the homes of many Chinese people. He expects that Cambodian corn will also be imported into the Chinese market soon.
He added that at the beginning of the new year, cooperation between the two sides will be very busy in January. Both sides will export pepper to China, and in March a second group of experts from the Chinese-funded Cambodian Agricultural Development Plan will arrive in Cambodia to begin work. In addition, the export of high quality agricultural products of Cambodia, such as: coconut shell products will be carried out in a row.
It should be noted that there are 74 longan plantations officially approved for export to the Chinese market, of which 40 are in Pailin, 28 are in Battambang and 6 are in Banteay Meanchey.
There are 8 packaging factories located in Kandal, 3 in Battambang, 2 in Pailin and 2 in Sihanoukville. The total area under Cambodia is 13,608 hectares in four provinces.
Fresh lentils are the third Cambodian agricultural product to be officially exported to the Chinese market in 2022, after mangoes and bananas. More than 300,000 plots of land titles issued to people in 2022
