The Cambodian National Council for Children holds a workshop to improve the implementation of the circular on the implementation of the recommendations of the UN Committee on the Rights of the Child.
(Phnom Penh): The National Council of Cambodia for Children (NCCC) has organized a workshop to improve the implementation of the Circular on the Implementation of the Recommendations of the United Nations Committee on the Rights of the Child on 27 December 2022 at the Cambodiana Hotel in Phnom Penh. Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and relevant officials, as well as other ministries, institutions and partners.
On that occasion, Mr. Kim Sovandy, Secretary General of the National Council of Cambodia for Children, stated that the purpose of this workshop was to disseminate and promote the implementation of Circular No. 6. Issued on September 20, 2022 on the implementation of the recommendations of the United Nations Committee on the Rights of the Child and the distribution of the circular on the implementation of the recommendations to relevant institutions and children's networks.
He said that the workshop was also to review the action plan being implemented by the relevant ministries and institutions in response to the recommendations to document the inter-sectoral plan on the implementation of children's rights of the United Nations Committee on the Rights of the Child.
The Secretary General of the National Council for Cambodia for Children said that this work is very important that the Ministry has the right time to consider as an activity to include in its action plan next year to respond to the above recommendations.
Mr. Kim Sovandy added that Cambodia had received a number of recommendations, the latest observations of the Committee on the Rights of the Child. The General Secretariat of the Cambodian National Council for Children, in collaboration with development partners UNICEF Plan Cambodia and ChalFan Cambodia, has been working to promote the effective implementation of the recommendations.
Work activities to promote the effective implementation of recommendations include:
1: Organized a national workshop to disseminate recommendations to ministries, institutions, children's networks, National Council of Cambodia for Children, Advisory Committee on Women and Children's Affairs at the Capital and Provincial Levels in June and disseminated through social media (Bayon TV).
2: Organized a roundtable discussion on the implementation of the recommendations of the last observation of the UN Committee on the Rights of the Child in July, a technical meeting with relevant ministries and institutions to discuss and comment on the distribution of recommendations. According to the relevant ministries and institutions in September.
3: Extraordinary meeting of the National Council of Cambodia for Children in early December to seek approval on the distribution of recommendations to ministries and institutions and prepare to publish a book. The final activity is to organize a workshop to improve the implementation of the recommendations of the UN Committee on the Rights of the Child and to prepare a response plan on this occasion.
The overall content of the latest observations of the UN Committee on the Rights of the Child is 59 points and is divided into four main sections, including: 1. Introduction 2. Monitoring measures and progress made by States Parties. Key areas of concern and recommendations 4. Implementation and preparation of reports.
