An Indian three-wheeled motorbike slipped and fell into a river, killing a girl in Kandal province's Saang district.
(Kandal): A girl died after her father's three Indian motorbikes slipped into the river while crossing the river to go home on the evening of December 26, 2022 at the crossing point of Koh Kor-Svay Proteal in Russey Chroy village, commune Svay Proteal, Saang District, Kandal Province.
Mon Dara, a 28-year-old uncle of the victim, said that before the incident, he drove an Indian tricycle to take his wife and two-and-a-half-year-old children and a six-year-old girl out of his mother's house in Prek Dong village. Kampong Svay, Kien Svay district, in order to bring you back home in Phnom Penh.
Crossing Svay Bal to the west bank, while disembarking, the boat left more than 10 meters from the shore because the driver did not take the wheelchair, causing his three-wheeled motorbike to slip into the river and fall into the river. And his wife, children and nephew on the three wheels went into the river together.
Suddenly, the wife grabbed her daughter and shouted for him to help her, but she could not help but jump off the tricycle and sink into the river, although she could not find it. And his wife and children, if there were no teenagers diving nearby to get out of the boat to help, would have drowned, and it was not until more than 40 minutes later that people found him, but he was dead. .
Morn Kanha, a 30-year-old mother of the victim, lamented that her daughter had been abandoned by her father in the womb and that her brother had come to visit her in the morning. Phone relatives say her daughter fell from the boat and died.
Ta Kong Song, 85, the owner of the boat, said that he would pay for the funeral of the girl and that after the funeral, he would be held accountable. The tricycle rider obeys the instructions when boarding the boat to let the passengers get off the tricycle and apply the handbrake and set the brakes properly so that there is no accident.
After the incident, the boat driver, who was about 15-16 years old, escaped and the residents and passengers who crossed the boat also criticized that the boat owner should not use underage children to drive the boat. Also, because the life of the passenger depends on the copier.
