This afternoon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen closed the meeting to review the work of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction.
(Phnom Penh): On Tuesday afternoon, December 27, 2022, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will preside over the closing ceremony of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction.
The ceremony will be held at the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction. In addition to closing the meeting to review the work of the Ministry, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will also cut the ribbon to inaugurate the Ministry of National Construction Laboratory building, which is worth about 3 million dollars, recently completed. Also.
The Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction was established by Royal Decree on May 6, 1999. This Ministry has the authority to lead and manage the field of land management, urban planning and construction in Cambodia.
On the morning of December 27, 2022, the Ministry held a meeting to review the work results of 2022 and raise the work direction for 2023. The ceremony was presided over by Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction. The ceremony was also attended by leaders and government officials of many ministries.
There are 510 Borey housing and housing complex projects. From 2019 to November 2022, there are 89,531 apartment buildings and 434 residential buildings.
In its report, the Ministry also expressed its assessment that the achievements of the Ministry were due to the rescue of the country from the abyss of Kovid 19 death with the support and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has always been Set out a vision, political program and strategy that is accurate and timely to respond to the sacred requests of the people and the national interest.
These achievements also reflect the talent, will and energy of the leadership and the efforts and strong internal solidarity of civil servants at all levels of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, as well as support and Good cooperation of ministries, relevant institutions, sub-national administration and the participation of people from all walks of life.
The report of the Ministry also mentioned that the above achievements will contribute to the establishment of a reference for the implementation of the framework and programs to restore and promote Cambodia's economic growth in the new normal path for 2021-2023 of the Royal Government. Especially for strengthening the potential of Cambodia's economic growth in the process of socio-economic recovery.
Duke Kith Meng's Wife Visits and Brings Donations to AFSIP Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 27, 2022, Lok Chumteav Mao Chamnan, Chief Executive Officer of Royal Group, the wife of Duke Kith Meng, paid a visit and brought some gifts to support AFSIP Cambodia.
Meeting and supporting organizations that are helping children and young women is an activity of sharing love to contribute to a good society.
On that occasion, she donated 110 sets of study materials, provided scholarships to 3 students studying at the college in the amount of 12,000 USD and also donated 10,000 USD to the organization. In addition to socializing, she also prepares KFC food, drinks and lunch there with the children and distributes some souvenirs.
Please be informed that AFSIP Cambodia is located in Village 24, Sangkat Prey Sar, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh. The organization is a place to help, provide psychological treatment and provide professional skills to girls and young women affected by various crises, including sexual abuse. Agriculture Minister receives 1 million animal vaccines from China to contribute to animal disease control in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on December 27, 2022, received 1 million animal vaccines donated by the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs of the People's Republic of China. China to the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Cambodia.
The handover ceremony of 1 million animal vaccines was attended by Mr. Wang Wentian, Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia, as well as other ministry leaders and subordinates. This ceremony was held at the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries this morning, December 27, 2022.
Taking this opportunity, on behalf of the officials of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Dit Tina expressed his great excitement and thanked the People's Republic of China for donating a vaccine to prevent animal diseases. 1 million levels to contribute to the management of infectious diseases in Cambodia.
Mr. Dith Tina said that the livestock sector plays an important role in increasing income, improving livelihoods and boosting the national economy. Raising animals mainly depends on breeding factors, health management and market promotion.
He added that in the past, the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, as well as the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries have made efforts to promote this sector to grow significantly, but we still face some difficulties:
1. Infectious diseases are one of the main obstacles affecting animal husbandry, meat supply and animal products in the market as well as the economy in Cambodia. Outbreaks and outbreaks of these diseases have devastated livestock and the economy.
According to Dith Tina, Cambodia has experienced outbreaks and outbreaks of foot-and-mouth disease in the past, such as foot-and-mouth disease, cattle disease, swine fever, bird flu, African swine fever and, most recently, tuberculosis. Cattle skin rash, which causes severe damage to livestock farmers, especially farmers in rural areas.
2. Laboratories and limited human resources have had a significant impact on the development of the livestock sector. In the past, the People's Republic of China has supported the animal husbandry sector, including the promotion of animal husbandry through various projects and cooperation, including biogas plants, vaccines, animal diseases and training programs.
