(Kandal): Khsach Kandal district authorities in Kandal province released a kingfish weighing 46 kg and 157 cm long into the Mekong River at Svay Ath Leu village, Prek Tamak commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province.
At the same time, Sangkat Khsach Kandal Fisheries Administration, in cooperation with the team of the Freshwater Fisheries Research Institute, visited and put on the badges of the fishery experts caught by the fishermen to know the evolution of the kingfisher and the kingfisher. The fishermen were released into the Mekong River.
It should be noted that the fishermen used a fishing gear to catch a royal fish weighing 46 kg and 157 cm long in Svay Ath Leu village, Prek Tamak commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province.
This kingfisher can live up to 60 years and is the fastest growing species, can weigh more than 10 kg per year. Crayfish are the main food, while aquatic insects are a secondary food. According to reports, in the last 20 years, a kingfish weighing nearly 300 kilograms and 2.74 meters long has been found. The kingfisher was equipped with a tracking device and was no longer allowed back into the river.
