Not only that, the Khmer Rouge regime still has the recognition and support of legitimacy from some Western countries, and especially among some ASEAN countries, by ignoring or ignoring the atrocities that the leaders The Khmer have treated the Cambodian people. The Khmer Rouge killed more than two million innocent Cambodians and almost completely destroyed Cambodia's infrastructure.
This great loss is a serious obligation that the people of Cambodia and the Government of the People's Republic of Kampuchea (later renamed the State of Cambodia), which was denied and has no seats in the United Nations, must restore and reunite the divided nation. Repeat. Therefore, bringing the Khmer Rouge leaders and the Khmer Rouge forces, which still have the support of some countries and still have weapons in hand, is a difficult and complicated task.
However, the Royal Government's unification negotiations and strategy to end the Khmer Rouge regime did not realize its importance in the region and the world. Therefore, I think that the inclusion of a win-win policy in the Ministry of Education's curriculum is an important benefit that makes children understand the value of peace and national reconciliation and encourages the Cambodian people to unite for a brighter future. .
This win-win policy should also be included in the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission's curriculum on human rights, community and the world, as win-win politics is Cambodia's strategy to raise awareness and contribute to the lessons of history on genocide. Race, peace and conflict resolution in the region and the world.
Victory Monument was built and inaugurated on December 29, 2018 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. December 29, 2022 marks the fifth anniversary of the Victory Monument and the 24th anniversary of the surrender of all Khmer Rouge leaders and forces to the Royal Government of Cambodia. Victory Monument represents peace and national unity that the Cambodian people must study and understand.
The director of the hospital said that his hospital treats common eye diseases such as red eyes, goats, as well as children's eye diseases, cataracts, glaucoma. In particular, the hospital has specialized doctors who can provide examination and treatment for cataracts as well.
The director of the hospital confirmed the quality of equipment and facilities in the hospital, so "our technical equipment is all modern technology equipment imported from Japan. "Because we can check and measure the patient's data in a short time can help ease the burden and reduce the patient's waiting time a lot."
In addition to modern equipment and facilities, the hospital also has a team of ophthalmologists with specific skills, both Japanese and Cambodian.
The eye is an important organ for people's daily lives that requires careful care and regular check-ups to avoid problems, especially for children.
The doctor shared the experience that children in Japan are highly concerned about eye health. Children in Japan have their eyes checked at school every four months, and medical records are kept to check for any changes in the future.
A Japanese doctor said that a proper eye examination is essential before undergoing any eye surgery. Based on the results of the examination, the specialist will make it easier to diagnose and develop a proper treatment plan.
Early and accurate detection of eye problems can help prevent and treat eye problems and diseases in a timely manner to maintain a comfortable quality of life. Therefore, solving the eye problems of the Cambodian people is a special mission for the leaders of the Japanese Eye Hospital who are present in Cambodia.
Please note that Japan Eye Hospital is a hospital that is registered and licensed to provide services in Cambodia by the Ministry of Health of Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Youk Bunna, Permanent Secretary of State and Director of the Royal School of Administration of the Ministry of Public Works, highly appreciated the 2022 Senior Officials Internship at Nokor Phnom Level of the Royal School of Administration as a good example in participating in the work. Society.
During the ceremony, the Director of the Royal School of Administration also mentioned the purpose of creating a social work program in the Royal School of Administration. According to the Prime Minister, the establishment of this social program is for trainees to know how to work in a team, increase the spirit of solidarity, and share knowledge and wealth with others.
In addition, to improve the software skills of trainee officers to follow the code of ethics, set a good example, learn to recognize mistakes, remember self-correction, give up selfish views, do not get used to using reason as a hindrance in the work. Listen to the opinions of others wholeheartedly, know how to understand and know the actual situation in all circumstances.
According to Mr. Sreang Phanith, Director of the Training Department of the Royal School of Administration, in addition to studying for more than 500 hours, the interns at Nokor Phnom took valuable time to participate in social work with the management team of the Royal School of Administration four times. Contains:
The first time: in Kampong Speu province, the program of Vesak Bochea, Flower Festival, Solidarity and planting luxury saplings at the Cambodian Buddhist Cultural Center.
Second: In Siem Reap, tree planting program on both sides of the road to the Jayavarman-Norodom National Park "Phnom Kulen" and the celebration of International Biodiversity Day under the chairmanship of Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and Chairman of the National Council for Development By Sustainability and Wives.
Interns of the 2022 Senior Officials Training Course at Nokor Phnom Level also donated $ 15,000 to the Royal School of Administration to participate in the construction of Trapeang Treang Primary School in Trapeang Treang Village, Changkrang Commune, Chit Borei District, Kratie Province.
Mr. Thuong Samnang, Representative of the Interns, expressed his sincere gratitude and thanks to Mr. Youk Bunna, Permanent Secretary of State and Director of the Royal School of Administration of the Ministry of Public Works, and the leadership, teachers of the Royal School of Administration and professors. All taught at the Royal School of Administration and all stakeholders who paid attention, led and trained.
