Real estate experts say the creation of three new cities near Phnom Penh will increase property prices in the area.
(Phnom Penh): Real estate experts say that the establishment of three new cities in Kandal and Kampong Speu provinces near Phnom Penh is a good sign for the real estate sector, which will boost the momentum of sales and real estate prices.
Recently, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia decided to establish three new cities, including Arey Ksat, Sampov Poun in Kandal province and Oudong Mey Chey in Kampong Speu province.
Chrek Soknim, a Cambodian real estate expert, told Fresh News that the establishment of the three cities was a mechanism by the government to boost the region's economy to be more attractive and prosperous, as well as to increase its supply. Public services are closer and more efficient.
He says as the new city begins to build, demand for land will increase, pushing up property prices. However, the preparation of the new city requires the investment of the Royal Government to build better infrastructure.
He said that for 2023, land prices may not change much due to the poor economic situation as well as the protracted problems of the Ukraine war. However, from 2024 and 2025, land prices may increase from 20% to 30% of current prices.
Oknha Sam Sok Noeun, President of the Global Real Estate Association, said that the establishment of the new city is a good sign that the area has the potential to have a growing population and economy, as well as show that the Royal Government continues to develop infrastructure in Areas continue to grow. This is a good sign for property prices, which will push up land prices.
He added that in the past, the Noble King was an unprocessed diamond area, although this area was near Phnom Penh. However, after the Royal Government issued a sub-decree to formally establish a city, it means that the Royal Government is preparing to push the Noble Kingdom area to grow even more in terms of infrastructure and population growth.
However, he noted that the momentum of buying and selling as well as property prices in the Noble Kingdom may not be higher than it is now because the region has seen better growth in the past. But the area will have more potential, real estate prices and buying momentum will increase when the foundation of the bridge across the river is hit.
The other two cities, Sampov Poun near the Cambodian-Vietnamese border and Udong Mechey, which used to be rural and agricultural land, could be turned into residential, commercial and industrial land, which will drive up land prices in the area. This increased significantly when such a city was announced.
Two municipalities in Kandal province, Arey Ksat, were excluded from six communes in Khsach Kandal district and five communes in Lvea Em district, while Sampov Poun, which borders Vietnam, was excluded from five communes in Koh Thom district. With Udong Mechey town in Kampong Speu province being separated from Udong district by removing 5 communes from Udong district.
