On December 24, 2022, another healthy dolphin died floating in the area near Koh Trong, about 10 km away, according to the official WWF page published on December 25, 2022. Below Anlong Kampi, Kratie Province.
After a thorough examination of the dolphin's body, researchers from the Kratie Fisheries Administration and WWF initially concluded that the dolphin had died after twisting into a fishing line. Many fill its body and tail.
The dead dolphin was an adult female, 196 cm long, between 7 and 10 years old and weighing about 93 kg. The dolphin is the third healthy dolphin to die in just seven days, prompting an urgent call for stronger law enforcement in the dolphin sanctuary. .
WWF-Cambodia once again calls on all responsible authorities to mobilize and strengthen law enforcement urgently to increase day and night patrols to protect the remaining dolphins. From deaths due to illegal fishing in dolphin sanctuaries.
"There is no other option but to strictly enforce the law immediately to completely stop all forms of illegal activity in the area where the dolphins live," he added. Mr. Seng Teak insisted: "To stop these activities, all river guard officers and relevant law enforcement officers must be present 24 hours a day, once a week, regularly patrolling the area day and night. "Dolphins."
In addition to this patrol, the perpetrators of illegal fishing or other fishing offenses in the dolphin sanctuary must be severely punished for inciting other fishermen to stop their activities. These are illegal.
The dry season from December to May is a time of need for protection. When the water recedes, dolphins and fish come together to live and do business in the deep canyons of the dolphin sanctuary. This is why they are so vulnerable to illegal fishing. It is during this time that it is time to step up law enforcement.
On behalf of the Fisheries Administration of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kratie Province and on behalf of the district director himself, I would like to request all people, especially fishermen, not to use clear fishing gear. The Dolphin Conservation Administration has banned the use of traps, fishing nets, fishing rods, fishing nets, which endanger the lives of dolphins from day to day.
At the same time, he requested the local authorities to help guide the dissemination of the benefits of the Mekong River dolphin, a precious national treasure of Cambodia, and how to protect the Mekong River dolphins. Let our Mekong dolphins survive for the present and the future. China decides to release data on 19 daily Kovid cases and deaths
BEIJING: The Chinese Ministry of Health announced on Sunday that China will no longer release daily figures for 19 cases of Kovid disease and death after the practice began. Last since the beginning of 2020. This was released by the AFP news agency on Monday, December 26, 2022.
