(Phnom Penh): The Information and Quick Reaction Team of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police on December 26, 2022 issued a clarification regarding the case of a police officer of Teuk Thla Administration who posted the ID card of the National Police or Ministry of Interior through the social network TikTok.
Immediately, the Information and Quick Reaction Team of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and Lt. Col. Hour Meng Wang, Sen Sok District Police Inspector, conducted a search and summoned Lt. Col. Mech Meas, ID 86904, to clarify the case.
After the interrogation, Lieutenant Colonel Mech Meas admitted that he actually posted the above content, but had no intention of selling anything, the purpose was to show off to friends of the same force.
After that, the authority of Sen Sok District Police Inspectorate instructed, educated, made a contract and imposed administrative discipline by deciding to issue a warning letter by suspending work and withdrawing from office for 3 months and appearing in the administrative section of Sen Sok District Police Inspectorate every day. .
