The bodies of three more Thai sailors were pulled from the water after the sinking of a warship, while 11 others remain missing
BANGKOK, Dec. 25 (Xinhua) - The bodies of three other sailors were pulled from the water after the sinking of a warship in the Gulf of Thailand a week ago, the Thai navy said on Sunday. This was released by the AFP news agency on Sunday, December 25, 2022.
With this discovery, the number of bodies found so far is 18, while 11 crew members are still missing.
Rohingya refugee boat docks in Indonesia after drifting for more than a month
JAKARTA: A wrecked boat carrying 57 Rohingya refugees landed off the west coast of Indonesia on Sunday evening after drifting for more than a month. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Sunday, December 25, 2022.
Thousands of Rohingya seeking persecution in Myanmar risk their lives each year on frequent sea voyages on low-quality ships attempting to go to Malaysia or Indonesia.
Sunday evening's arrival comes after UNHCR and Southeast Asian politicians called for the rescue of another ship carrying 200 Rohingya refugees, including women and children, stranded in the area. Sea for several weeks.
