MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russian President Vladimir Putin condemned the West for trying to "divide" Russia in small pieces in an interview broadcast on state television on Sunday evening. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Sunday, December 25, 2022.
"At the heart of all this is the policy of Russia's geopolitical rivals, which aims to divide Russia historically," Putin said.
Putin used the concept of "historical Russia" to argue that Ukraine and Russia were originally one country and one people, justifying his 10-month invasion of Ukraine.
"We are moving in the right direction, we are defending our national interests, the interests of our people and our people," Putin said.
However, the Russian president reiterated that Moscow was ready to negotiate (to find) an acceptable solution with all players in the process of resolving the dispute.
