With Samdech Techo's visit to the US Embassy, the Deputy Prime Minister and Cambodian diplomat expressed confidence that Cambodia-US relations will continue to grow for the benefit of both countries.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon confirmed on his Facebook page, "It is a great pleasure to accompany the Prime Minister to visit the US Embassy in Phnom Penh yesterday evening as we celebrate the end of the year together."
"I am confident that the bilateral relations between the two countries will continue to grow for the mutual benefit of our people," he added.
It should be noted that on December 23, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen visited the US Embassy in Cambodia. During the visit, Samdech Techo and his delegation were warmly welcomed by US Ambassador Patrick Muffy and US Embassy staff.
According to the US Embassy, Ambassador Mofi and Samdech Techo Hun Sen have discussed ways to improve bilateral relations and hope that 2023 will be a fruitful and resilient year. Strive to strengthen the friendship between the American people and the Cambodian people.
Through that outreach, the United States appreciates Cambodia's leadership as ASEAN chair in a year of regional and global challenges.
The US Embassy also highlighted Cambodia's support for ASEAN chairmanship of the Special US-ASEAN Summit in Washington, DC, as well as hospitality for President Jo Biden's participation in the November Summit. Phnom Penh and support for the development of a comprehensive US-ASEAN strategic partnership.
