(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia-Kuwait Friendship Hospital organized a free consultation and treatment for 172 people with visual and physical disabilities under the chairmanship of Ms. Chhay Chanrithy Solida, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information and Honorary Vice President of the Music Association. The voice of the disabled represents Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information.
Mr. Chap To, President of Samneang Music Association for the Disabled, representing the visually impaired in Cambodia, is very excited that the Cambodian-Kuwait Hospital has organized medical check-ups for 172 visually impaired and physically fit people. Free of charge. Mr. Chap To confirmed that the Samneang Music Association for the Disabled is registered with the Ministry of Interior, with a total of 654 disabled members in the association, including 284 women.
In the past, Ms. Nhem Morakot, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, Honorary President of the Association, and Mr. Chap To have always considered the well-being and well-being of people with disabilities by seeking generous help and requesting intervention from Calmette Hospital, Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital, Russia Hospital Japan National Children's Hospital to help treat and operate on children with disabilities.
The director of the Cambodia-Kuwait Hospital said that when people with disabilities come to the hospital for treatment, even if they need serious surgery, the hospital does not charge a fee.
The director of Youth Street Cambodia also said that she will try to find donors to support food as well as find more skills and jobs for people with disabilities who are members of the Samneang Music Association for the Disabled.
