Cambodia will participate in the "Kuomintang-Montreal Global Biodiversity" framework adopted at the UN Summit on Biodiversity
This is a historic event in which 196 States Parties to the United Nations Convention on Biological Diversity have agreed in a global effort to protect 30% of the land, freshwater, coastal and oceans in the world. By 2030, only 17% of the mainland and 10% of the sea will be protected.
