US Congress approves $ 45 billion aid package for Ukraine
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The US House of Representatives on Friday approved the latest $ 45 billion aid package for Ukraine following a visit by the Ukrainian president to Washington this week. This was released by the AFP news agency on Saturday, December 24, 2022.
The package, approved by the Democrat-controlled House of Representatives, is part of the US government's $ 1.66 trillion budget, which passed the Senate on Thursday. Therefore, it will now be forwarded to US President Joe Biden for signature.
The new US package will add to the nearly $ 50 billion military, financial and humanitarian aid that Washington has provided to Ukraine in 2022 since the outbreak of war.
