Prior to 2020, the United States treated Hong Kong, a separate WTO member from China, in a similar manner, before the city was ceded from British rule to China in July 1997.
US President Donald Trump then signed an order demanding a change of status, with Washington saying the Chinese city of Hong Kong was not autonomous enough to be treated differently from China. The WTO framework. This regulation will come into force at the end of 2020.
Reuters reports that a three-member WTO jury found that the United States had violated its obligations to Hong Kong by treating the city unfairly compared to other WTO members in terms of requirements. Identify the origin of the city’s commodity products.
The United States has said it has implemented an exemption law that allows action to be taken to protect a country's "vital security interests."
The WTO jury acknowledged that tensions had risen between the United States and Hong Kong, but said they had not risen to the level of "emergency in international relations", the level required. The exemption conditions that the United States applies.
The commission concluded its 96-page report with a suggestion that the United States should implement its measures in accordance with global trade law.
The United States has said it strongly rejects the interpretation and conclusion that the WTO resolution is "erroneous" and that it does not intend to exclude the application of identification requirements. This goods.
Meanwhile, the Hong Kong government welcomed the decision and said it had reaffirmed its special status as a separate customs territory from China. According to Reuters.
Ministry recommends the Department of Tourism to compile statistics and expenses of guests during the Global New Year
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has instructed the Department of Tourism in all capitals and provinces to make a summary report on tourist statistics and tourist expenses at resorts and tourist destinations and to send it to the Ministry of Tourism in a timely manner.
This guidance is set out in the circular on the management of tourist flows and the improvement of tourism products during the Global New Year, which will take place from December 31, 2022 and January 1, 2023. .
This circular has 5 points that the Ministry of Tourism has pointed out to the Department of Tourism in all capitals and provinces to participate in the implementation, and in the fifth point, the Ministry of Tourism has instructed the Department of Tourism to "..... make a summary report. "Statistics and spending of tourists at resorts and destinations will be sent to the Ministry of Tourism in a timely manner on a daily basis."
It should be noted that in the past, the Ministry of Tourism has always published statistics on weekly tourists as well as during major festivals, but there is not much information related to the cost of tourists, especially in the new circular. Additional requirements to sum up the cost of tourists.
