(Battambang): The Battambang Provincial Department of Commerce, in collaboration with NGOs and relevant institutions, organizes exhibitions of community products and small and medium enterprises to promote farmers' products such as chickens, eggs, rice, all kinds of vegetables, rice, agricultural products and equipment. Agriculture.
Mr. Nget Vibol said that this program was carried out under the framework of the project "Creating Job Opportunities in Rural Areas to Rehabilitate the Economy of People Affected by Kovid 19 (RECOVER)" which received funding from the European Union for 3 years. Year from January 2021 to December 2023, implemented in 5 target provinces around Tonle Sap Lake, including Battambang, Siem Reap, Kampong Thom, Kampong Chhnang and Pursat.
The project works with the Royal Government to help rehabilitate the rural population who have lost their jobs and lost their livelihoods due to the global Kovid 19 disease by ensuring food security, income and community employment opportunities for workers. Migrant workers and the unemployed, working closely with the private sector, civil society organizations, and improving relations between producers, processors and buyers.
In addition, smallholder farmers will increase food production and adequate food through vegetable and animal husbandry by better applying agricultural techniques, products and services, and migrant workers and the unemployed with Kovid disease. 19 will gain skills related to financial markets and social protection.
