German company BioNTech launches human trial to test malaria vaccine
BERLIN (Reuters) - German company BioNTech on Friday launched a preliminary study to evaluate the human efficacy of its experimental vaccine against malaria. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, December 23, 2022.
The effort is among a handful of efforts to develop a vaccine to fight the mosquito-borne disease, which kills more than 600,000 people a year, mostly children. In Africa. The forms as well as the complex life cycles of malaria parasites have long hindered efforts to develop vaccines against the disease.
Efforts are underway to develop another malaria vaccine that is under close scrutiny: the University of Oxford University Vaccine Candidate. Data from its mid-range test were released to the public in September.
WHO officials claim that soaking alcohol for women after childbirth is useless and causes problems for mothers and children
(Phnom Penh): After seeing the tradition of the ancients who mistakenly soaked in alcohol for women to give birth and drink without knowing the effects of drinking, Dr. Yil Daravuth, an official of the World Health Organization. Claiming that soaking alcohol for postpartum women to drink is a complete misconception because it is not only useless, it also causes problems for mothers and children.
This morning, December 23, 2022, Dr. Yil Daravuth addressed the seminar on the effects of alcohol on women, organized by the Health Action Coordinating Committee. (HACC) and the Cambodian Movement for Health (CMH) in collaboration with the Ministry of Women's Affairs at the Diamond Center in Phnom Penh.
The Consultative Workshop on the Impact of Alcohol on Women was organized with the aim of disseminating the effects of alcohol use on women, exploring national and international legal frameworks related to alcohol, and supporting measures. Effective to reduce the effects of alcohol on women.
He said that the use of alcohol affects people, both men and women, but women are more vulnerable than men because after drinking alcohol can increase the risk of hepatitis, breast cancer, menopause that can develop. To osteoporosis.
Dr. Yil Daravuth added that if a woman is pregnant and consuming ethanol in alcohol will affect the fetus, both physically and mentally, and at birth will have mental health problems. Not as good as others, especially facing the problem of birth defects and so on.
On that occasion, representatives of the Ministry of Women's Affairs and national and international organizations also acknowledged that the use of alcohol and the promotion of alcohol by all means have a significant impact on women, including the violation of the right to live without action. The director of the Kandal Provincial Department of Rural Development is determined to do a better job after Kandal became the third province to end open defecation (Video inside)
