Chinese Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Jiang Yu's Regular Press Conference on Hong Kong Case
BEIJING, Dec. 21 (Xinhua) - The World Trade Organization (WTO) dispute settlement team for the China-Hong Kong case filed a report on US measures to determine the origin of US goods on Tuesday, citing US measures and restrictions on certification. The origin of the goods violates WTO rules.
At a regular press conference on December 22, while answering questions on the matter, Chinese Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Mao Ning said China urges the United States to respect the "expert judgment" and correct its mistakes. Practical term.
"China welcomes the fair trial of WTO experts," Mao Ning said. Hong Kong's role as a separate tariff zone with China is to be approved by the Chinese government and to be certified in the "Basic Law of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China" as well as to recognize multilateral law. Of the WTO, but not of any Member State.
"China will strictly adhere to the one-country policy and strictly oppose the external forces that come to interfere in Hong Kong's affairs, and strongly support Hong Kong's role as a tariff zone," Mao said. "Apart from China, it strongly supports Hong Kong to strengthen and expand its role as a center for finance, tourism and international trade."
