The Hor Namhong-Borei Hor Foundation will continue to help with this surgery and call on philanthropists to help save Soeun Srey Oun, who could not survive without the new bowel surgery.
The Cambodian position was made at an informal ministerial consultation on the situation in Myanmar, hosted by Thai Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs Don Pramatwinai in Bangkok, Thailand on December 22, 2022.
The meeting was also attended by the Foreign Ministers of Laos and the Deputy Foreign Minister of Vietnam, as well as the Ministers of the Republic of the Union of Myanmar in charge of Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation and Investment and Foreign Economic Relations.
The consultation was conducted in accordance with Article 14 of the ASEAN Leaders' Review and Resolution on the Implementation of the Five-Point Consensus (5PC), emphasizing the importance of finding ways to support the work. ASEAN's joint efforts to help Myanmar bring a peaceful solution to the current crisis
According to a statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the meeting also commended Cambodia's efforts and the work of the Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair to facilitate the implementation of the 5PC, especially in the area of providing humanitarian assistance to people in need. .
Ministry of Tourism and AFD Disseminate Joint Achievements After More Than 4 Years
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism and the French Agency for Development (AFD) have held a workshop to disseminate the achievements of the TCBP after four and a half years.
The workshop was held on the afternoon of December 22, 2022 at the Cambodiana Hotel, chaired by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, and Mr. Jacques Perle, Ambassador of the French Republic to Cambodia, and Ms. Sandrin Bousse, Director of the French Agency for Development (AFD) in Cambodia. .
Mr. Aing Sovannaroth said that as a result, the TCBP program was implemented on 18 major activities, and subdivided into more than 24 activities, which focused on strengthening the capacity of officials of the Ministry and the Department of Tourism to implement policies and strategies. Development of Cambodia's tourism sector, strengthening the capacity of the private sector in tourism, pilot implementation of research projects and some study projects.
The TCBP Implementation Team has developed a joint development plan for the Tassal and Tapeu Dam resorts, studying the potentials of the Totepuot and surrounding areas to develop a strategic plan for tourism development in the area. Potential ecotourism and ecotourism destinations and isolation.
In addition, the TCBP program provides legal support activities that study the legal requirements for tourism vocational schools and for the tourism industry association, as well as the development of professional ethics and professional codes of conduct for tourism vocational schools. And the Tourism Industry Association, which will contribute to strengthening the quality of the Cambodian tourism industry and orienting the tourism profession.
On that occasion, the French Ambassador considered the implementation of those projects as another testament to France's participation in helping Cambodia's socio-economic sector.
Jacques Pelé believes that the fruits of implementing the Trade Capacity Building in Tourism (TCBP) program will help create economic opportunities for the local tourism community and help promote Cambodian tourism to a wider global market, which is beneficial to the recovery. The Cambodian economy in the future.
The Trade Capacity Building in Tourism (TCBP) program also focuses on collaborating with the private sector in the French tourism sector, as there are currently French investors who have been investing in the tourism industry. In Cambodia, such as hotels, guesthouses, restaurants, resorts, etc. in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap and Kampot.
Dr. Sok Touch expects that China will help Cambodia restore and dig canals connecting rivers to the sea to facilitate the transportation of goods by water
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, expressed hope that the Chinese government will help restore and dig canals along the Bassac River from Prek Ambel to the sea to facilitate water transport.
Dr. continued that for the planning of the restoration of waterways and satellite construction of Cambodia is a direction that is very important to shorten the transport distance from all rivers to the sea, reduce the time and distance. Reduce transportation costs, reduce traffic accidents and pressure on road use, as well as increase waterway transport activities.
"We take it by land, it is very expensive, but if we take it by water, it is cheaper. We know that 100 cars is equal to one train, 10 trains, one train, so having a cargo ship makes it cheaper and easier to carry goods." Compete. ”
Dr. Sok Touch said that Cambodia and China are related on five major points from the past to the present, including history, economy, culture, environment and the future.
Among these five points is the economic sector, with China helping to make Cambodia prosperous by investing in other sectors and increasing property prices in Cambodia. He hopes that at the end of Kovid-19, Chinese investors will come to invest more in Cambodia.
Please be informed that the Royal Government has authorized the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to study the restoration of waterways along the Bassac River from Prek Ambel to Takeo, Kampot and Kep provinces, a distance of 168 kilometers.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, confirmed that the Ministry will dig a new canal between 5-7 km between the river and the sea to facilitate water transport from the river to the port of Kep.
The General Department of Inland Waterway Transport and Ports of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport have taken a step-by-step study of this process, with the results confirming that the 168-kilometer waterway from Prek Ambel to Takeo and connected to Kep Port is 68%. Existing rivers and more than 20% are irrigation systems that need to be rehabilitated and expanded.
Currently, Cambodia is making steady progress in the field of transportation, both land and water. The Royal Government, through the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, has expanded the potential of the inland waterway transport sector as part of its contribution to national economic growth. Cambodia Angkor Air announces first flight between Siem Reap and Hanoi
Cambodia Angkor Air returned to Siem Reap at 5:15 pm and arrived at 7:00 pm the same day with 81 passengers on board.
Cambodia Angkor Air has confirmed that from today onwards, Cambodia Angkor Air will operate three regular flights a week between Siem Reap and Hanoi, every Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday.
Please note that Cambodia Angkor Air has set its vision to be the leading airline in Cambodia and the first airline in Cambodia to receive the International Air Transport Association (IOSA) Safety Operation Certificate and be an official member of This organization started in 2017, which made the company gain high trust from passengers and business partners both at home and abroad.
