Minister of Commerce thanks Australia for contributing to development in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, thanked the Australian Government and people for their assistance in developing Cambodia as well as promoting trade in Cambodia.
The Minister thanked Australia in a meeting with Australian Ambassador to Cambodia Pablo Kang. On the afternoon of December 22, 2022, Mr. Pablo Kang met with the Minister of Commerce after his term as Australian Ambassador to Cambodia.
During the meeting, Mr. Pan Sosak extended a warm welcome and congratulations to the Ambassador for his successful mission in Cambodia, as well as appreciated the Ambassador's active role and contribution in Promote Cambodia-Australia cooperation and relations, especially in the field of trade.
On that occasion, the Minister also celebrated the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries and thanked the Government and people of Australia for their continued support for the economic and social development of Cambodia, including Sponsorship of Kovid-19 vaccine, a contribution to the Royal Government of Cambodia's vaccination campaign.
