WASHINGTON (Reuters) - Concerns in recent days that Belarus may be forced to take part in the war in Ukraine and the resumption of operations in the capital Kiev from Belarus have been on the rise. Especially after President Vladimir Putin's visit to Minsk to meet with his counterpart Alexander Lukashenko earlier this week.
In addition, in recent months of war, Belarus has allowed thousands of Russian troops to deploy tanks and other weapons, as well as to allow Russian warplanes to use its air bases to launch attacks across Ukraine. Russia has also used drone strikes to destroy power infrastructure in Kiev and other Ukrainian cities.
But there could be two major scenarios if Belarus decides to help Russia. Scenario 1: That is an attack on the capital Kiev, but the target is not completely controlling the capital. Ukraine's victory in expelling Russian troops from Kiev shows that Belarus is not a partner of the Ukrainian army, which is using Western-supplied weapons.
A renewed attack on the Kiev capital could divert attention from Ukrainian troops on the front lines in the eastern and southern regions of the country. This means that such attacks are intended to force Ukraine to withdraw its troops or weapons to defend the capital Kiev, to give Russia a chance to re-launch offensive operations in order to seize or control much or completely of the four territories. Putin annexes Russia
Scenario 2: That is the attack by the Belarusian army on some areas of western Ukraine bordering Poland, where there has been a lull from war for more than 10 months and a major supply route used by Ukraine. In transporting humanitarian aid and weapons from Western countries. In this scenario, even if it is not a big success, it can at least cause endless problems on the Ukrainian border.
The war in Ukraine is currently focusing on the south and east of Ukraine, but it can not be underestimated from the border with Belarus, which experts believe could be the next hotspot. The Ukraine War in 2023.
Dr. Sok Touch: In the next 3 years, Cambodia will have Cambodian Chinese language teachers with full training and clear pedagogical skills
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, expressed his optimism that in the next three years, Cambodia will have Cambodian Chinese language teachers with full training and competence with sufficient pedagogical knowledge to continue. Sustainable Chinese language training.
Dr. Sok Touch made the remarks while presiding over a keynote address at the Scientific Forum on "Cambodia-China Relations and Commemoration of the 100th Anniversary of His Majesty the King" organized by the Confucius Institute at the Royal Academy of Cambodia on December 22, 2022.
Dr. Sok Touch The Confucius Institute at the Royal Academy of Cambodia has become one of the best Confucius Institutes in the world, training Chinese language human resources and integrating a better understanding of Chinese culture in Cambodia.
However, the President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia decided to set up a regional Chinese language pedagogical institute to train advanced Chinese language human resources with pedagogical knowledge to contribute to the strengthening of Chinese language training in Cambodia as the Chinese language became An important language in communication, economy, trade, diplomacy, tourism and other functions in Cambodian society as well as in the world of globalization.
In addition, he stressed that because Cambodia and China are steel friends, strategic partners in all fields and have reached the highest level of communication in history, the study of language, culture and history about each other is the main point. In strengthening and expanding cooperation, mutual understanding, connection and exchange between Cambodia and China.
Dr. Sok Touch emphasized that in the historical relationship between Cambodia and China for thousands of years, the two countries have never opened a Chinese language pedagogical training course, and the past experience has shown very well. Clearly need to continue to train Chinese language human resources to contribute to building a stronger Cambodian-Chinese community of common destiny.
He also pointed out that through this vision, the Royal Academy of Cambodia will achieve the goal of building human resources in the Chinese language training in the next three years.
