Siem Reap Provincial Health Department Holds a Working Group Meeting to Eliminate Malaria in the Fourth Quarter of 2022
(Siem Reap): In the afternoon of December 21, 2022, the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department held a meeting of the Provincial Working Group for Malaria Eradication for the fourth quarter of 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Pin Prak, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province and Dr. Kros Sarath, Director of the Provincial Health Department, as well as the participation of about 59 relevant departments and units.
Dr. Kros Sarath, Director of the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department, stated that the purpose of the meeting was to update the malaria situation, achievements, challenges and implementation directions towards the complete eradication of malaria by 2025. To strengthen the role of the Malaria Eradication Task Force and to intervene in a timely response to malaria, challenges and solutions are discussed.
Mr. Kras Sarath said that in order to provide recommendations and implementation directions to achieve the goal of eliminating malaria, psychological challenges and discussions on research tests in some ODs have been a bit slow, especially the implementation. HCS test.
If anyone has malaria, they are not allowed to be treated at any private clinic and are sent to a public hospital. About 777 out of 60,000 people, 24 of them, tested positive. There are more positive cases than in previous years, as well as Pf, which is a serious type, so the Department of Health has advised local authorities to be involved in promoting the most active prevention methods.
At the same time, Mr. Pin Prak, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap, said that we must work together to prevent and prevent malaria in 2025 in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government. Malaria is not only in our country, but also in some countries.
At the same time, Mr. Pin Prak also urged the team to carry out outreach activities as well as the distribution of mosquito nets in health centers or communes in Siem Reap province. In that, 69 mosquito nets were distributed to health centers and 100 percent were distributed, especially the authorities of some villages, communes and ODs in the province to participate in disseminating education related to malaria to the people to recover with the spread. Of this malaria as well.
(Phnom Penh): Traders in the transport sector say that at present, large trucks use the expressway to transport goods is limited due to the high cost of road services, which makes them more expensive. In each transport, they want the Royal Government to consider in talks with the road construction companies to lower the current price.
Businessmen in the field of transportation said this in response to the speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on December 22, calling for the return to use the expressway to transport goods for profit and fuel. Time.
Samdech calls on the owners of transport companies to use the expressway at a time when gasoline prices are currently rising, and if they turn to the expressway will greatly reduce gasoline consumption, while the cost of use is only $ 12. Only. At the same time, the use of highways by these large trucks will contribute to greatly reducing traffic accidents on Route 4.
Samdech Techo further emphasized, "I observe that there are no trucks on the expressway on the expressway. At this point, I should warn the truck owners, car owners." Using highways is more profitable than conventional roads, less fuel, more time in the supply chain. " I appeal to owners who have more cars to use expressways to use the economy more profitably than to leave in the narrow lane."
Speaking to Fresh News on December 22, 2022, Mr. Chea Chandara, President of the Association of Freight Forwarders and Supply Chains, said that in the past, some transport companies that are members of the association have used the expressway, but Very few, unless absolutely necessary, that the goods are in a hurry or fear of unloading, decide to use this expressway.
He explained that the reason they decided not to use the expressway to transport goods was due to the high cost and high cost of repairs if the car broke down on the road one by one.
He said that although the road construction company has reduced the price, the transporters still understand that the price is still high, that is, every transport company costs from $ 54 to more than $ 60 per foot, which includes It costs $ 108. The second problem is that if there is a broken car on the road, the company will have to spend a lot of money on repair costs, both remote call and towing.
He asked the Royal Government to "ask the Royal Government to help talk with the expressway company in the review related to the price. At the same time, the repair should also be considered at a price that we can accept, because most of the cars used in Cambodia, we imported cars are used cars, so if Damage, it is difficult for them.
Expressway - Phnom Penh Sihanoukville is the first expressway and the most important strategic corridor in Cambodia. Reduces travel time from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville seaport from five hours to just two hours and reduces Logistics costs as well.
Heang Sotheayut, Director General of the General Department of Technology and Public Relations of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, said that during the 80 days of operation on the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, more than 83,000 vehicles were in traffic. On average, there are about 10,000 vehicles per day.
Commentary: Agreements with real value will indicate the direction of governance on global biodiversity
In a context where global biodiversity is being severely undermined, public opinion generally recognizes that this "framework" of practical value seems to be the "Paris Agreement" on the conservation of nature, which clearly sets goals and paths for global biodiversity governance. From now to 2030 and longer.
The results were encouraging, but the process was difficult. Due to differences between developed and developing countries on responsibilities, rights and interests in biodiversity conservation, and differences in knowledge, capital and capacity, there were significant differences of opinion at the meeting. During the key moments, as chair of COP15, China played a guiding role in coordinating the parties and promoting the meeting process.
If comparing global biodiversity conservation to the construction of skyscrapers, our humanity now has a detailed engineering plan. Only by design engineering can the concept of "by 2050 coexist in harmony between humanity and nature" be achieved. Furthermore, the parties must not only maintain strong political will, but also demonstrate executive strength.
