(Phnom Penh): On December 20, 2022, Mr. Ly Chantola, President of the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia, signed a decision on "Honors of the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia".
The establishment of this honor to equip and present to the members of the Bar Association and dignitaries who have done meritorious deeds and loyalty to the Bar Association, the legal profession and social justice as a thank you, encourage, promote and strengthen the capacity of lawyers for excellence. And the prestige of the legal profession in five categories:
1: Honors of Excellence: To equip and present to the President of the Bar Association, the former President of the Bar Association, the Bar Council, the former Council of the Bar Association, the Director of the Bar Professional Training Center, the former Director of the Bar Professional Training Center or dignitaries to thank for outstanding achievements. Or good governance, which is in the best interests of the legal profession and the Bar Association.
2. Honors: To equip and provide lawyers with many years of membership and seniority to honor and respect as a senior in the legal profession.
3: Social honors: To equip and provide lawyers who have dedicated their time, energy, physical strength and personal budget to contribute to the promotion of social justice to the poor, the weak or the minority.
4: Honors Qualifications: To equip and provide lawyers who have dedicated their time, energy, and physical strength to training, research, publishing and dissemination, which are in the field of justice and the profession of lawyers or lawyers who have contributed money to the work. And the activities of the Bar.
5: Honors: For equipping and giving to the deceased lawyer as a reminder and remembrance of the heroism, achievements and merits of the legal profession.
The establishment of this bar honor is in response to the sixth point of the policy of Mr. Ly Chantola, President of the Bar Association, which was promised during the election campaign for the President of the Bar Association in the 13th mandate (2020-2022).
