Mikami Masahiro is an ambassador who has tried to use the Khmer language through messages on the embassy's Facebook page as well as in public forums. By trying to use the Khmer language, he gained a lot of attention and respect from the Cambodian people.
With the completion of his mission in Cambodia, Mr. Mikami Masahiro expressed his deep gratitude for supporting his work for 3 years and 4 months in Cambodia.
In his message to the Cambodian people, the Ambassador emphasized, "I would like to remind you of my mandate with sincere gratitude to the Cambodian people."
The Ambassador recalled that he began his mission in September 2019. He said that despite the challenges of the Kovid-19 crisis, Japan-Cambodia relations have progressed well at all levels, from top-level visits to grassroots exchanges in all areas.
"This year, the Prime Ministers of our two countries, His Excellency Kisida Fumio and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, met four times in Cambodia and Japan and last month announced that they would upgrade bilateral relations to next year, the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between our two countries." This is the confirmation of Mr. Mikami Masahiro.
In his farewell message to the Cambodian people, the Ambassador praised the great achievements of the Cambodian people, even though the country was devastated by the civil war.
"I am pleased that Japan has contributed to the peace process and the reconstruction of the country," he added. "Currently, the relationship between Cambodia and Japan has been expanding not only in terms of assistance from Japan, but also in business and other sectors, as the Cambodian economy grows and Cambodia's capabilities improve."
The Ambassador recalled during his time in Cambodia that he had the opportunity to meet many Cambodians and experience Cambodian culture through gatherings and events. He now has a better understanding of the country and the people of Cambodia compared to when he first arrived.
He added that he is happy to see that people's lives have improved over the past 30 years, but there are still many challenges ahead.
The Ambassador wished Cambodia more democratic development towards a society that leaves no one and everyone happier.
Mr. Mikami Masahiro also said that after completing his mission in Cambodia, he will continue to work in Belgium.
Despite finishing work in Cambodia, he will continue to be a strong supporter of Cambodia and Cambodia-Japan relations.
