NEC Holds a Meeting to Decide on the Comments of Stakeholders Regarding the Draft Regulations and Procedures for the 7th National Assembly Election
Regarding the regulations and procedures for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023, the NEC has reviewed all the recommendations of the relevant parties who have made suggestions to the NEC.
After a thorough discussion based on the principles of the law in force and the experience of the previous election, some recommendations were accepted by the NEC and some were not. The NEC meeting decided to ask Mr. Tep Nytha, Secretary General of the NEC, to adjust the spirit of the meeting and respond in writing to those parties, stating the reasons for accepting and rejecting.
The NEC meeting also reviewed and approved the documents to be used in selecting the composition of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission (CEC) for 175 members of the 7th National Assembly Election 2023, which is Short-term contracted officers for 25 provincial capitals.
The composition of the Election Commission to be selected for each Capital and Province is 7 people with the following positions:
1: Chairman of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission 1: Deputy Chairman of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission 1: 3: Member in charge of Administration 4: Member in charge of Finance 1: Member in charge of Finance 1 Electoral and Technical Operations 6: 1 Member in Charge of Legal Services, Dispute and Electoral Security 7: 1 Member in charge of Education, Information and Public Relations.
According to the recruitment calendar for the above short-term contract staff, the recruitment will be announced in early January 2023.
Finally, Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC, instructed the specialized units to pay attention to the training and education of election officials in implementing the rules and procedures for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023. Accurate and effective, especially polling station officials and counting ballots.
