Announcing the new Commander of the Battambang Provincial Gendarmerie, General Sao Sokha Introduces 3 Core Work to Strengthen Work Efficiency and Maintain Internal Unity
(Battambang): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, this morning, December 22, 2022, presided over the inauguration of the new Provincial Gendarmerie Commander. Battambang by Brigadier General Hem Vuthy, replacing Brigadier General Meas Sovann.
Speaking on the occasion, General Sao Sokha stated that the appointment, promotion and change of positions in the Armed Forces, civil servants, as well as the private sector, is a rule of thumb in organizing human resources for job growth and also Opportunity to change the workplace environment Change of position has four key benefits:
* First: to protect the honor and dignity of officers * Second: to organize human resources in accordance with the ability, skills and temperament * Third: to provide opportunities for successors * Fourth: to share good experiences in Aims to make organizational units grow simultaneously. On the other hand, to change the work environment, increase capacity through learning.
For the commander to be appointed today, Brigadier General Hem Vuthy should take care of three core tasks:
* First: Management - People management must understand and implement 7 points, including: eating, dressing, accommodation, health, education, transportation, entertainment and problem solving - maintenance work, facilities and equipment - work Property Management - Work Processes by Administration and Army Hierarchy
* Second: Unit building work - Work place (building, office and workplace) - Education place - Training place for the army to stay and eat in the unit
