Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on transport companies to use the expressway to transport goods for profit (Video inside) (Sihanoukville): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, calls on transport companies to use Expressway to transport goods for profit, fuel, time and reduce accidents on National Road 4.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this call on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the inauguration of the road connecting Prey Nup district to Sihanoukville with a total length of more than 43 kilometers in the morning of Thursday, December 22. This 2022.
Samdech Techo added: "I observe that there are no trucks on the expressway on the expressway, at this point I should warn truck owners, car owners. Using highways is more profitable than conventional roads, less fuel, more time in the supply chain. " I appeal to owners who have more cars to use expressways to use the economy more profitably than to leave in the narrow lane."
Samdech calls on transport company owners to use the expressway at a time when petrol prices are currently rising, and if they switch to the expressway, it will significantly reduce fuel consumption while the cost of use is only $ 12. Only. At the same time, the use of highways by these large trucks will contribute to greatly reducing traffic accidents on Route 4.
Expressway - Phnom Penh Sihanoukville is the first expressway and the most important strategic corridor in Cambodia. Reduces travel time from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville seaport from five hours to just two hours and reduces The cost of logistics as well. Prek Pnov District Governor Calls for People to Seek Services at OWSO Do Not Rely on Others
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Them Sar An, Governor of Prek Pnov District, requested the people who need any service, please go to the OWSO yourself to receive the service, please do not rely on them, if you rely on others Money and you always put the burden on the authorities to eliminate the mediator, we do not need a mediator. We, the service providers, we need to meet the people who come to receive services, the people who are in need of services, the government agencies as the service providers.
