The groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the reinforced concrete road by Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh took place in the presence of Mr. Them Sam An, Governor of Prek Pnov District, Deputy District Governor Mr. Hour Huot and Mr. Chea Virak, as well as professional officials. More than 200 people.
"This is another new achievement of Ponsaing commune, which is a precious gift of Mr. Khuong Sreng. He always thinks very much about the well-being of the people," he said. "The governor always promotes the process of local development, including the construction of new roads or repair damaged roads, such as the road we are opening this site, as well as other important physical infrastructure."
"Last week, under my coordination, I successfully led the opening of a 12-meter-wide, 1,000-meter-long road in Boeung Vun village, and now it has been built as a paved road with pits and compacted soil," he said. Volunteers donate land next to the road and have philanthropists help build the road. This is a good participation of the people of Sangkat Pansang Yeung in our local development process.
At the same time, the district governor requested the people to cooperate with the district authorities in providing various information related to local irregularities, especially before the non-criminal signs that cause social insecurity. All information provided by the authorities will be kept confidential, which means that you have joined the authorities in implementing the policy (safe villages and communes) effectively.
With this request for interpretation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also continued to criticize the person But Bun Tinh, who always considered himself smart when going to the new United States and that those who went to the United States in the past were also fools. Minister of Cults and Religions calls on all priests to join in curbing acts of exploitation of religion
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chhit Sokhon, Minister of Cult and Religion, recommended that all abbots and abbots throughout the country cooperate with the clergy at pagodas and relevant authorities to prevent activities that exploit religion. To value Buddhism as the state religion.
This introduction was made during the 7th meeting with 1,000 priests and nuns from all over the country in the capital-province, with the participation of the leaders of the relevant ministries, institutions, cults and religions in the capital-province today. December 22, 2022
On that occasion, Minister Chhit Sokhon contributed to make a number of recommendations to promote the implementation of religious beliefs, practices in accordance with the Khmer traditions and customs, and to strengthen the power of priests and nuns to promote the values of culture, traditions and religion to remain stable. Into the currents of globalization and development in all areas.
He advised all abbots to work closely with the pagoda to help improve the pagoda to be beautiful, have a good environment, suitable as a resort and a place of worship.
"In particular, it is necessary to comply with the existing legal documents to prevent all activities in the form of business exploitation, which affects the value of Buddhism, which is the state religion," he said.
He added that the abbots who have studied the training must adhere to the roles, duties and ethics, avoid pride alone, must know how to cooperate with the monks, the committee of abbots, whether in pagodas or ceremonies must be wise. In finding procedures to resolve all the needs of monks and Buddhists of all backgrounds.
He added that the Acharya-Acharini must continue to increase knowledge, research the scriptures, ordinances, rules, rituals, ceremonies and other ceremonies, especially the general principles that have been studied in the past to apply and disseminate more widely at the local level.
Mr. Chhit Sokhon further advised that the Acharya-Acharini must not be biased against castes, which is an act of lack of virtue and cause disputes or athikar in the pagoda or in the community.
The Minister called on the Acharya-Acharini to strive to contribute to the implementation of the Royal Government's political program related to the field of religion, tradition and customs, and to understand the progress of the society by educating and continuing to spread to Buddhists in all walks of life.
He went on to call on the Acharya-Acharini to adhere to the seven kinds of charity: to know the cause, to know the result, to know the self, to know the estimate, to know the time, to know the saint and Know the person to be worthy as an elder with experience and knowledge in the village, commune, district, city, province, capital and area.
At the same time, Minister Chhit Sokhon also instructed the priests to be able to explain the meaning of each ritual clearly and lead Buddhists and the masses to be faithful in Buddhism to love and care for. The cultural heritage, traditions and customs of the nation to be stable and long-lasting help prevent the influx of various cultures.
