(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance this morning, December 22, 2022, signed a cooperation financing agreement with the Asian Development Bank (ADB) and the French Agency for Development (AFD) for six projects / programs. A total of 381.45 million US dollars and 1 technical assistance financing of 1.7 million US dollars to support the implementation of the energy sector development program.
1: Energy Sector Development Program - The first sub-program aims to support Cambodia's transition to clean energy, which will promote sustainable economic growth, accelerate the pace of green economy and reduce carbon emissions, and boost Competitive investment in the energy sector through public-private partnership mechanisms.
2. The Sustainable Marine and Coastal Fisheries Project aims to develop maritime institutions and infrastructure to enhance marine fisheries productivity, diversify the resilience of climate-resilient fishermen, promote sustainable development and promote marine fisheries trade. .
3. The Transboundary Animal Health Project and the Promotion of Animal Value Chains have two main objectives: 1. To increase productivity, quality, trade, diversification and expansion of animal husbandry and processing of livestock products in accordance with the framework of the strategic plan for Livestock development in 2016-2025 and 2. Promote livestock health and expand the value chain infrastructure with environmental brotherhood.
4: Border Health Project in the Greater Mekong Subregion aims to improve access to health services for people living along the border and some cross-border migrants, with a focus on improving the quality of health services and Financial protection for health care services for migrants.
5: Trade and Competitiveness Development Program - The first sub-program aims to promote trade efficiency and competitiveness in Cambodia, focusing on three factors, namely: 1. Promoting a favorable environment for investment and employment. Business, secondly, to promote the growth of small and medium enterprises, and thirdly, to improve trade policies and trade facilitation.
6. The Science and Technology Project for Secondary Education aims to improve the quality and efficiency of upper secondary education by focusing on three factors, namely: Expanding the scope of standardized and equitable secondary education; second, strengthening the quality of education in science, technology, engineering and mathematics; and third, improving institutions in planning, management and teaching.
The workshop was held from the 19th and ended on the 21st of December 2022 for about 18 leaders, professors, doctors and professors of medicine from the University of Health Sciences of Cambodia and the University of Medicine and Medicine of Ho Chi Minh City. This training was conducted at the University of Health Sciences.
In addition to the continuity of management and distance learning - teaching of educational institutions, this training contributes to improving the quality of teaching by providing knowledge and skills in managing students' learning, managing and organizing lessons. As well as the inclusion of lessons in various forms and activities according to the pedagogy of teachers, professors, exams or assessments online, etc.
