Mr. Heang Sotheayut said that for the largest amount of traffic in the last 80 days, in November 2022, during the Water Festival with up to 18,000 traffic. Per day and in December, there is about 15,000 traffic per day.
The director general of the General Department of Technology said that after the Ministry cooperated with the expressway company to automate the payment of travel on the expressway to facilitate people's travel. It is noteworthy that there is no traffic congestion on this expressway, although there are many vehicles on the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway.
At the same time, Mr. Heang Sotheayut also pointed out that for the last period, the growth of trucks on the expressway has also increased significantly compared to the initial launch. He claimed, however, that the number was still small compared to expectations before the expressway was opened.
Heang Sotheayut also expressed confidence that with the increasing volume of traffic on the expressway of this heavy truck will continue to improve, which will improve both the private sector, vehicle owners and The private sector benefits by reducing time, budget savings and reducing the rate of road accidents.
The expressway is divided into three lanes and three lanes, including:
Roads for normal traffic: Drivers of all types of vehicles must drive on the right lane of the freeway, which is the lane for normal traffic.
* Overtaking lane: In case of overtaking, the driver must give a left turn signal for at least 5 seconds and turn to the left lane of the freeway which is the lane for overtaking. When overtaking, the driver must give the right turn signal to return to the lane for normal traffic.
In case of heavy traffic, drivers can use both lanes, while heavy vehicles must adhere to the lane for normal traffic. In this case, the vehicle on any lane driving faster is not considered overtaking and the vehicle behind them must use the warning light.
* Emergency lanes: General lanes are not allowed to be used by general vehicles, except for fire engines, hospital ambulances, police vehicles, military police, military police, road maintenance vehicles that are on duty and vehicles that are damaged or have Traffic accident or emergency.
