Commentary: Can the United States Recover the Promise Lost for Eight Years?
The White House said in a statement that the US-Africa summit underscored the US commitment to deepening ties with Africa. The Joe Biden administration still plans to invest at least $ 55 billion in Africa over the next three years. But the three-day meeting ended in disagreement.
After eight years, the Joe Biden government's commitment to Africa is in doubt, as $ 55 billion in investment has been allocated to about 50 African countries, which will not be implemented in just three years. However, this investment will be included in the budget in 2023 and implemented in 2024, while at the same time will face the problem of whether the Republican-controlled House of Representatives can approve the budget or not.
Speaking of Africa today, the most needed thing is the real and honest help of big countries. The United States should respect Africa, do practical work for Africa, to impress the African people with America's sincerity, as well as gain the trust of Africa through practice.
