It should be informed that the Angkor Sankranti event was authorized by the Royal Government of Cambodia to be held for the first time in 2013 in the Angkor area of Siem Reap province to celebrate the Khmer New Year. However, this Angkor Sankranti event has been suspended from 2018 until now.
However, on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the third national sports event in 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, decided to re-organize the Angkor Sankranti event in 2023, on the occasion of the Khmer New Year.
As planned, this Angkor Sankranti 2023 event has 6 entertainment venues with 44 programs, with a presentation of Cambodian products for 4 days from the morning of April 13 to 16 and the opening ceremony This Angkor Sankranti 2023 event is presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
