Ministry of Environment opens forum on protection and conservation of natural resources under the theme "Diversification of businesses to increase local economy"
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, on December 20 opened a forum on the protection and conservation of natural resources under the theme "Diversification of businesses to increase the local economy."
The event was attended by the Secretary of State of the relevant ministries and institutions, the leadership of the Ministry of Environment, the leaders of the Community Network Committee, the Community Committee of the 25 Capital-Provincial Departments of Environment, the sub-national administration and many other partner organizations.
On that occasion, Mr. Say Sam Al said that today's forum is very important and also a place for dialogue between communities with the Ministry of Environment as well as the Royal Government, which can work closely together to orient where we should go. Be clear.
At the same time, he encouraged the community to continue to grow crops, raise animals, plant trees to ensure the economy, food security for families and communities.
He emphasized that the peace, political stability we are enjoying is a golden opportunity to build a family and community economy. All of these factors have allowed Cambodia to have more of its own protected areas and make Cambodia more environmentally conscious. Conservation areas are a pillar for supporting the economy, society, culture, especially community life.
It should be noted that the organization of the forum on the protection and conservation of natural resources under the theme "Diversification of businesses to increase the local economy" is a mechanism to continue to examine the progress of participation of local communities and stakeholders in the protection and conservation of biodiversity. And address challenges and set directions for participatory and sustainable management and use of natural resources in protected areas.
The forum serves a number of main purposes, including:
* First, review the progress of participation in the management and use of natural resources in protected areas and discuss challenges.
* Second: Share knowledge, information and experience in promoting local community economy, livelihood options, independent of natural resources.
* Third: Promote ownership and provide opportunities for communities as well as stakeholders at the sub-national level to participate in the management and sustainable use of natural resources, set common goals to continue to manage and utilize natural resources and promote business diversification. Innovative and friendly to conservation.
