Mr. Oknha Pech Bolen made the remarks at the 2022 Outstanding Entrepreneur Awards Ceremony organized by the Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association on the night of December 19, 2022 with the participation of Mr. Heng Sokong, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Industry. Science, Technology and Innovation Mrs. Srou Narya, President of the Cambodian Youth Congress, International Businessmen and Entrepreneurs.
"Most of the start-ups start with a passion but no business skills, sometimes some entrepreneurs have skills but are still vague, which is why we have the Best Entrepreneur Award," said Pech Bolen. (CYEA) to allow Sakrin to participate in gaining knowledge, including a lot of training.
"I would like to advise all entrepreneurs that when starting a business, it is necessary to have knowledge, skills, start-ups, start a business, not only look at the Cambodian market, but also look at the ASEAN market as a whole before starting a business," he said. "Something to consider in terms of impact, profitability and risk factors in the future for at least five years."
He continued that for today, young Cambodian entrepreneurs, together with the President of the International Congress of Young Entrepreneurs of Cambodia, organized an award ceremony for the best entrepreneurs in 2022, with the participation of many entrepreneurs. This program is designed to encourage good entrepreneurs to measure their ability to know if their business meets any of the business model standards.
Mr. Heng Sok Kong praised the 2022 Outstanding Entrepreneur Awards. He said that through this program, Cambodia has many outstanding entrepreneurs and has contributed significantly to addressing entrepreneurial competition in society, the country and the region.
He added that, therefore, would like to encourage the creation of more activism for the Cambodian Young Entrepreneur Award to create prestige for the nation.
Ms. Srounarya said that the 2022 Best Entrepreneur Awards can go on until the finals, despite many obstacles after a two-season hiatus due to the 19 crisis.
"I would like to continue to encourage our winners to make more efforts to continue competing in international forums as indicators to strengthen and expand their business, as well as to guide Cambodia to regional markets in the immediate environment," she said. "The economy of living in a new way."
Please be informed that the Cambodian Young Entrepreneur Awards Program organizes awards ceremonies for the 5 Best Entrepreneurs and 9 Final Entrepreneurs.
The Cambodian Young Entrepreneur Awards program was first organized in 2015 under the auspices of the Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association and the Cambodian Young International Chamber of Commerce, with the support of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, the Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Women's Affairs. Director of National Children's Hospital asks Korean MPs to speed up $ 16 million new 5-storey building project
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Nhep Angka Bos, Director of the National Children's Hospital and Advisor to the Ministry of Health, requested the Member of Parliament of the Republic of Korea to accelerate the construction of a new five-storey building worth $ 16 million so that the hospital can open its services. Treat more new diseases to children.
The request was made on the afternoon of December 19, 2022, when a parliamentary delegation from the Republic of Korea, led by Mr. Ee Ying-yeon, Head of the Korean Parliamentary Alliance for Children, People and Environment, inspected the achievements. Korea provided to Cambodia, especially at the National Children's Hospital.
According to the hospital director, the new five-storey building with an area of more than 9,000 square meters in the National Children's Hospital is scheduled to start construction at the end of 2023 and be completed by the end of 2026 at a cost of about 16 Millions of dollars, including the construction of buildings, training, medical equipment and equipment for patients.
He added that this is the second building that the Korean government has helped build for the National Children's Hospital, while the first three-story building, built in 2007, is called the Cambodia-Korea Friendship Building and will open in 2029. Then, due to the growing demand of the hospital, Korea renovated and expanded in 2013 and opened in 2016.
He added that the hospital also received assistance from Korean organizations in organizing training for doctors from various provinces in the field of infant care and rehabilitation.
He added that the Korean support is very important to contribute to improving the quality of services of the National Children's Hospital with a clear definition of special diseases such as ear, nose, throat, eye, kidney, cancer. Blood, lungs, stomach, intestines, like the elderly, which is scheduled to open in the near future, while in the past, the hospital treated general pediatricians without any specialization in children.
