"Japan is causing a serious security crisis on the Korean Peninsula and in Asia," a spokesman for the North Korean Foreign Ministry said in a statement released by KCNA on Tuesday. "The East through the adoption of a new security strategy that recognizes the ability to carry out preventive attacks against other countries."
The spokesman added that the security environment in the region has changed dramatically due to Japan's new policy, which violates the UN Charter and poses a serious challenge to international peace, and that North Korea has the right to take military action. Strictly aimed at protecting its fundamental rights as well as responding to the complex security environment in the region.
