Senior officials of the Ministry of Public Works meet with Kampong Thom provincial administration officials to strengthen waste management efficiency
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Ros Vanna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, said that he convened a meeting with the leadership of Kampong Thom Provincial Administration, Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport to hand over the sub-project for the construction of a landfill in Stung Sen City and introduced the work to strengthen Effectiveness of waste management.
In a meeting held at the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kampong Thom province on the afternoon of December 19, 2022, Mr. Ros Vanna said that the garbage problem is very important that the provincial authorities must pay attention to manage it effectively because If not managed properly, it will have an impact on the environment and the permanent health of the people, which is the highest risk to their health.
The Secretary of State continued that the new landfill is a standardized and well-maintained landfill, large space and needs to recruit staff with clear management skills, so the Kampong Thom Provincial Administration must take into account Human resources need to be trained in effective management.
In the past, garbage collection has been difficult because some people did not participate and some did not understand the impact of littering on their health. Therefore, the Royal Government as well as the Kampong Thom Provincial Administration have made efforts to manage this waste effectively and prioritize what kind of waste can be reused.
He added that the landfill is that we have received loans from development partners that require conditions, and these conditions are a condition that provides benefits and robust development to the project owner, focusing on: 1. Construction site 2 Environment (impact on people's livelihood) 3. People's well-being 4. Benefits 5. Long-term sustainability
He also urged the Kampong Thom provincial administration, in cooperation with the Department of Public Works and Transport, to carefully consider other landfills located in cities / districts, including landfills and wastewater treatment plants, because if Authorities do not have a clear plan, everyone will have a hard time choosing a suitable location.
Mr. Ros Vanna stated that Samdech Techo Prime Minister has agreed and approved the inclusion of garbage and dirty water into the water bill, which requires people to pay permanently, meaning that in the bill there is a service fee for garbage, clean water and dirty water, but The Ministry demands to explain to them the reasons that affect serious health factors and short life expectancy.
