Mr. Steng Sokhom: Peace, democracy, rule of law are the foundation of sustainable development in all areas
(Prey Veng): Mr. Steng Sokhom, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Working Group of the Local Party in Kamchay Mear District, Prey Veng Province, stated that peace, democracy and the rule of law are the foundation of sustainable development in all areas. He stressed that these foundations are enshrined in the national constitution and also in the policy of the Cambodian People's Party from the beginning.
Mr. Steng Sokhom made the remarks while chairing a meeting to disseminate the decision on the joint plan for the 7th National Assembly election of 2023 in Kamchay Mear district, which will take place in July 2023.
The ceremony was held at the CPP headquarters in Kamchay Mear district on December 18, 2022, with the participation of the district party working group, the chairperson-vice-chair of the eight commune party working group, the district party committee, the branch chairman. Village Party, District Youth Working Group, District Party Women's Movement Working Group, total 226 members.
Speaking to the Kamchay Mear District Local Party Working Group, Mr. Steng Sokhom said, "Peace, democracy, the rule of law are the foundation of all-round and sustainable development that is related to the policies of the Cambodian People's Party and "Obviously in today's society."
Mr. Steng Sokhom also explained the consequences of the war, citing the example of the Khmer Republic and the Khmer Rouge regime, showing that because the wars of those two regimes did not build anything, the war destroyed all the achievements. In the society almost completely and has caused difficulties for people, there are deaths, injuries, disabilities and family breakdown. People live in fear, have no time to do business, their children are not educated.
He stressed that war can not create anything new, so if the country is at war, all the national budget will turn to war, there is no budget for nation building. Thus, war is the enemy of peace, war is the enemy and development in all fields, war is the enemy and development of human resources, war is the enemy and Buddhism.
Mr. Steng Sokhom drew the attention of the participants that with the increasing number of members for us is not enough, we need good quality members. The party has set its goal of "one party member is the one vote for the party." That is why the party adheres to the efforts to retain the old members who are the core strength of the party and maintain it with the utmost care, we want a member who has a real body and heart.
Mr. Steung Sokhom continued that we, the party leaders at the grassroots level, we are the activists of the party, we are all committed to achieving new achievements and achievements for the party, especially through the results of the upcoming election, because we have enough time. From now on, to act towards the 7th legislative election to be absolutely successful.
