The Ukrainian Air Force claims that its air defense system shot down about 30 Russian drones in the latest round of attacks, while authorities in Kiev claim that about 18 of the 23 drones were shot down. In the sky of the city with a population of 3.6 million.
Kiev Governor Oleksiy Kuleba, who includes Kiev and surrounding areas, said Monday that Russia's drone strike had caused "considerable damage" and that some areas had been cut off from power supplies. There were no immediate reports of injuries or severe damage.
On Friday last week, Russia fired a total of more than 70 missiles on several areas of Ukraine, including the capital Kiev, while a few days earlier on Wednesday, Moscow forces launched a drone strike on Russia. The same city of Kiev where there were more than 10 drones at that time. Russia has been carrying out drone and missile strikes on Ukraine since October.
Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates continue to negotiate the second round of Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates have resumed the second round of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (CEPA) negotiations, which both sides expect after the entry into force of this agreement to boost the export of priority goods to meet demand. Each other.
The second round of negotiations for the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates (CEPA) was held for three days from December 19 to 21 at the Sofitel Phnom Penh, chaired by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce. Karma.
Cambodian Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak says this is the first time that Cambodia has reached a free trade agreement with countries in the Middle East, having only previously been in Asia because the United Arab Emirates is a partner. Cambodia's leader for the Middle East.
He noted that the United Arab Emirates is being touted as a potential market for Cambodia's exports in the future due to its high income, which is about 42,880 US dollars per person per year. And when the CEPA enters into force, the two sides expect the trade volume between the two countries to reach $ 1 billion in the next five years.
The Minister of Commerce stated that the CEPA is a complementary agreement between the United Arab Emirates, which has food needs, while Cambodia has energy needs, ie all exports and imports. Instead of competing, they meet each other's needs, while the United Arab Emirates is one of the world's major oil and fuel exporters and Cambodia has a food surplus.
He expects that priority goods in exports, including textiles such as footwear, clothing, bicycles, travel products, agricultural products, etc., will be exempted or taxed. At the same time, Cambodia will consider importing goods from the United Arab Emirates, such as automotive lubricants, rubber, fertilizers and animal feed, to meet domestic demand.
He said that in the future, the country will invest in food processing in Cambodia to be more standardized and competitive to export, not only to the United Arab Emirates, but also to Europe and Africa. Also.
Juma Mohammed AI Kait, Deputy Minister for International Trade of the United Arab Emirates, said that the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates will increase trade volume between the two countries. On existing growth. The working group of both sides will continue to make further efforts towards achieving the expected formal conclusion of negotiations.
"Cambodia is an important supplier of food products, and the United Arab Emirates sees that in addition to importing goods, UAE investors will also set up industrial plants in the future," he said. In the future, the UAE business group also plans to visit Cambodia and implement the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between the two countries.
It should be informed that the trade volume between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates in 2021 was worth about 279 million US dollars, an increase of 40%, which is still low because Cambodia has not yet reached an agreement and mutual investment. President of the Cambodia-China Friendship Association: Sino-Cambodian cooperation improves the lives of Cambodians
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ek Sam Ol, President of the Cambodia-China Friendship Association, said that through cooperation between China and Cambodia, improve the lives of Cambodians.
Mr. Ek Sam Ol made this remark on the occasion that he and Duke Tong Chamroeun, President of the Jiangsu Chinese Entrepreneurs Association in Cambodia, were invited to the Spring Festival 2023 on the evening of December 18, 2022 at the Huangshan Hotel. Phnom Penh. The program is organized by the Jiangsu Chinese Entrepreneurs Association in Cambodia and the Jiangsu Chinese People's Friendship Association in Cambodia, with the participation of government officials and other stakeholders.
Ek Sam Ol stated that the Cambodian-Chinese friendly relations would not have been possible without the trust and support of all and from all walks of life in Chinese society. He said that Cambodia-China cooperation is closely linked to the development of both Cambodia and China.
On that occasion, Mr. Ek Sam Ol continued that under the Belt and Road Initiative, we are working together to build a platform of connectivity, financial support and cooperation, all these joint efforts have contributed to the growth. In our country and development across the region.
"I have no doubt that our cooperation will drive growth in both Cambodia and China and improve the lives of our people," he said. We warmly welcome Chinese business and work with us to expand our investment and increase your cooperation in Cambodia. ”
In addition, Mr. Ek Sam Ol added that through the relationship between Cambodia and China will continue to improve the economy, improve the well-being of the people, maintain social cohesion and promote free trade. He believes that these national priorities will create further impetus for our cooperation in the fields of economy and investment, financial connectivity, innovation and social governance.
Zhang Yong, Executive Director of the Jiangsu General Chamber of Commerce, said: "In Cambodia, we have always taken the Chamber of Commerce as our core, keeping warm together and fighting for ways to survive under the pressure of the 19 epidemics of Kovid. Significant changes in the economic environment. Many of our Chamber of Commerce colleagues have persevered and achieved great results.
He also firmly believes that under the proper guidance of the Chairman of the Board and the joint efforts of all colleagues in the Chamber of Commerce, we will continue to create new conditions for the development of the Chamber of Commerce and make new updates for the Chamber of Commerce. Karma. Promoting Sino-Cambodian friendship for regional economic development and social stability.
