(Kampong Chhnang): The Autumn Festival is a public event of the Autumn Festival in Cambodia, in line with the time when Cambodians all over the country have been harvesting rice, punching, flying kites and celebrating the new season in the villages. Districts. This festival is the second year that the Eng Foundation has organized and sponsored the Dal Ambok program.
Separately, this year, the Foundation organized an Autumn Festival event, including the Dok Ambok ceremony, the launch of the Khmer kite and all kinds of kites, as well as local traditional performances, folk dances, chapei dong veng, bassac, khaol, ayai, and concerts. Folk games and many other mixed art forms are also organized with the cooperation of the Department of Culture and Fine Arts of Kampong Chhnang Province and technical support by fireworks.
Please note that both nights also have the display of 2023 lanterns and a lot of fireworks, and also has a long chapei concert, bassac performances, regional theater, Khon dance, Ayay dance, popular dance games. Concerts featuring many celebrities and circus performances, Cambodian Circus, Fa and Fa Ponleu Selpak Association and many other events.
