The MF Foundation has a mission to promote the rich culture, traditions and customs of the Khmer people, the soul of the nation, and to improve the lives of the people in Kampong Leng district and the people around this area who will benefit. Directly from the conservation and protection of eco-tourism in the area of the Foundation.
In addition to promoting Cambodian culture and traditions, the Eng Foundation has focused on a number of other social activities, including capacity building for local students in Kampong Leng, support for Buddhism, participation in environmental protection, forest protection and wildlife presence, and Biodiversity and participation in local development such as roads, water and sanitation.
Looking at the opportunity to train the human resource nursery during this great event, Duke Ing Bun Hou organized the recruitment of 150 students from Kampong Leng High School as volunteers to facilitate the Autumn Festival. Trained by fireball, a company with rich experience in organizing traditional arts and culture events that we all know is "Bon Phum".
Through this training, all students will gain both knowledge, skills and experience to prepare a good standard program, which is part of the development of hard and soft skills for them. This is also an opportunity for all young people to start thinking about their future careers well.
