(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sok Hay, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, on December 19, 2022, attended a meeting to review the provisional results of the completion of the 2022 voter list and voter registration at the Provincial Election Secretariat. Kampong Thom.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Chea Pum, Director of the Secretariat of the National Election Commission of Kampong Thom, representatives of municipal administrations, representatives of relevant departments around the province, as well as the working group of the National Election Commission at the district level.
Mr. Chea Pum stated that the examination of the 2022 voter list and registration will last for 50 days, from October 20 to December 8, 2022, starting at the commune hall, then mobile. Go to the villages according to the actual commune / sangkat calendar and end at the commune / sangkat hall and close for 3 days for meetings with stakeholders from November 3, November 18 and December 2.
Mr. Chea Pum said that the initial voter list and voter list will be removed from the commune / sangkat voter list and posted in the commune on January 13, 2023 and the official voter list will be announced on the 21st. February 2023.
During the meeting, Mr. Sok Hay raised three points:
First, January 13, 2023 is the closing of the first voter list, requesting all relevant authorities to verify in detail whether the list of people in their jurisdiction is correct or not? If there are any irregularities, they must cooperate and correct them in time because the National Election Commission will close the official list on February 21, 2023.
Second, all relevant authorities must maintain security and order to the people by maintaining safety.
Thirdly, all stakeholders must cooperate to disseminate to the people to check the list and register to vote for everyone, especially the municipal authorities to encourage commune authorities to cooperate and coordinate the work of representatives. Political parties to avoid criticism of some inactive activities caused by local officials.
Mr. Sok Hay requested all stakeholders to cooperate in all aspects to make the process of reviewing the voter list and voter registration smooth, free, fair and acceptable.
