This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Receives Lifetime Achievement Award of the World's Greatest Leader
(Phnom Penh): On Monday morning, December 19, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, received the "Lifetime Achievement Award of the World's Greatest Leader" award.
The awarding ceremony of the Lifetime Achievement Award of the Outstanding Leader will be held at the Peace Palace. The World Leaders' Lifetime Achievement Award is presented by the Asia-Pacific Strategic Institute (KSI).
KSI Institute is based in Malaysia. The institute is an independent, non-profit organization and a link between government, business and civil society to turn initiatives into influential results. The main goal of the Institute is to build better countries across the Asia-Pacific region.
KSI is the leading organizer of influential and innovative conferences and forums, with the participation of more than 3,000 policy makers, business leaders and NGO leaders through more than 60 high-level events. Since the end of 2018. KSI is currently the Secretary for the prestigious Economic Club of Kuala Lumpur, the ASEAN Economic Community (AEC) and the Rakyat Dialogue Forum.
The institute regularly evaluates and awards leadership awards to national leaders, business people, and civil society organizations for their achievements.
The decision to award the "Lifetime Achievement Achievement of the World's Greatest Leader" to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, was made after the Institute has studied and evaluated in detail the leadership qualities and achievements. From the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The Institute recognizes the ingenuity, wisdom and conscience of the nation and its people, and has worked tirelessly to bring peace, tranquility, progress and prosperity to the nation and the nation of Cambodia.
In addition to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the KSI Institute has also awarded the "Lifetime Achievement Achievement of the World's Best Leaders" to former leaders of ASEAN member countries and leaders of some Asian countries.
Please note that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as the longest leader in Cambodia, has brought many achievements for the nation and the people. The achievements of Samdech Techo's leadership to put an end to the fires of war, bring peace, national unity and promote national development to rise from the status of a poor country have been recognized in Country and international.
All those achievements led to Samdech Techo to receive the following honors, awards and medals as follows:
Seeing the great efforts and voluntary contribution to the cause of national unity, peace and socio-economic development, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was conferred the title of "Samdech" on February 1, 1994.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen received a degree in political science from a Cambodian higher education institution and a doctorate in political science from the National Academy of Politics in Hanoi in 1991.
In 1995, Samdech Techo Hun Sen received an Honorary Doctorate in Political Science from the University of Southern California for his major, and in 1996 an Honorary Doctorate in Law from the University of Wesleyan, Iowa. ) Of the United States.
On November 15, 2001, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was awarded an Honorary Doctorate in Political Science in International Relations from Ramkhamhaeng University of the Kingdom of Thailand.
On August 6, 2002, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was awarded the full position of a full member of the Academy of Natural Sciences of the Russian Federation and awarded a medal in recognition of his leadership in Make Cambodia peaceful, stable and develop socially and economically.
On September 04, 2002, the Committee of the ASEAN Federation of Engineers decided to award Samdech Techo Hun Sen his first and highest honorary title, "Honorary Engineer" in recognition of his national conscience and leadership ability. End the civil war, rehabilitate and develop in all areas of the society and open the possibility for national engineering intellectuals to participate in the national construction and development movement.
July 08, 2004 Recognizing the Contributions and Achievements Achieved in Protecting, Building and Developing Cambodia, Together with Leadership, Demonstrating Knowledge of Advanced Political Science, Reform in All Sectors, Especially in Education At the higher education level and the maintenance of national reconciliation, stability and regional integration, the University of Cambodia decided to award Samdech Techo Hun Sen an honorary doctorate degree in political science.
On September 15, 2004, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was recognized as a member of the Cambodian Bar Association.
On March 21, 2006, during an official visit to the Republic of Korea, Soon Chun Hyang University in Seoul presented Samdech Techo Hun Sen with an honorary doctorate in Political Science and Philosophy to highlight the country's leadership, reconstruction and development. Dedicate all your energy to peace and prosperity for Cambodia and Southeast Asia, especially to pay attention to enhancing friendly relations with the Republic of Korea.
January 29, 2007 Referred to the valuable contribution to the social and economic development of Cambodia, which led to the rapid and multifaceted development of the Ministry of Education and Training of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, together with the National University Hanoi presents Samdech Techo Hun Sen with honorary doctorate in education
On November 25, 2008, in Vientiane, Lao People's Democratic Republic, President Choummaly Sayasone presented the Lao National Gold Medal to Samdech Techo Hun Sen in recognition of his efforts to improve relations, create favorable conditions, as well as develop the economy, society and culture between the two countries. Laos and Cambodia.
January 07, 2009 in Phnom Penh, Recognizing and Appreciating the Substantial Contribution to the Improvement of Economic Cooperation between the Republic of Korea and the Kingdom of Cambodia, Woosuk University Higher Education Committee Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen holds an honorary doctorate in economics.
On October 15, 2015, accompanied by an official visit to the People's Republic of China, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was awarded an honorary doctorate degree in literature by Guangxi University for the Nation in recognition of his outstanding leadership skills. To unite the country and build strong relations between China and Cambodia.
March 29, 2016 By universally recognizing the work of the cause of peace building, restoration and development of Cambodia from zero to progress as it is today, especially the opening of freedom of the press, both online and on television, the federation ASEAN media presented Samdech Techo Hun Sen with the "Peace and Development" award.
On December 09, 2017, the European Council for Tourism and Trade nominated Samdech Techo Hun Sen as "World Goodwill Ambassador for Tourism and Sustainable Development Goals" in recognition of the leadership Peace to the nation and attract the growth of tourism. In the same event, Phnom Penh was named the "Capital of World Culture and Tourism".
On March 19, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen became the first world leader to receive an honorary doctorate degree in "Political Relations" through the decision of the Krirk University Council of Thailand on December 24. 2018 with the assessment that Samdech Techo is a leader full of knowledge and ability to use political relations to achieve many achievements for Cambodia.
On December 15, 2021, the envoy of the President of the Russian Federation presented a Medal of Friendship from the Russian Government to Samdech Techo Hun Sen in return for his contribution and important role in maintaining and strengthening relations between the people of Russia and Cambodia.
On February 12, 2022, in Seoul, South Korea, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was selected as the winner of the 2022 Sun Hak Peace Prize by the Sun Hak Peace Prize Committee in recognition of his achievements in ending the war. Civil and building a full and lasting peace in Cambodia.
On August 05, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was awarded an honorary doctorate degree in "Development" by the Royal University of Phnom Penh. Samdech Techo Hun Sen became the first national figure to be awarded a degree by the university.
