(Phnom Penh): The Royal School of Administration, which is the staff of the Ministry of Public Function, has started to organize the 10th recruitment exam for Kramakar students of the Royal School of Administration to select only 120 final candidates for the first round of Kramakar training. Year 2023 at the Royal School of Administration.
On the afternoon of December 18, 2022, the 10th recruitment of Kramakar students of the Royal School of Administration, the first subject began at 1:30 at the examination center of the Royal University of Law and Economics, including 2,520 candidates from all over the country participated in the 10th Kramakar Student Selection Exam. Mr. Youk Bunna, Representative of Minister Prum Sokha, also invited the judging ceremony for the candidates.
Mr. Youk Bunna advised all candidates to show all their knowledge to the best of their ability and for candidates who pass the exam in the first stage to be prepared and further strengthen their ability to compete in the second stage. In particular, for candidates who fail the exam, do not despair, make an effort to learn more about the lack of their knowledge to be ready to participate in the exam next year.
In front of the candidates, Mr. Youk Bunna claimed that the current exam was conducted in accordance with the basic principles of the Royal School of Administration to be transparent, fair and quality, so the candidates with real knowledge and ability are only candidates. Only those who have passed the first writing test will be allowed to take the second writing test.
It should be noted that in the first phase of the exam, out of 2,520 candidates, only 240 were eliminated to advance to the second stage. The second phase of the 240 candidates will be reduced to 120 for the one-year training in 2023 at the Royal School of Administration.
