(Phnom Penh): The South China Sea Buddhism Roundtable 2022 held in Phnom Penh went smoothly and ended successfully. The meeting was held on December 15, 2022, with the participation and participation of monks and Buddhist leaders from 18 countries.
Mr. Chhit Sokhun, Minister of Cult and Religion, praised Venerable In Sun for his courage and long-term vision in initiating and establishing the South China Sea Buddhist Roundtable, and received strong response and support from Many Buddhist countries successfully complete the South China Sea Roundtable on the Phnom Penh Forum.
Mr. Wang Winthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, congratulated the success of the South China Sea Buddhist Roundtable on the Phnom Penh Forum. He said the meeting was held for seven consecutive years under the theme "New Hope, New Vision, Together to Build a New Future", not only to continue and develop the spirit of the previous mandate meeting. That, in turn, responds to modern voices today.
He highlighted the good relations between China and Cambodia, and the Buddhist Roundtable reflected the close friendship between the two countries, with the Chinese side choosing Cambodia as the first foreign country to host the event. This meeting. He believes that this forum will help promote better cultural relations between the two countries.
He added that 2023 is the 65th anniversary of Cambodia-China diplomatic relations and also the year of Cambodia-China friendship. He hoped that the Cambodian-Chinese Buddhist sector would move forward, increase cultural activities in the Buddhist field to another level, strengthen the friendly relations between the people of the two countries to contribute to building peace and progress in the world. He will build a single destiny for mankind.
At the same time, Mr. Ek Sam Ol, President of the Cambodia-China Friendship Association, said that the friendship between Cambodia and China is stronger than steel, not only becomes a model for the international community on trust and development cooperation, it is also a great asset. The two countries have good cultural relations, making people and people close to each other.
He commended Venerable In Sun for his significant contribution to the promotion and development of culture, education and philanthropy in Cambodia, and hoped that 2023, the 65th anniversary of Cambodia-China diplomatic relations, the Roundtable Will play an important role in promoting the people of the two countries to better understand each other, learn from each other's civilizations and continue to play a more important role for both countries.
Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Tep Vong and Samdech Preah Abhisiri Sokunthea Moha Sang Reachathipat Bour Kri expressed their congratulations and appreciation for the successful South China Sea Buddhist Roundtable on the Phnom Penh Forum, emphasizing that the meeting This will definitely improve the relationship between Buddhists from all walks of life.
Venerable In Sun has highlighted his sentiments with Cambodia and the Cambodian people over the years. The Phnom Penh Forum is a new development in South China Sea Buddhism, opening a new page in the history of Buddhist relations in civil society, and we will continue to strengthen and expand the development of Buddhism.
To promote Cambodian-Chinese Buddhist relations and to build a common destiny of the South China Sea, he made the following four recommendations:
* First: Continue to strengthen one destiny as a successor to promote the sincere Cambodian-Chinese traditional friendship * Second: Continue to strengthen one destiny as a protector of peace and strong South Sea development * Third: Continue Strengthen One Destiny as an Initiator of the Powerful South Sea Civilization Study * Fourth: Continue to Strengthen One Destiny as a Model Leader of the South Sea Roundtable.
At the roundtable, monks and Buddhist representatives from Mongolia, Myanmar, Thailand, Japan, Nepal, Britain, Sri Lanka, South Korea, the United States, Laos, Indonesia, Malaysia, Europe, Taiwan and Hong Kong, China were present. Also participated in comments both in person and through video clips. The Roundtable also signed a joint statement on the "Phnom Penh Forum Initiative of the South Sea Buddhist Roundtable".
Kratie Branch of Cambodian Red Cross Celebrates World AIDS Day on December 1
(Kratie): Ms. Heng Nary Vathorn, Chairperson of Kratie Provincial Outstanding Elite Working Group, on December 17, 2022, led the celebration of World AIDS Day on December 1, 2022 under the theme "Equality". Visiting and distributing gifts to 60 families living with HIV and the disabled at the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Chhlong district.
Each family of 60 people living with HIV and people with disabilities received 1 box of noodles, 1 fishing rod, 1 blanket, 1 scarf, 4 T-shirts and 40,000 Riels.
Moreover, discrimination in society has been reduced and eliminated almost completely, while now this vicious disease is being controlled and controlled by human beings by various means, and it has become an effective means for Victims are able to adapt to live in the community as well as other people.
She is very confident in the slogan "Make Equality" based on the leadership of His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, combined with other driving forces such as the Ministry of Health, the Red Cross, various organizations and other stakeholders. Most importantly, people involved in the disease need to take care of their health and strictly follow their doctor's prescriptions.
She also urged all people to stay healthy and join the fight against the deadly Kovid-19 disease and to join the Royal Government in implementing health measures to continue to adapt and learn to live in a new way.
On the same day, Ms. Heng Nary Vathorn continued to visit the homes of two other disabled people in Bos Leav commune, Chit Borei district, a woman who was a former leader of the Red Cross volunteers, who had chronic high blood pressure for many years. And another grandmother has been suffering from spina bifida for many years. Each of them received a blanket, a scarf, 4 T-shirts and the budget of the branch and philanthropists more than 200,000 riels.
