Mr. You Sereyvuth and Mr. Phen Phalla Meet and Have Solidarity with Journalists
(Phnom Penh): Mr. You Serey Vuth, Special Task Force of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, and Mr. Phen Phalla, Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, met with about 200 journalists.
In a meeting and a solidarity dinner on the night of December 17, 2022, Mr. You Serey Vuth thanked the journalists for their hard work in covering events in Cambodian society.
For You Sereyvuth, journalists have played a very important role as a mirror of reality in society and also a mirror to improve the provision of better public services. More importantly, the press plays an important role in maintaining security and social order, avoiding any corrupt movements that want to cause social unrest or want to destroy peace.
Mr. You Serey Vuth encouraged all journalists to continue their efforts to do their job based on integrity, publish the truth with professional ethics, in accordance with the recommendations of Samdech Techo "Do not violate the rights of others, do not distort the truth."
Mr. You Serey Vuth also encouraged journalists to unite against fake news and corrupt information by reproducing the reality of Cambodia in order to maintain security, order and peace in Cambodian society. New house donated by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to veterans in Baray district
(Kampong Thom): A new house donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, President of the Cambodian Veterans Association and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen was handed over to a retired veteran in Samrong village, Baray commune, Baray district, Kampong Thom province.
The handing over of the house was made by Major General Som Sun, Commander of the Military Operations Area and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province on the afternoon of December 17, 2022.
Lt. Gen. Som Sun confirmed that Lt. Gen. Son Sob, a former Baray District Police Inspector from 1981 to 1989, was the Kampong Thom Provincial Police Commissioner from 1990 to 1994 and was later transferred to the Ministry of Interior. Retirement area as determined.
He said that Major General Son Sap had a wife and five children in his care, as he had health problems and could not work outside the regime set by his superiors, so he was not able to build a suitable shelter on his own land. He has.
Seeing this difficulty, the working group of the Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province asked for the decision to build a new house 232, which was a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to build it on the ground. Cast iron in and around the house, smart walls, galvanized roof.
During the handover ceremony, Lt. Gen. Som Sun brought the gifts of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet and Mrs. Pech Chanmony and gave him 200 kg of rice, 5 boxes of noodles, 3 boxes of fruit juice, 2 boxes of fish sauce and fish sauce. 5 cans of soy sauce, 2 cases of pure water and some money.
Mr. Son Sob and his family expressed their gratitude and best wishes to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as Mr. Hun Manet and Mrs., including the Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province.
