Inauguration of the pavilion and achievements in Wat Tang Krasang North, Po Sen Chey district worth more than 170,000 USD, Mr. Keut Chhe: Peace has led to the continuous development of Cambodia, both empire and Buddhism
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, on December 17, 2022, said that the factors of peace have led to the continuous development of Cambodia, both empire and Buddhism, which all people are happy and wish for. Everyone.
Mr. Keut Chhe said this on the occasion of representing Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh at the inauguration ceremony of the pavilion and achievements in Wat Tang Krasang North in Sangkat Kakap II, Khan Por Sen Chey, presided over by Mr. Kittisangkhab Dr. Tep Ngon, Second Vice President Representing Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate.
He said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has provided the Cambodian people with peace, stability, national unity, democracy and openness in religious practice, making Buddhists in Phnom Penh and the provinces live in harmony, and the achievement of physical infrastructure, pagodas and temples. Places of worship have been erected all over the country.
He said that the achievements that were built in the northern Krasang pagoda now are the result of "peace and development of the motherland" under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen through the great power. The unity of the Royal Government, local authorities, monks, grandmothers, grandfathers, Buddhists, pagodas, people, as well as philanthropists, both inside and outside the country, to support the promotion of Buddhism.
"Peace" is a fundamental and invaluable factor, and if our country is not peaceful, there is no national unity and no development, then the achievements of physical infrastructure, pagodas and places of worship all over the country, really, "he said. Can not build as many sequences as today.
On that occasion, the Honorary Doctor Tep Ngorn said that the progress of the empire and the Buddha should be proud of ensuring harmony between all religions in Cambodia and without discrimination and religious conflict. In particular, the steady growth in the field of Buddhism, the state religion, was born out of the clear and fervent beliefs of Cambodian Buddhists throughout the country and abroad.
He said that the development of Buddhism is an important contribution to socio-economic development through education, human resource development and has played an important role in promoting the preservation of culture, peace, solidarity and friendship, which is a great way to lead. To achieve the social goal is to eliminate violence, hostility, crime and other evils.
It should be noted that the achievements to be inaugurated now are a new hut with a size of 12 meters by 14 meters on the ground floor, which was buried on November 28, 2019 and completed. It was completed on March 18, 2021 by purchasing 28 marble statues as a shrine at a total cost of $ 173,614.
