(Phnom Penh): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, called on the people to learn and remember the win-win policy, a policy that brings Cambodia away from the flames of war. Of national unification and development as it is today.
With the end of the war in 1998, it was time for Cambodia to find peace, rediscover national unity and territorial integrity after the fall of the Angkorian Empire, which lasted at least 500 years.
By 2022, it has been 24 years since Cambodia was completely peaceful and provided an opportunity for Cambodia to build and develop its national economy, raising Cambodia from a poor country to a low-middle-income country.
General Ith Sarath emphasized that the progress, prosperity and prosperity of the Cambodian nation was due to win-win politics. For General Ith Sarath, peace is the greatest achievement of win-win politics.
Win-win politics has the greatest merit for the nation and the people of Cambodia. In order for the win-win political spirit to bring peace and continue to lay a solid foundation in Cambodian society, General Ith Sarath called on the Cambodian people to make an effort to understand this politics. The general also called on the Cambodian people to be grateful to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the founder of win-win politics, as well as other operators.
On December 29, 2022, the Royal Government will celebrate the win-win political anniversary at the Win-Win Political Palace.
The general confirmed that 4,688 people attended the celebration of this historic day. In total, 272 national and international guests, 7 monks, armed forces, including 19 scouts, equal to 2,315 people, youth plans from the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, 894 Red Cross scouts, 1 population plan, 200 people.
The event also featured 19 booths on the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces' win-win political practice. Among them, there are 12 booths under the Ministry of National Defense and 7 booths of the Commander-in-Chief, and fireworks were fired at night.
It should also be noted that in order to celebrate the win-win political day in January 2022, the Royal Government of Cambodia has issued a circular to designate the win-win political day on December 29 in the annual calendar without a break.
In that circular, the Royal Government instructed all ministries, institutions, capitals, provinces and private public institutions to prepare banners and slogans to celebrate the win-win political day with the message, "Thank you, peace!" Thank you, win-win politics! "Thank you to the founders, guides and political operators, win-win that brings peace and complete national unity!" Driving, do not violate the speed limit! 1 killed, 9 injured in road accidents nationwide on December 16
