Editor-in-Chief: Samdech Techo Hun Sen joins forces against opportunists to take refuge under the banner of the press to preserve the values and dignity of the media (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Recommended 5 points to be the basis for study and prepare the direction for implementation, the main point is that Samdech Techo to unite against the opportunists take refuge under the label of the press.
In a message sent to the 19th Editorial Press Conference of the Cambodian Press on December 17, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, Take refuge under the label of the press to maintain the values and dignity of the media.
The 19th Press Editors' Forum was attended by nearly 100 editors, editors-in-chief, associations and media leaders from 60 institutions, leading to the adoption of the Joint Statement on "Strengthening the Code of Ethics for Journalism in Cambodia".
According to the same message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also recommended the training of journalists in both professional and digital media technology so that journalists in Cambodia can keep up with the development of modern media today. Samdech Techo also called to join the fight against false information and not to be a distributor of false information that pollutes society, which causes the country to fall into chaos and lose social order.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen to continue to promote measures to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 more actively and advise people to get vaccinated Kovid 19 for everyone. Samdech Techo also recommended to promote the journey to the 32nd SEA Games 2023, which Cambodia hosts widely and deeply to all levels of the public.
In a message sent to the 19th Editorial Forum of the Press of Cambodia on December 17, 2022, which was received by Fresh News, Samdech Techo Hun Sen claimed that through this participation, the Royal Government has been given the opportunity to open the country. It will be put into operation in all areas that make the Cambodian economy work well.
In addition to the opportunity to reopen the country, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the prevention of the spread of the 19 Kovid disease has made it possible for Cambodia to host the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and The 40-41 ASEAN Summit and the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Meeting (AIPA) were a great success, furthering Cambodia's prestige on the international stage.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, this great and historic achievement shows the cooperation and partnership between the Royal Government of Cambodia and other institutions and journalists who have overcome all obstacles to report and share. Extensive and up-to-date information to the people, despite the fact that our media has been affected economically by the global political crisis as well as the crisis of the Kovid 19 epidemic.
1. Strengthen the code of ethics and professional practice and oppose opportunists under the label of the press to maintain the values and dignity of the media.
2: Train journalists in both professional and digital media technology so that journalists in Cambodia have the ability to keep up with the development of modern media today.
3. Participate in the fight against false information and do not be a distributor of fake information that pollutes society, causing the country to fall into chaos and lose social order.
4: Continue to disseminate measures to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 more actively and advise people to get vaccinated Kovid 19 for everyone.
5: Disseminate the journey towards the 32nd SEA Games 2023, which Cambodia hosts widely and deeply to all levels of the masses.
