(Ratanakkiri): The owner of a rubber plantation based in Kanang village, Ting Chak commune, Bor Keo district, Ratanakkiri province, expressed his happiness after the price of rubber increased more than before, before the Royal Government of Cambodia did not allow the export of rubber. And unprocessed rubber abroad.
Mr. Hy Kim Heang, the owner of a 5-hectare rubber plantation in Ti Chak commune, claimed that when the Royal Government did not revoke the circular on rubber and unprocessed rubber trees abroad, the price per kilogram was between 1,700 and 1,800 riel, but now the price of rubber is not. Processed 1 kg between 2150 to 2200 Riel (traders buy from plantations).
He pointed out that in his area of about 5 hectares, he used 15 workers and divided the percentage is 700 riel per kilogram. If the price of unprocessed rubber is more expensive, the workers may go up a little more, which will lead to a better life for both the plantation owners and the workers.
At the same time, he also asked other rubber plantation owners not to take advantage of brokers, such as embedding soil, embedding heavy stones in rubber, because it damages the quality of rubber, damages the reputation of plantation owners in Ratanakkiri. It is a province that grows rubber and agro-industry. He also expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for revoking the above-mentioned traffic.
However, with the increase in prices, he also received complaints from brokers who seemed unhappy with the authorities stationed at the international ports that they owed a lot of unofficial fees, which led to lower rubber prices. No fee.
