(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kao Kosal, Director General of the General Department of Trade Promotion of the Ministry of Commerce, on December 16, 2022, urged all producers and exporters to improve the quality and strengthen product services for consumers. Have confidence in Khmer products.
This promotion was made on the occasion of Mr. Kao Kosal's participation in the workshop on "Improving the quality of Cambodian products and services to boost exports" organized by the Department of Market Development, General Department of Trade Promotion of the Ministry of Commerce this morning. December 16, 2022.
The workshop on "Improving the quality of Cambodian products and services to boost exports" was attended by about 100 inter-ministerial officials, representatives of companies, enterprises and supermarkets at the Cambodiana Hotel in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Kao Kosal stated, "All producers and exporters need to improve the quality and service of Cambodian products with high quality, proper packaging, selling at a reasonable price to be able to promote the export of Cambodian products to foreign markets." Country.
In addition, Mr. Kao Kosal said that the main purpose of this workshop is to inspire the masses, especially the Cambodian people to turn to support the use of more Cambodian products.
According to the Director General of the General Department of Trade Promotion, this seminar is accompanied by the 15th Cambodian Products and Import-Export Fair for Cambodians to see and know more about Cambodian products.
Heng Chak, Deputy Director of the Market Development Department, said that the Ministry of Commerce has been developing policies and strategies to negotiate market access in order to obtain free trade agreements with eight major countries and regions around the world, including: China, South Korea, Japan, Britain, US, India, Mongolia and the Eurasian Economic Union (EAEU).
According to the Deputy Director of the Department of Market Development, the Eurasian Economic Union has five other members: Armenia, Belarus, Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan and the Russian Federation.
He emphasized that the exhibition of Cambodian products and export-import goods was held in order to promote widely both nationally and internationally in promoting trade activities, creating market opportunities, presenting the business environment, and investment potential, as well as protection policies. Of the Royal Government to the private sector.
International exhibitors include China, the United States, India, Japan, Italy, South Korea, Turkey, Singapore, Vietnam, Laos, Indonesia, the Kingdom of Thailand, and the Islamic Republic of Pakistan. Products on display at the fair include:
* Agricultural products, vegetables, fruits and agro-processing * Food and beverage products * Vehicles, machinery and warehousing equipment * Silk and souvenirs * Books and reading products * Jewelry and precious stones * and other by-products Others such as cosmetics, office supplies, investment projects, handicraft products and general consumer goods.
The exhibition runs for four days from December 15-18, 2022, with a total of 268 booths, including booths from foreign embassies in Cambodia, booths from the capital-province, Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, Rice Federation, NGOs. Business associations of local and foreign enterprises with a total of 181 enterprises.
