2. Retired Veteran Ly Bunjer, Male, 65 years old, joined the army in 1987. The 5th Army Defense Brigade received the back of house 231 in Chhouk Beong village, Chhouk commune, Prasat Sambo district, Kampong Thom province.
Lt. Gen. Som Sun added that seeing that their two families were living in poverty and could not afford to build a decent house on their own, the committee of the Kampong Thom Veterans Association asked for a decision to build a house. Samdech Techo's precious gift to him now, which is the back of the 230th and 231st houses, built high above the ground, concrete pillars, steel bones, planks, boards, smart walls, corrugated iron roofs and stair treads.
During the handover ceremony, Lt. Gen. Som Sun brought the gifts of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet and Mrs. Pech Chanmony to give to each family: 50 kg of rice, 2 boxes of noodles, 2 boxes of fish sauce and soy sauce. Carriers and kitchen utensils, as well as some budget.
Veterans and their families would like to express our deepest gratitude and best wishes to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as Mr. HUN Manet and Ms. Hun Sen and the Committee of the Kampong Thom Cambodian Veterans Association. Tea and the five blessings of the Buddha, do not forget.
