US inflation slows in November, easing consumer sentiment
On a monthly basis, the consumer price index also fell sharply. Commodity prices rose 0.1 percent in November, down from 0.4 percent in October.
ABC News reported that the biggest contributors to the monthly price increase included accommodation costs, which rose 0.6 percent in November. Food prices also jumped 0.5 percent in November. But prices have fallen for a wide range of goods, including gasoline, used cars and trucks, and medical services.
"In a world where inflation is rising to double digits, in many major economies around the world, inflation is declining in the United States," he said. If I am not mistaken, prices are still very high. We have a lot of work to do. "But things are getting better, moving in the right direction."
The slowdown comes after a sharp rate hike by the US Federal Reserve in a bid to bring commodity prices back to normal. According to ABC News.
