Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth: Cambodia is actively working to achieve its vision of becoming a high middle income country
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, said that Cambodia is actively working to achieve the vision of transforming Cambodia into a high-middle-income country by 2030 and become As a high-income country in line with the development path that set out the vision of Cambodia 2050.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth said, "Cambodia is actively working to achieve the policy framework, economy, trade and sustainable development goals to move towards achieving the vision to become Cambodia. "As a high middle income country by 2030 and become a high income country in line with the development path set out the vision of Cambodia 2050."
He stressed that Cambodia still needs official development financing support from development partners to Cambodia, including the United Kingdom, and continued trade and investment cooperation from the United Kingdom.
The Deputy Prime Minister emphasized that faster adaptation to new trends in the aftermath of the Kovid 19 crisis has become a priority for socio-economic development. In this context, Cambodia is implementing the strategic framework and programs to restore and promote Cambodia's economic growth in living with Kovid 19 in the new normal path for 2021-2023.
There are three pillars: rehabilitation, reform and resilience. In order to have a sustainable and resilient economy, of course, Cambodia needs to strengthen trade links, promote digitalization, mobilize domestic financing for socio-economic development, and encourage private sector investment. Accelerate green development.
At the same time, Cambodia has been implementing a primary policy framework on the development of securities, which will include considerations for the development of climate change-responsive financial instruments.
The Ambassador commended and commended the Royal Government of Cambodia for its excellent results in curbing the spread of Kovid 19 and the rapid resumption of socio-economic activities.
The Ambassador thanked Cambodia for supporting and assisting the United Kingdom to become an ASEAN dialogue partner, and the United Kingdom will continue to strengthen cooperation and deepen relations, especially the strengthening of trade relations between the two countries.
