Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen "Kolthida Humanitarian"
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, His Excellency Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, is highly regarded by the Cambodian people and world leaders as a Cambodian nobleman who has acted Enthusiastic about humanitarian causes and a supreme symbol of rescuing all victims in Cambodia, regardless of race or color.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit has also been named as a midwife in society, like the world-famous leader "Socrates" and even as a midwife like "Socrates".
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen was born from a family of farmers in Village 2, Roka Khnor Commune, Krouch Chhmar District, Kampong Cham Province on December 15, 1954. There is a father named Lin Kry (deceased) and a mother named Bun Seangly (deceased), 6 siblings, 2 sisters. As of December 15, 2022, Samdech Kittipritthbandit, Mother of Humanity of Cambodia, has reached the age of 69.
On this birthday, the King, Queen, Cambodian officials at all levels, including the Cambodian people, expressed their wishes that show the deepest affection and love.
In the advanced age of Khmer youth in the rural areas along the Mekong River, at a time when the motherland of Cambodia is facing a crisis of war, it is consumed with hardship and does not have the opportunity to sit and absorb knowledge as high as the youth in the local era. No peace today. Bun Rany graduated from high school only.
At a time when the country was falling into chaos, Bun Rany joined the resistance movement at the age of 16. The resistance movement began after the famous head of state during the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, was overthrown by a coup d'état by Lon Nol and Prince Sisowath Sirimatak on the 18th. March 1970
The physical and mental effort of the Bun Rany Khmer National Liberation Movement, along with tens of thousands of other Khmer lovers and patriots, has fallen into despair as the achievements of the struggle have been overshadowed by a group of individuals like Paul. Pot Nuon Cheang, Khieu Samphan, Ieng Sary, Ieng Thirith ... instead.
The Democratic Kampuchea regime has re-suffered young Bun Rany and millions of Cambodians in the dark and miserable veil of darkness. However, the life of Bun Rany during the Pol Pot regime is like meeting the "light in the dark days". "Light in the Dark Ages" Because the life of young Bun Rany is difficult, but this regime is also the time that led this young woman to meet the man of her heart, young Hun Sen.
But the group marriage (13 pairs) of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen on January 5, 1976 during the genocidal regime of Pol Pot left an indescribable bitterness. The weight of the pain and suffering is endless: the loss of her husband, who went out to fight for national liberation in 1977, and her unborn child. To be safe, life and children from a vicious regime must endure, hide their names and hide their history.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen once stated that the love life of Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, the Supreme Wife, swam through hardships and millions of tears, and never imagined that there is life until now.
After Pol Pot's 3-year, 8-month and 20-day black-shirt regime was overthrown by the National Salvation Front, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen took part in a great campaign to save and restore Cambodia from the ashes. His Excellency Samdech Techo Hun Sen through humanitarian activities and education.
During the inauguration ceremony of the "Honorary Doctorate" from the Royal Academy of Cambodia on July 25, 2011, Samdech Kittipritthbandit highlighted the many achievements that are the achievements of the efforts to serve the people and the beloved country to Respond to humanitarian activities, the improvement of living standards, social welfare, the protection of dignity and the promotion of human values.
In the book "Bun Rany, the wife of the strong man of Cambodia" by Mr. Chhay Sophal, Samdech Kittipritthbandit said, "In my whole life, I have nurtured my heart since I was young, that is to help the general life to get rid of Adversity. "Especially to help the poor, the disabled, the victims of natural disasters, fires, orphans and patients."
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany became the First Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross for the first mandate (1994-1998) and became the President of the Cambodian Red Cross for the second, third, fourth and fifth mandates from 1998. To the present.
Not only Cambodians, even people in countries around the world who suffer from natural disasters such as hurricanes, floods or earthquakes, etc., Samdech Kittipritthbandit has always contributed to save the nation to the victims. Those accidents, too.
Overall, at the age of 67 (December 15, 1954 - December 15, 2020), Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen made great sacrifices to save the Cambodian people in times of hardship.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit is an exemplary wife, an exemplary mother, an exemplary grandmother of all Cambodian women and an outstanding descendant in Cambodian society, speaking separately and as a rare person in the world, because Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen is a midwife. Relieve social hardships like the world-famous leader "Socrates" and even a midwife like Socrates' mother.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit has also been named one of the most outstanding women in the history of Cambodia, including Princess Liu Yi, Princess Indratevi and Queen Sisowath Kosomak Nearyrath.
Through this humanitarian mission to save humanity, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen has received honorary titles and medals from national and world institutions, including:
* 2: Medal for the Promotion of a Unique Heart of the World from the Sri Mai International Peace Center, December 22, 2001.
* 3: Medal of Her Majesty Queen Sisowath Monivong Kosomak Neary Rath, Class Mahasreywat, presented by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk on October 19, 2001.
* 4: Monisaraphon Medal, Maha Sereyvath Class, presented by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni on January 23, 2005.
* 6: Medal of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Moha Sereyvath Class, presented by His Majesty King Samdech Preah Boromneath Norodom Sihamoni on November 19, 2007.
* 7: The medal was presented by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni on November 20, 2007.
* 8: Honorary Doctorate in Humanities from the University of Cambodia on October 16, 2008.
* 9: Honorary Doctorate in Economics from Seoul Women's University, Republic of Korea, June 3, 2009.
* 10: Honorary Doctorate in Literature from Jiunju University, Republic of Korea, July 6, 2009.
* 11: Awarded the Asia-Pacific Leadership Award for HIV / AIDS and Development from the United Nations High Commissioner for AIDS and AIDS on 17 November 2009.
* 12: Honorary Doctorate in Education from Seila University, Republic of Korea, April 1, 2010.
* 14: Received the title of Samdech Kittipritthbandit from the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni on May 8, 2013.
