(Phnom Penh): The United Nations and the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training have pledged to strengthen cooperation with each other to achieve further progress on strengthening cooperation in the field of labor and vocational training.
This statement was made during a courtesy call and discussion between Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Mr. Joseph Scheuer, the new United Nations Resident Coordinator in Cambodia on the morning of 15 December. 2022 at the Ministry of Labor.
At the same time, he also congratulated the Cambodian government for well-prepared measures to prevent Kovid-19, which has led to the return of most major projects.
Mr. Joseph Scheuer stated that the United Nations will continue to support the Royal Government of Cambodia's ambitious goal of transforming Cambodia into a high middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2050. The nation will continue to establish a framework for cooperation with the Cambodian government for 2024-2028, making Cambodia-UN a stronger partner.
The Minister will work together with the United Nations to make the Youth Employment and Employment Appropriations Program in Cambodia (DEY) a model project for other countries to implement as Cambodia succeeds in implementing more factory projects. Better in Cambodia (BFC).
The two sides are committed to promoting cooperation in all fields, and in the field of employment and vocational training will support all priority programs of the Ministry. The two sides share a common vision for achieving the 2030 Sustainable Development Goals, and the Royal Government of Cambodia achieves the goal of transforming Cambodia from a low-middle-income country to a high-middle-income country. 2030 and become a high-income country by 2050.
