Senior official of the Ministry of Education: Student health is an important issue that the Ministry of Education and the leadership of the Royal Government pay close attention
(Battambang): Ms. Khun Rachana, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, stated that the health problems of students caused by the use of drugs, alcohol and drugs are important issues that the leadership of the Ministry of Education as well as the leadership of The Royal Government pays great attention to the development of human resources that are healthy and intelligent, have a good attitude and have good morals for society.
At the same time, Ms. Khun Rachana also stated that the participation of students in the study will gain more knowledge related to alcohol will enable all students to adapt and control themselves to stay away from alcohol and drugs. Addiction is the cause of health effects.
Ms. Khun Rachana, on behalf of the Ministry of Education, also called on all students to be useful and socially needed, without trying to use alcohol and drugs to help themselves, help their families and society.
At the same time, many students have argued that restricting alcohol advertising is an effective measure to reduce the dangers posed by current alcohol use. This karma has attracted young people who are the source of bamboo shoots to start using alcohol, which is a drug that leads to more harm to health.
Ms. Khuon Sodary, Representative of Samdech Kittipritthbandit, Receives 19 Doses of Kovid Vaccine Donated by the Chinese National Red Cross Society
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Kitti Sangkhab Dr. Khuon Sodary, Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross, High Representative of Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, on the afternoon of December 15, 2022, received the 199 Kovid vaccine. (Sinopharm), a grant from the Chinese National Red Cross Society to the Cambodian Red Cross 300,000 doses.
Please be informed that during August 2021, the Chinese National Red Cross Society also provided 100,000 doses of Kovid 19 vaccine to the Cambodian Red Cross. The vaccine is an important reference in the fight against Kovid 19 and protects the lives of people from this global epidemic.
From 1998 to the present, cooperation between the Cambodian Red Cross and the Chinese National Red Cross Society has been strengthened through the exchange of leadership visits, the signing of bilateral cooperation agreements in stages, the provision of humanitarian aid in Disasters during the Kovid phase and the implementation of community resilience health projects, including:
According to Dr. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, on December 15, 2022, the vaccine for Kovid 19 was a total of 74.5 million doses (the remaining 2023 is 20.5 million doses). In the warehouse of the Ministry of Health, the remaining 6.3 million doses are injected daily.
