First, the Cambodian people are no longer at risk of injury and loss of life due to landmines, which are known as hidden killers. Second, some areas that are threatened by the presence of landmines and unexploded ordnance are Become a safe area and an area where people can grow crops and develop.
The definition for the phrase "Cambodia is mine-free" was presented by Dr. Hun Manet during the proclamation of Tbong Khmum province as a mine-free province on the morning of December 15, 2022.
On that occasion, Dr. Hun Manet, the popular Prime Ministerial candidate, highlighted the suffering of the people due to landmines and unexploded ordnance, which are the remnants of war. He also outlined the clear goals and plans of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to make Cambodia a landmine-free country by 2025 by releasing a national budget package for demining and unexploded ordnance operations.
It should be noted that due to the war torn apart since the late 1960s, Cambodia has been turned into a minefield and buried millions of unexploded ordnance. After overthrowing the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and finding internal unity with the help of friendly countries, Cambodia began clearing mines and unexploded ordnance left over from the war in 1992. By 2022, it will be 30 years.
For the past 30 years, in the joint mine action mission of the Royal Government of Cambodia, donors, development partners, national and international operators, and all stakeholders have made significant contributions to addressing the impact of landmines and explosive remnants of war in Cambodia.
For more than 30 years, the Royal Government has provided more than 200 million US dollars to participate in mine action in Cambodia, as well as support the institutional process and monitor the implementation of the National Strategic Plan.
The case of a foreigner who hijacked a taxi in Chhep district, Preah Vihear province is a fiction, the owner of the taxi confessed and apologized to the authorities for causing confusion
(Preah Vihear): The case of two foreigners hijacking a taxi in Cheb district, Preah Vihear province while traveling to Stung Treng province, which caused a surprise on the afternoon of December 15, 2022, is a fiction that Made by the car owner himself, while the car was sold to pay off his brother's debt and did not want the family to find out.
Oeun Song, who initially claimed to be the victim of a robbery caused by two foreigners who rented his car from Siem Reap to Stung Treng, was robbed in Cheb district, Preah Vihear province. Apologized in front of the authorities for fabricating the information, causing surprise and confusion from the public.
Mr. Oeun Sang confirmed to the police that the car he had invented was stolen and that he had sold it in Siem Reap this morning to pay off his debts. After the sale, he boarded a taxi from Siem Reap province to Stung Treng province. The car itself.
Colonel Chhour Madi, police inspector of Cheb district, Preah Vihear province, told Fresh News that after the interrogation and confession, the authorities made an education contract and called the family to come and bail them out before they were allowed to return home. Back.
Immediately after receiving this information, the specialized police force under the direct command of Major General Sous Sok Dara, Preah Vihear Provincial Police Commissioner, conducted an urgent search to find out that the victim fabricated the information.
