Minister Ith Sam Heng Introduces Modernization of ASEAN Labor Inspection through Information Technology
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, recommended that the ASEAN Labor Inspection Commission and ASEAN institutions use information technology effectively to modernize the labor inspection system in order to improve the implementation of laws and regulations. Involved in the labor sector in the ASEAN region more effectively.
He said this on the occasion of the opening of the 11th ASEAN Labor Inspection Conference under the theme: Modernization of Labor Inspection through the post-pandemic technological revolution on the morning of December 15, 2022 at the Ministry of Labor. From the ASEAN Labor Inspectorate, the ASEAN Occupational Safety and Health, the ASEAN Secretariat and the ASEAN Partners through the video system.
The 11th ASEAN Labor Inspection Conference aims not only to share experiences and practices of the ASEAN Labor Inspection System, but also to discuss innovations, challenges and strategies towards the use of ICTs in Labor inspection system as well.
To make the conference a success, the Minister made the following recommendations:
First. The ASEAN Labor Inspection Commission and the ASEAN Institutions should consider additional possibilities for the establishment of mechanisms to monitor and evaluate the implementation of the conclusions and recommendations made by previous conferences, and encourage Member States to propose consistent projects / activities. As stated in this recommendation and mobilize the participation of external partners outside ASEAN.
Second. ASEAN should expand cooperation between ASEAN Member States and ASEAN dialogue / development partners to share their experiences and successes in the field of labor inspection, especially with countries using advanced technology to optimize their national labor inspection systems in Forms such as study tours, workshops / sharing forums and so on.
Third. The ASEAN Labor Inspection Commission should disseminate information, training and awareness of technology in the field of labor inspection and the provision of public services to workers in ASEAN countries.
Chinese man arrested in Sihanoukville in connection with illegal weapons use and drug possession
(Sihanoukville): A Chinese national was arrested by the Sihanoukville police force and sent to the provincial court in connection with a case of illegal possession and use of weapons and possession of drugs. The arrest was made during an open administrative operation at a villa building located in Group 9, Village 1, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, which is suspected of kidnapping.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Chuon Narin said on December 15, 2022 that this operation took place on December 11, 2022 by the specialized force of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police in cooperation with Sangkat Administration Police Force. 3 and with the coordination of the procedure by Mr. Penh Piseth, Deputy Prosecutor of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court and under the guidance of Mr. Min Kompheak, Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province.
According to the General Commissioner, during the administration visit, it was found that there were foreign people sitting working with computers in the common room and in the private room, suspected to be involved in committing any crime. In fact, a total of 26 Chinese and Vietnamese and 4 Cambodians and some other materials were found.
During the operation, when the team went to the location of the building above, one of the suspects, YI XIAO LONG, jumped over the back fence, escaped into the forest, and was chased by the police and brought to the suspect. A search of the suspect's room turned up two handguns and some items.
Currently, the light criminal police office has built a case related to the case of illegal possession and use of firearms and cases of illegal possession and storage of drugs and sent the suspect to the provincial court for legal punishment.
