(Phnom Penh): Thousands of bottles of Dutchmill milk, which was smuggled in by infringing on intellectual property and damaged, were cracked down on by the Economic Crime Police Department of the National Police.
The authorities confirmed that the operation on December 14, 2022 was based on the complaint of UNT Holsell Co., Ltd. and with the participation of local authorities and company representatives under the direct coordination of Mr. Say Nora. Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
After inspecting that all dairy products were not transported and stored at the specified temperature, which may damage the quality and violate the exclusive distribution rights of UNT, so the Deputy Prosecutor decided. Confiscate all exhibits and temporarily store them at the department and require the site owner to come to the Economic Crimes Police Department for questioning to continue the procedure.
NEC Meeting to Review and Decide on the Implementation of Social Security Regulations on Pensions and Procedures for Retirement of Civil Servants
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) held a meeting on the morning of December 15, 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC to review and decide on the instructions. Procedures for the implementation of the social security system on pensions and procedures for the retirement of civil servants of the National Election Committee (NEC).
According to the content of this instruction, the NEC shall apply only for retirement by reaching the retirement age (60 years), early retirement by the voluntary consent of the officials of the National Election Committee (NEC). (NEC) with a seniority of 30 years or more and retirement with loss of professional qualifications only.
The Social Security Pension Unit for Civil Servants of the National Election Committee (NEC) shall regularly review and update the status of each retiree every six years. Once a month.
The absence of an extradition treaty is a major issue for Indonesia, as Jakarta has raised concerns about the difficulty of prosecuting those accused of embezzling large sums of money during the 1997 Asian financial crisis. 1998.
Under the treaty, signed by the leaders of the two countries in January this year, those who have committed 31 crimes will be able to be extradited and it will be effective for the crimes committed. Until 18 years ago. On the other hand, it means that perpetrators will not be able to escape the law by simply changing their nationality.
In addition, the extradition treaty will also support Indonesia's efforts to prevent criminal suspects from fleeing abroad and for them to be arrested within Indonesia itself. In fact, Jakarta has long sought to ratify such a bilateral treaty with Singapore.
Europe commends Cambodia's efforts and special envoy work to promote implementation of five-point agreement on Myanmar crisis
(Brussels, Belgium): The European Union (EU) commends Cambodia's efforts and the work of its special envoy to promote the implementation of the five-point agreement on the crisis in Myanmar.
This is according to a press release issued by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair on Myanmar, at the EU Political and Security Committee on Developments in Myanmar on the 14th. December 2022.
"The European Union commends Cambodia's efforts and the work of its Special Envoy to promote the Five-Point Agreement (5PC) and reaffirms its strong commitment to supporting the ASEAN Community," the statement said. "And ASEAN's leadership role in helping Myanmar return to democracy as soon as possible."
Meanwhile, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon emphasized that Cambodia, as the chair of ASEAN, expressed its gratitude to the European Union for its generous contribution to ASEAN in this important effort, especially in the field of humanitarian assistance in Myanmar.
The five-point agreement of ASEAN was unveiled at a special summit on April 24, 2021 in response to the political crisis in Myanmar. These five principles include:
First, the violence in Myanmar must be stopped immediately and all parties must increase their tolerance to the highest level.
Second, start a constructive dialogue among all stakeholders to find a peaceful solution for the benefit of the people.
Third, the Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair will facilitate the facilitation of the dialogue process with the assistance of the ASEAN Secretary-General.
Fifth, special envoys and delegations will visit Myanmar to meet with all stakeholders.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen Sends Condolences on the Death of Ms. Khun Sophal Svay Sitha
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, on December 15, 2022, sent a message of condolences on the death of Disciple Svay Yan, the biological mother of Ms. Khun Sophal Svay Sitha. Died at 07:48 in the morning on December 13, 2022 at the age of 92.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen considered that the death of Disciple Svay Yan was the loss of his mother, mother-in-law, great-grandmother, great-grandmother, and Brahma, who throughout his life always adhered to good morals, virtues, and strived to raise him. Nurture, nurture, educate, give good advice to children, grandchildren and families to become intellectuals, dignitaries, valuable human resources for society.
In addition, devotees have contributed to many achievements in contributing to the promotion of Buddhism in Cambodia. Samdech Kittipritthbandit and his colleagues, please dedicate your prayers for the soul of Disciple Svay Yan to go to his death.
At the same time, Ms. Khun Sophal Svay Sitha and her family expressed their deep gratitude to Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross for sending a message of condolence and 5 million Riels for the funeral.
Please be informed that the body of Disciple Svay Yan is being kept at 12, Street 313, corner of Street 546 in Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
