ADB approves $ 73 million loan and investment to support Cambodia's energy interaction program
(Phnom Penh): The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has approved a sectoral development program that includes $ 50 million in policy-based loans and $ 23 million in project investment to support Cambodia's energy interaction. This is according to the press release issued on December 15, 2022.
The Sectoral Development Program for Energy Interaction includes ADB's first comprehensive policy reform package for Cambodia's energy sector, which will be financed by a $ 40 million loan from ADB Concession Resources and 10 loans. Millions of dollars from the ASEAN Infrastructure Fund, part of the ASEAN Green Catalyst Finance (ACGF).
For the $ 23 million infrastructure investment, the Climate Investment Fund's Renewable Energy Enhancement Program for Cambodia will provide $ 6 million in loans and $ 5 million in climate financing, and the Green Climate Fund will add 12 loans. Million dollars through the Green Recovery Program of ASEAN Green Catalyst Finance. All funds will be managed by ADB.
This program supports the Royal Government of Cambodia's energy interaction agenda to increase renewable energy and energy efficiency and move away from fossil fuels. It develops planning and regulation using data for power systems to increase flexibility and resilience, and strengthens investment in new infrastructure for strategic planning, as well as introducing new technologies and business models.
The program is based on significant successes that demonstrate the transformation of active energy. The country's first solar-connected system was privately owned and financed by the ADB in 2016.
