Interior Ministry Spokesman: 60 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on December 14
(Phnom Penh): At least 60 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on December 14, 2022 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on December 15.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 60 suspects, 32 were arrested in 14 criminal cases and 28 were arrested in 14 drug cases.
(Phnom Penh): In the joint conference of the ASEAN-EU Anniversary Meeting and the 45th Anniversary of the ASEAN-EU Dialogue Partnership on December 14, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman ASEAN 2022 reaffirms Cambodia's position on the Russia-Ukraine war.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in our ASEAN, there is not the same position on the past UN resolutions, in which some countries voted in favor and some countries voted against.
"For Cambodia, we voted in favor of the UN resolution condemning the invasion or territorial seizure. In addition, as chair of ASEAN, we have also facilitated the issuance of relevant statements or dialogue," he said. "Ceasefire between Russia and Ukraine."
In relation to Ukraine, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also confirmed the sending of Cambodian technical officials, along with Japan, to assist Ukraine in demining training. "We also accept Ukrainian trainees this January to be deminers because it is dangerous and it is humanitarian, but we are not sending our troops to fight Russia in Ukraine," he said. "
The Ministry of Telecommunications explains to the students who just passed the exam about "Why should you choose to learn skills related to digital technology?"
(Phnom Penh): Students who have recently completed the Baccalaureate exam are considering choosing to study at a university while waiting for the results of their exam. Choosing a major in higher education must be considered thoroughly and carefully because a decision that affects the future of one's career.
Therefore, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has explained to students why they should choose skills related to digital technology?
According to the research, there are many reasons, including 5 main reasons that motivate students to choose to study skills related to digital technology as follows:
1: High salary and high demand in the labor market
2: Start your own business
In our country today, the number of people doing business in the field of digital technology is still small, so professionals in this field can strive to turn from professionals to business owners or startups through the provision of services. New, unique and easy to enter the market. Today, business opportunities in the digital technology sector are still plentiful compared to traditional businesses.
3: There are many scholarships
4: Many useful and interesting subjects
5: Participate in promoting the Cambodian economy to progress
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and chair of ASEAN in 2022, urged to accelerate the free trade agreement between ASEAN and Europe as soon as possible for the benefit of the two nations. "We should not put political issues in place to block free trade."
This was stated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Joint Conference of the ASEAN-EU Anniversary Meeting and the 45th Anniversary of the ASEAN-EU Dialogue Partners.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded of the strategic partnership between ASEAN and Europe, despite the distance between the two regions. In addition, Samdech expressed the intention of the leaders of the two regions to have a free trade agreement in the ASEAN-Europe Anniversary Meeting now.
"And what is the main purpose of our meeting is to find a free trade agreement between ASEAN and Europe, the two regions should do this as soon as possible." This is according to Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that ASEAN is not waiting for anything to be helped by Europe, but to complement each other between the two economies. ASEAN does not want our people to be poor forever and have to wait for help from Europe. Due to this, the two regions have initiated free trade agreements. Samdech Techo Hun Sen added, "We should not put political issues to block free trade."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled the words of the President of Indonesia at the opening ceremony of the meeting, saying that the partnership must be equal, can not take the law of one part to one part. "It is not possible to rely on the situation in Myanmar or any other country to interfere with the establishment of free trade between the two regions." This is according to the additional confirmation of Samdech Techo.
