(Brussels, Belgium): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, has asked EU businessmen and investors to target ASEAN member countries for their investment.
The Minister's request was made at the 10th ASEAN-EU Business Summit co-organized by the EU-ASEAN Business Council and major companies from the ASEAN and EU region in Brussels, Belgium on 13 March. December 2022.
During the meeting, the Minister said that ASEAN and the European Union have come a long way together to achieve the main objective of further strengthening and expanding relations between the two communities in all fields, especially trade and business. Modern, durable and environmentally friendly.
On that occasion, the Minister highlighted the important role of the private sector as a driving force in promoting the effective implementation of mechanisms set by the governments of regional countries.
In addition, Mr. Pan Sosak, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia and Chairman of the ASEAN Summit for 2022, called on all foreign businessmen and investors, especially European businessmen and investors, to select ASEAN as a potential investment destination to start or expand. Its business.
It should be noted that according to the data of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and the European Union in 2021 reached 4.18 billion US dollars. Of that, Cambodia's exports amounted to 3.22 billion US dollars and imports amounted to 0.95 billion US dollars. Compared to 2020, bilateral trade volume in 2021 will increase by 8.43%.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made the remarks at the opening ceremony of the ASEAN-EU Anniversary Summit to celebrate the 45th Anniversary of the ASEAN-EU Dialogue Partnership in Brussels, Belgium on the afternoon of the 14th. December 2022 in Brussels is the night of December 14 in Cambodia.
The summit was co-chaired by Charles Michel, President of the European Council, and Samdech Techo Hun Sen as ASEAN Chair. The summit is also attended by leaders of the European Union and other ASEAN member states. But there was no presence of the Myanmar leadership.
He noted the ASEAN-EU relations and cooperation, saying, "Our common spirit and aspiration for peace and prosperity in our two regions has led to the establishment of a successful strategic partnership with ASEAN." "With a clear and comprehensive action plan for 2023-2027 covering many areas of cooperation under the three pillars of ASEAN."
For the way forward, Samdech Techo Hun Sen believes that ASEAN and the European Union must work closely together to ensure international order based on the rule of law, openness, transparency and mutual benefit. Come on.
"As a two-party bloc based on the rule of law and accountability, ASEAN and the European Union must do their utmost to protect and promote the UN Charter and its laws, norms and principles," he said. "Recognized globally as the foundation for building peace, stability and improving the quality of life and livelihoods of our people in our region as well as the world."
Based on the experience of the protracted and tragic conflict in Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that peace cannot be achieved through war or the threat of war. In this regard, Samdech Techo proposed to determine the peaceful settlement of the conflict.
"I sincerely hope that we should define peaceful settlement of disputes through dialogue and consultation as our common approach." This is the request of Samdech Techo, the head of ASEAN.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed confidence that the discussions in this summit will allow the ASEAN-EU to change the common spirit to a pragmatic vision that will benefit the region and the world. For decades to come.
