LONDON, Dec. 14 (Xinhua) - At least three people have died after a boat carrying migrants sank off the country's southeast coast, government sources said on Wednesday. English. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, December 14, 2022.
After the British Coast Guard, the French navy and emergency helicopters went to the rescue, another 43 passengers were rescued.
The incident comes a day after British Prime Minister Rishi Sunak outlined a five-pronged strategy to combat illegal migration, including a new law banning migrants from staying in the country.
