Neak Oknha Kith Meng Requests International Barcode Institution to Support Cambodian Barcode Institution Technically and Technologically
The meeting focused on promoting barcode technology in Cambodia and exploring the possibility of expanding cooperation across ASEAN.
Renot de Babut briefed Duke Kith Meng on the strategic direction of Barcode Institutions around the world in promoting digital technology in the industry and helping to solve the supply chain.
He added that the Barcode Institute has been established and operated for more than 50 years. Currently, the main sectors that barcode technology is using are: retail, health, transportation, logistics and food.
Mr. Rinot stated that the priority points that the bar code institution focuses on are 1-data on companies, 2-barcode technology and 3-standards. In this regard, he was pleased to continue the good cooperation with Barcode Cambodia in promoting barcode standards and technology and requested Duke Kith Meng as Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council to examine the possibility of establishing cooperation throughout. ASEAN.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and President of the Barcode Institute of Cambodia, welcomed the cooperation with the International Barcode Institute on the promotion of barcode technology and invited Mr. Renot to visit Cambodia and organize a joint barcode event.
