(Koh Kong): Ms. Mithona Phuthong, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee in Koh Kong Province, together with the Kirisakor District Sub-Branch Committee in collaboration with the Provincial Health Department, participated in the celebration of World AIDS Day on December 1, 2022 under the theme "Make Equality" and Volunteer Day, December 5, 2022 under the theme "Unity through Volunteers".
In this ceremony, held on December 13, 2022 in Koh Sdach Commune, Kirisakor District, Koh Kong Province, Mrs. Mithona Phuthong read to the ceremony the message of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and dignitaries. National Outstanding Asia-Pacific Leadership Forum on HIV / AIDS.
At the same time, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen called on all Cambodians to join in implementing the Royal Government's strategic map to achieve the end of AIDS by 2025 and "equality" through key activities. As follows:
1: Let all compatriots, the private sector, national and international organizations join forces in the same national current, prevent communicable diseases to end HIV / AIDS by 2025 with equality in society.
2: Compatriots, especially young men and women, must regularly find out new knowledge on the prevention of HIV transmission and the spread of HIV to protect ourselves, our families, our community and our society.
3. Citizens who have committed or suspected the risk of HIV infection, should seek counseling services and blood tests for HIV by keeping confidential in public services, civil society services, private services, etc. To be able to decide to receive care and treatment in a timely manner
4: Pregnant women should seek care and check-ups at least 4 times and regularly according to the instructions of medical staff for maternal and child health, especially to help prevent the transmission of HIV and syphilis from mother to child. Baby
5: People should stop discriminating against people living with HIV and AIDS, which is against the law on the prevention and control of the spread of HIV and AIDS in Cambodia.
6: High-risk members, including men who have sex with men, transgender people and women who work in adult entertainment institutions, should continue to pay attention to the prevention of HIV and other infectious diseases, both now and in the future. . Meeting with Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Outgoing Japanese Ambassador affirms continued to support development in Cambodia
