In the first 11 months of this year, the General Department of Taxation collected more than 3,200 million USD, 14% more than planned
Confirmation of the increase in tax revenue was made during the meeting to summarize the results of tax collection in November and for the first 11 months of 2022, as well as the direction for further implementation, organized online (Zoom Meeting) under the chairmanship of Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation.
He said that the state of the Cambodian economy was going through a difficult period and affected by the Kovid-19 crisis, which has not yet fully resolved, geopolitical tensions between the great powers, the recent crisis of the war between Russia and Ukraine. Still, the state of inflation has also affected tax revenue management.
The General Department of Taxation must continue to strengthen the management of tax revenue collection by examining the feasibility and potential of revenue sources, and at the same time examine the possibility of reducing unnecessary and controllable expenditures and promote the implementation of work through Use technology to further transform the tax administration into E-Administration.
The General Department of Taxation will continue to promote the rights and obligations of taxpayers, especially those related to audit cases, in order to strengthen the provision of services to taxpayers, reduce complaints and challenges from taxpayers.
The General Department of Taxation needs to further improve the efficiency of registration, which requires the participation of many stakeholders, which is very important and necessary, which requires thoroughness, clarity and comprehensiveness.
The General Department of Taxation has prepared rules and procedures for the management and collection of tax revenue in the field of commercial gambling (casino) and will continue to strengthen real estate inspections and update real estate information in order to strengthen the provision of services to the public. Property in the declaration and payment of annual property tax.
Minister Kong Vibol instructed taxpayer management units to promote and monitor tax registration for active but unregistered enterprises and to inspect or, if necessary, request cooperation with banking institutions for information. About financial transactions or income-expenditure situation to strengthen the management of the enterprise, request to suspend activities or stop activities permanently.
Please be informed that through the draft law on finance for administration in 2023, the General Department of Taxation is required to collect 3,571.70 million USD in internal tax revenue, an increase of 26.70% compared to the financial law plan. For the 2022 administration, which requires tax collection of $ 2,819.55 million).
