(Phnom Penh): A Korean company specializing in waste storage and recycling, as well as a waste, has joined hands with the Cambodian Ministry of Environment to carry out operations to collect and store garbage and waste, especially the recycling of waste and garbage for economic benefit.
A Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Ministry of Environment of Cambodia and Dehan Corporation to operate on the collection and storage of garbage and waste, as well as the recycling of waste and waste was held on December 13, 2022. Through this Memorandum, the Company will operate to plan for the most efficient disposal of household waste and reduce the environmental impact caused by humans.
Speaking to reporters after the signing of the memorandum, Mr. Tum Pen Vireakvitou, President of the Cambodian Civil Society Network and the facilitator of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Environment and the company, said that the signing of the memorandum was a company willing to help Cambodia. Dispose of and dispose of waste for economic gain.
He said the company and the Ministry of Environment will turn all the waste into state revenue and increase local employment, while the waste will no longer have an impact on the environment.
The company also intends to invite members of the Cambodian Civil Society Network (CCN) and environmental officials to promote and explain more about waste management in Cambodia so that people have a better understanding of the problem of waste and litter. In addition, the company will invite Ministry of Environment officials to visit Korea in the near future to gain experience related to waste and waste processing.
Please also note that this Memorandum is valid for two years from the time of signing. However, the MoU can be extended through a review between the two parties one month before the MoU expires.
