According to the source, the commune technical team inspected the project implementation process of Phearum Company and found that the drainage system was not in accordance with the technical standards of the contract. In the contract, a 123-meter-long temporary drain with 100 cross-sections will be installed at a bid price of 42 million riels. Lay the bottom with a drain.
Mr. Sumol, Governor of Romeas Hek District, said that according to the inspection of the technical team, the decision to install the sewer at the mouth of the canal was acceptable, requiring the excavation company to measure the level of the sewer at the mouth of the national road. 13 Laying sand, gravel, and then draining and laying bricks to prevent erosion is acceptable.
He added that in 2021, there are two projects: a 2,500-meter-long paved road with 120 million riels, which Phearum has already built in 2021. The 123-meter sewer project has just been implemented with a cost of 42 million riels. The district administration cooperates with the provincial procurement officials and the commune council to inspect the technical standards only if the contract is accepted.
