(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, has decided to implement new measures with Cintri Company to improve garbage collection in Kampong Cham City. This was stated by the provincial governor on the morning of December 13, 2022 at the 43rd Ordinary Meeting of the Provincial Council of the third mandate at Kampong Cham Provincial Hall.
Mr. Un Chanda said that in the past, there have always been suggestions from provincial councilors as well as residents in Kampong Cham about the slow collection of garbage in Cintri by Cintri, which affects the beauty in Cities and people's lives. Therefore, in order to improve the garbage collection, the provincial authorities have decided and conducted a six-month trial with Cintri to allow garbage collection in Kampong Cham.
At the same time, the provincial authority has given the right to another company to collect revenue from the people, handed over to the Kampong Cham municipal authority to pay the garbage fee with Cintri Company in kilos, which is 1 ton for $ 18, which is currently the price of the company and the authority. The city is negotiating.
The provincial governor further stated that the preparation of the new regime as above is aimed at improving the garbage collection in Kampong Cham province, as the cost of garbage collection is in kilograms, so Cintri needs Must collect a lot of garbage to get more income. The work has to be tested for 6 months, if Cintri is successful, the provincial authority will make a contract to give it back.
In other districts, Cintri is required to continue collecting garbage and collecting revenue on its own for the same six-month trial period.
