Dr. Hun Manet Presents Diplomas to 467 Winners of Dewey International University in Battambang
(Battambang): Dr. Hun Manet, Chairman of the Poor Student Scholarship Committee of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, presented diplomas to 467 winners of Dewey International University in Battambang Province.
The ceremony was held on the morning of December 13, 2022 at the meeting hall of the Happiness Center of Battambang City, with the participation of Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province, University Leaders, Authorities, Forces, Directors of Departments around the province, civil servants, parents. Many students also participated.
59 needy families receive donations from 3k battery shop owners and Has Bey Guesthouse
(Banteay Meanchey): 59 needy families from Sangkat Kampong Svay, Sangkat O'Ambel and Sangkat Preah Ponlea in Serey Sophorn City received donations from Mr. Dom Vandy and Mrs. Koy Savon, owners of 3k Battery Shop and Has Bey Guesthouse, Serey Sophorn City to share with And the Royal Government to help people who are struggling to solve daily problems.
The distribution was also presided over by Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, on the afternoon of December 12, 2022 at the new home of Mr. Dom Vandy, located in Khla Kon Chas Village, Sangkat Kampong Svay, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Expert: Nutrition is at the heart of the Sustainable Development Goals
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Samnang, Vice Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, Office of the Council of Ministers, said that nutrition is at the heart of the goal of sustainable development. If we invest $ 1 in nutrition, we will get back $ 16 for many positive outcomes of the Sustainable Development Goals, including social stability, higher education, gender equality and so on.
Mr. Chea Samnang made this remark during the opening of the seminar on food system that considers nutrition in Phnom Penh on December 13, 2022.
Workshop on Nutritional Conservation System, co-organized by the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, Office of the Council of Ministers, with the International Institute for Rural Rehabilitation (IIRR) in Cambodia, International Center for Tropical Agriculture (CIAT), Joint Nutrition Movement Discuss and discuss 4 points:
Mr. Chea Samnang pointed out that although the world is facing crises, including the global epidemic of Kovid 19, the climate change crisis and the Russia-Ukraine war, Cambodia has not shown any serious signs of serious food security.
It should be noted that the Council for the Rehabilitation of Agriculture and Rural Development, in its capacity of the Royal Government, has cooperated with the private sector development partners and relevant ministries and institutions to prepare a roadmap on the food system for sustainable development in Cambodia by 2030. Approved by the Royal Government in September 2021 and is a document that is in-depth and interconnected in the implementation of this roadmap is based on four priorities:
Mr. Chea Samnang also encouraged her participation in the workshop, emphasizing the importance and usefulness of ministries, institutions, relevant organizations that have the task of studying, researching, policy making, etc. And participate in discussions and share experiences and information in the process of eliminating all forms of malnutrition in Cambodia for national development through innovative thinking.
Mr. Chea Samnang believes that today's workshop will contribute to further promote the cooperation between ministries, institutions and all relevant organizations to contribute more effectively and comprehensively in the field of food systems. Consideration of nutrition in Cambodia aims to contribute to the socio-economic development of our country by building human capital to have the quality of physical, mental, intellectual and technical skills.
Tomorrow, the Ministry of Culture will hold a great cultural event in Angkor, Siem Reap to celebrate the 30th anniversary of the inclusion of the Angkor site as a World Heritage Site (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): On December 14, 2022, tomorrow, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts will organize a great cultural event in Angkor, Siem Reap, with the participation of 300 famous artists of all forms.
The event is organized to celebrate the 30th anniversary of the inclusion of the Angkor site as a World Heritage Site, as well as to commemorate the 12 Cambodian heritage sites inscribed on the World Heritage List. UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity and the Memory of the World.
The above event is to promote the cultural sector and contribute to the restoration of tourism in Angkor after the Kovid-19 crisis.
The program will be held on December 14, 2022 at the backyard of Angkor Wat at 5:00 pm under the chairmanship of Mrs. Katisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Senate Relations, National Assembly and Inspection. For organizing this cultural event, people can visit freely.
