ADB approves $ 62.9 million budget to support Cambodia in livestock sub-sector
(Phnom Penh): The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has approved a $ 62.9 million budget to help Cambodia improve food security and promote inclusive economic growth by improving health and value chains, as well as formal trade and investment. Livestock products. This is according to the press release of the Asian Development Bank, which was received by Fresh News on December 13, 2022.
The project will enhance the productivity and resilience of the livestock sub-sector by reducing the risk of transboundary diseases, animal diseases and resistance to pesticides, establishing animal health inspections and providing services to improve food safety and security. Promote sub-regional cooperation in the Greater Mekong Subregion.
The project will be financed by a $ 50 million loan from ADB concessional resources, a $ 12 million grant from the Asian Development Fund (ADF) and a $ 900,000 grant from the Climate Change Fund (CCF). The Asian Development Fund provides assistance to ADB member developing countries, and the Asian Development Fund aims to strengthen support for low-carbon development and climate resilience in developing member countries.
