This morning, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court will try three large-scale drug criminals.
(Phnom Penh): After three adjournings, on the morning of December 13, 2022, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court will open the trial of three large-scale drug traffickers.
According to the order to bring the accused No. 4226 dated 16 November 2022 of the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, it is stated that there are 3 accused in this case:
The defendants were charged with illegally transporting, storing and trafficking nearly 2 kilograms of methamphetamine and methamphetamine.
According to Article 40 of the Drug Control Law, defendants could face between 20 and 30 years in prison or life in prison.
It should be reminded that on the 5th and 6th of February, 2021, the specialized force (A8) of the Department of Anti-Drug Crime launched an operation to crack down on large-scale drug trafficking cases in 3 locations:
