In the first 11 months of this year, Cambodia exported more than $ 20 billion worth of goods to international markets
(Phnom Penh): In the first 11 years of 2022, Cambodia exported major goods to international markets worth more than 20 billion US dollars, an increase of 18.1%. This is according to the report of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia.
The United States is the main market for Cambodia's largest exports of more than $ 8 billion, followed by Vietnam, China, Germany, Japan, Canada, the United Kingdom, Thailand, Belgium, the Netherlands, Australia, Spain, France, India, Italy, South Korea, Mexico, Hong Kong, Taiwan, Malaysia and more.
In the past 11 months, Cambodia has exported more than $ 8 billion worth of garments, nearly $ 1.7 billion worth of machinery and equipment, more than $ 1 billion worth of natural grain, more than $ 1.5 billion worth of footwear and other goods, according to the General Department of Customs and Excise. Some more.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Deputy Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, said recently that due to the strength of the manufacturing sector, exports will boost Cambodia's economic growth to around 5%. This 2022 and about 6% in 2023, which is in line with the forecasts of major international financial institutions such as: IMF, WB, and ADB.
He said that at a time when the world is changing the structure of the economy and relocation of investment, the Royal Government of Cambodia has worked hard to seize this opportunity to attract foreign investors to invest in Cambodia to produce exports. Periodic logical infrastructure reform, training of human resources in the field of digital power, investment climate and investment law.
