Angkor Math Competition is the largest national math competition with more than 5,000 candidates from 25 capitals and provinces and more than 300 schools, both public and private. Angkor Mathematics Competition is a platform for mathematics competition, providing opportunities for students to measure their mathematical ability, improve their science education, and improve their education.
The exam is divided into 5 levels: Level 5-6, Level 7-8, Level 9-10 and Level 11-12. The competition is conducted in three stages, with students being selected in succession. The final round will be held on Sunday morning, December 11 at the Institute of Technology of Cambodia called Techno. The finals were attended by more than 1,500 students.
This is the second math competition organized by Bright, while the first was held in 2021. In the second year, the student participation rate increased up to three times compared to the first year.
In order for students to be able to measure their level of math knowledge and be proud of the results, the Angkor Maths competition program has also carefully selected the subject level. According to El Nori, the course is organized by a doctor of mathematics and is available to both Cambodians and foreigners.
The students who participated in the competition were very happy and excited about this competition. The result is one thing for them, but what is more enjoyable is that this competition has made them aware of their level of mathematical ability, providing them with an experience to further develop their abilities.
While happy with the results, Ny Visal Snu revealed the reasons why he always applied for the math competition. For Ny Visal Snu, this competition always provides new experiences for him.
"When we come in, we see our own shortcomings that we want to improve," he said. It gives me a better understanding of not only the exercises in the book but also the exercises outside the book and not only stimulates my thinking.
The second gold medalist in the Angkor Maths competition praised the organization of the competition for giving students the opportunity to compete. It is also an opportunity for students to participate in extracurricular activities to gain experience and learn about knowledge that is not available in school.
The Angkor Maths competition in the finals saw many parents spend their time bringing their children to compete and encourage their children. This aspect clearly shows the strong support of parents for their education, which not only supports their budget but also their emotional support.
Parents expressed their happiness and satisfaction with the Angkor Math Competition, a rare event in Cambodia.
Mr. Meng Phalkuntha, the father of Meng Lay Sun student, said, "I am very proud and happy to hear the name of the first child in my heart. I am very excited and very proud of my son for his ability. Personal.
Mr. Meng Phalkun also praised and appreciated Bright Company for organizing this competition so that Cambodian children can show their abilities.
ADB approves $ 554 million package to support reconstruction efforts in Pakistan after devastating floods this year
Islamabad: The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has approved a $ 554 million financing package to support reconstruction efforts in Pakistan after this year's devastating floods, as well as disaster relief and rehabilitation. The country's climate resilience. This is according to the release by Xinhua on Monday, December 12, 2022.
The ADB said in a statement on Monday that the financing will support the rehabilitation of irrigation, drainage, flood risk management, farm water management and transport infrastructure in Balochistan, southwestern Pakistan. Severely affected by floods.
The Asian Development Bank (ADB) said its emergency flood relief project would also include climate and disaster response measures in infrastructure design, adding that it had relocated an additional 71 million existing loans. US dollars to support the government's flood response efforts.
