JAKARTA: The Indonesian Foreign Ministry said on Monday that Jakarta had summoned a United Nations (UN) official for comment after the top international body expressed concern over the threat. As for the rights and freedoms of the people, which may be due to the recent reforms of the Indonesian Penal Code. This was released by the AFP news agency on Monday, December 12, 2022.
Last week, the Indonesian National Assembly formally approved its criminal law reform, which includes a ban on extramarital affairs and cohabitation, as well as amendments to the law. Other controversies. Indonesian officials claim that the amendment aims to maintain "Indonesian values" in this large Muslim-majority country.
The United Nations has said that the revised penal code could lead to a sharp decline in freedom of the press, as well as privacy and human rights in one of the world's three largest democracies. This.
According to a spokesman for the Indonesian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the ministry summoned a UN coordinator in Jakarta over the UN comment, saying the UN should consult with the Indonesian government before expressing any misconceptions. It is public like this.
