The Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia has confirmed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is currently leaving for Brussels, Belgium to co-chair the ASEAN-EU Memorial Summit to celebrate the 45th Anniversary of the ASEAN-Dialogue Partnership. EU with Charles Michel, President of the European Council, to be held on December 14, 2022.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs said that the current Prime Minister was accompanied by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Minister Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, and Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports. And other senior government officials as well.
The Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs said that the Plenary Session of the Anniversary Summit will review current ASEAN-EU cooperation and set future directions for ASEAN-EU relations.
Leaders are expected to focus on ways to strengthen the economy and people-to-people contacts, digital transformation, connectivity, ensuring green change, energy and food security, and sustainable development. Leaders will also exchange views on regional and international issues of common concern and interest.
During the commemorative summit, a number of accompanying events will be held, including lunch, the 10th ASEAN-EU Business Summit Roundtable, the ASEAN-EU Youth Summit, the ministry said. And the celebration of ASEAN-EU People's Cooperation on Higher Education.
Please note that present in Europe now, before attending the Summit to commemorate the anniversary of Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen will pay a working visit to the French Republic. The President of the French Republic, Emmanuel Macron, will welcome the Prime Minister at the Élysée Palace and host a dinner in his honor.
During his stay in Brussels, the Prime Minister is expected to hold bilateral talks with a number of European leaders.
Samdech Techo will also have a working breakfast with Mr. Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of Vietnam and Mr. Phorn Kham Viphavan, Prime Minister of Laos.
