(Phnom Penh): In the Cambodian Book Fair from December 9-11, 2022, which is located in the National Library of Cambodia, Street 92, Sangkat Wat Phnom, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, we see students, Cambodians and people visit and buy Lots of books to read and explore.
Khmer civilization expert, Mr. Rath Sandab, said that when it comes to reading this book, whether it is our Khmer nation or the nations of the world, reading this book is very important because it cultivates and inspires. The ideas from the book help us to understand the reasons for illuminating the way for us to see what is good and what is bad.
Therefore, reading a book is the key to opening the door of our intellect to see a beautiful world, as well as entertainment, as well as to increase the imagination and have many benefits to the nerves and positive emotions. Well.
In short, the importance of reading a book is as follows:
Strengthen brain activity: Reading books stimulates our brain to remember and even expand our dreams and dreams towards growth and success.
* Increase communication: Reading books is a rich source of knowledge and makes us a more engaging conversationalist and can empower us to talk to more people from different backgrounds and experiences because we can connect based on Information shared from reading to enhance our conversation partner conversations beautifully.
Help yourself: Reading books can help us escape the dangers of life and lead our adventures to success. When we are reading a book, it can lead us to think of new things, to explore culture, history, economics, politics, social events, and world events that we have never heard of before, and to adopt thought-provoking thinking methods. Or enhance our identity.
* Increase intelligence: The more we read, the more we learn from books, because the more we read, the wider our minds become, and the more we benefit physically, mentally, and spiritually.
* Entertainment: Reading books is a form of entertainment that can lead us to timely evolution and the world of luxury.
* Provide good value: Reading books can teach us to promote self-worth and society by choosing and quoting a selection of good words to use in the family and society.
* Increase creativity: Reading books has the potential to increase our level of creativity for fun, stimulate new ideas or images in our minds that can result in creativity and expression. More comments.
Reduce stress: Reading books can reduce stress and increase our mental relaxation by focusing on the text of the book. Because reading books benefits from the benefits of meditation that reduces stress levels.
