Cambodia-China Friendship Radio UN Security Council approves resolution exempting humanitarian efforts from the effects of sanctions
NEW YORK (Reuters) - The United Nations Security Council on Friday passed a resolution authorizing humanitarian aid to operate unhindered to sanctions-imposed countries. UN, especially the freezing of assets. This was released by the AFP news agency on Saturday, December 12, 2022.
The text of the resolution emphasizes that the provision of "funds", "economic resources", "goods" or "services" necessary to ensure timely humanitarian assistance efforts is permitted and does not violate the sanctions imposed. Submitted by the UN Security Council. The resolution was passed by a 14-vote majority, except for India, which voted unanimously.
"I want to make it clear that this is not a matter of personal punishment," she said. Our goal remains the same: to prevent terrorists and human rights abusers by using the right means to maintain peace and security, but at the same time allow the necessary humanitarian efforts to save lives to take place for those in need. It.
In the past, when humanitarian organizations were affected by UN sanctions, the Security Council usually dealt with issues depending on the circumstances of each case. Therefore, the resolution passed on Friday broadly states that supportive activities for humanitarian efforts will not be considered in violation of UN sanctions.
This decision applies directly to UN institutions, as well as to international organizations and UN General Assembly observer humanitarian bodies such as the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC), as well as aid groups working with UN agencies. Nation.
An additional 65 million people will be in need of humanitarian assistance next year, bringing the total to 339 million in 38 countries, according to UN estimates in early December. The UN has announced a $ 51.5 billion budget for aid by 2023.
