This evening, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the Opening Ceremony of the 9th Sea Festival
(Preah Sihanouk): On Saturday evening, December 10, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the opening ceremony of the 9th Sea Festival, Round 3, which was held at Samdech Techo Square in Preah Krong. Sihanouk, Preah Sihanouk Province.
The Sea Festival was missed for two years, 2020 and 2021, due to the outbreak of Kovid 19. The Sea Festival in 2022 has been rescheduled after the Royal Government overcame 19 epidemics of Kovid, and this event is also an opportunity to promote the tourism potential of coastal tourism in Sihanoukville after the province has developed infrastructure in The city as well as the attractive coastal development.
This year's Sea Festival is organized under the theme "Beach of Peace, Beach of Hope".
Minister of Tourism Thong Khon said that the introduction of this topic is in line with the Cambodian context, where peace has played an important role in the development of the country, creating a strong hope for the whole people. In this sense, peace is absolutely indispensable for supporting the development of the nation, while many hopes for the future are creating more opportunities starting from this peace.
This year's Sihanoukville Sea Festival runs for three days from December 9 to 11. Accompanying the Sea Festival is a series of events such as sports competitions, art shows performed by celebrities, as well as exhibitions of food, beverage and other services.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, always presides over the Sea Festival every year. The presence of Samdech Techo clearly reflects the Royal Government's high priority in promoting tourism in the coastal area, as well as participation in the development and conservation of coastal areas.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen once said that the celebration of the Sea Festival not only contributes to the promotion of tourism potential of coastal provinces, but also supports the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the development of sustainable tourism and reception. High responsibility based on a clear common commitment to balance the economic, social, environmental and cultural interests of local people.
The Prime Minister also expressed the hope that the celebration of the Sea Festival will be a great new opportunity for Cambodia to make Cambodia's coastal cities and beaches become quality tourist destinations in line with the slogan. "Cambodian Coast: Star of the Southwest" as well as increase the spirit of patriotism, solidarity and friendship.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister called on the Cambodian people to participate in the sea festival in Sihanoukville now.
