The Minister of Information and the Minister of Culture open the 9th National Book Fair under the theme "One day, one day reading"
(Phnom Penh): Seeing that Cambodian students, youth and people love to read books and study to gain new knowledge, the 9th National Book Fair Organizing Committee 2022 organized a book fair under the theme "One day read, one day know."
The exhibition was presided over by Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, Dr. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Representative of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on the morning of December 9, 2022 at the National Library of Cambodia, Street 92, Wat Phnom Sangkat, Daun Penh District. Phnom Penh.
According to the report of Mr. Hok Sothy, a representative of the Organizing Committee of the 9th National Book Fair 2022, he recalled the success of the 8th National Book Fair 2019, which was attended by 3 days. About 180,000 people had 140 book stalls, compared to the first exhibition in 2010, which was attended by only 1,000 people in three days, with only 10 book stalls. For the ninth time, there were 198 booths.
Taking this opportunity, the Chairman of the Exhibition Organizing Committee requested all bookstore owners to help reduce the price of the book or provide it for free so that the prison officer, who is the librarian, can afford to buy and receive more books. Take it to the detainee for reading as well.
Through this request, Mr. Chhay Sophal, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Information and author of the book, also provided 5 books in 5 pages to the prison officials.
Following a series of keynote speeches by key stakeholders of the exhibition, including Mr. Prum Radio, Representative of the Director General of Tiger Bam, Mr. Fabrice Eden, First Adviser to the French Embassy in Cambodia, and Ms. Ton Saim, Under Secretary of State Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
Dr. Pheung Sakona encouraged all parents to have a library in each house so that their children and ourselves have the opportunity to read a lot of books, make children like to read books, get more knowledge and know the gratitude. The value of our Khmer national literature. Reading more books will make young people, who are the pillars of the nation, think, find responsibility, have virtues, live in a highly developed society.
Minister Khieu Kanharith said that in 2022, there will be a significant increase in both participants and booths at the Cambodia Book Fair 2022, which shows that now the general population, both old and young, are more interested in reading books as a bridge. Increasing knowledge.
As a result, young people have increased their knowledge of reading books, e-books, and the level of foreign language and technology.
