Cambodian Organization for the Elderly celebrates International Human Rights Day under the theme "Legal Support for the Rights of the Elderly"
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 9, 2022, the Cambodian Organization for the Elderly, in collaboration with the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, organized a celebration of International Human Rights Day under the theme: Law on the Rights of the Elderly ”to support the Cambodian Elderly Network.
The event was held at Mekong Tower 01, Phnom Penh, with the participation of Mr. Nhem Bunthean, Deputy Director General of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, Ms. Ou Vanda, President of the Cambodian Elderly Network, Mr. Tum Vira, Executive Director of the Cambodian Elderly Organization and speakers. Many honors.
The celebration of International Human Rights Day in Phnom Penh was attended by a total of 128 participants from 14 capitals and provinces of Cambodia, representing nearly 30,000 elderly people, with support from the Dutch Government and the European Union, as well as German donors. .
This important event is organized under the theme "Legal Support for the Rights of the Elderly", which focuses on understanding the needs and priorities of older people in relation to legal support for their rights. To be an input for the relevant ministries and institutions to consider or consider in the process of drafting the old human rights law in the next step.
The Cambodian Organization for the Elderly is a local non-governmental organization that works with the elderly so that they can lead a dignified, active, healthy and safe life. The organization has been present in Cambodia since 1992 and has completed its mission in the eight provincial capitals of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Please note that the Cambodian Elderly Network is a platform for the Association of the Elderly, NGOs and other institutions to work together in order to improve the quality of life of the elderly and contribute to the effective implementation of policies. Beneficial for the elderly. This morning, the National Council for Social Protection organized a press conference on the mechanism and procedures for implementing the cash subsidy program for vulnerable families.
