(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan has agreed to provide $ 506,595 to two recipients under a grant scheme for the Small-Scale Human Security Project (Kusanoni Grant). For the improvement of facilities at the rehabilitation center, fitness and construction of maternity and neonatal care facilities at the hospital.
The grant agreement was signed on December 08, 2022 by Mr. Taninai Ichitomo, Ambassador of the Embassy of Japan to the Kingdom of Cambodia; Takeo Provincial Rehabilitation Center, Mr. Yin Sinath, Director of Kampong Cham Provincial Referral Hospital to implement the following projects:
First, the project to purchase machines to make artificial equipment and build a dormitory for the rehabilitation center of Takeo province in Takeo province (budget 162,715 US dollars) Recipient: Rehabilitation center of Takeo province.
The grant will be used to install 15 types of equipment for the production of prosthetics and rehabilitation equipment and to build a nursing home at the Takeo Provincial Rehabilitation Center (PRC) in Takeo Province.
The PRC has been facing a number of problems due to the deterioration of equipment currently needed to produce prostheses and satellites and the dilapidation of nursing homes. Through this project, we expect that 700 patients who come to PRC every year will benefit from better facilities and services.
Second: Project for construction of maternity and newborn care building at Kampong Cham Provincial Referral Hospital in Kampong Cham Province (US $ 343,880) Recipient: Kampong Cham Provincial Referral Hospital.
The grant will be used to build a three-story building for maternity and neonatal care at Kampong Cham Provincial Referral Hospital in Kampong Cham. The hospital has been facing issues such as overcrowding in the current maternity ward for mothers and time spent transporting newborns in emergencies to distant neonatal care units. .
Through the construction of this new maternity and neonatal facility, we expect the hospital to be able to provide more affordable accommodation for new mothers and to provide the necessary treatment for infants with immediate needs.
