(Kiev): Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky has said that Ukraine cannot fully rebuild its energy infrastructure, which has been attacked by Russia, and urged its own people to cope. This is according to the publication by the Russian newspaper RT on Thursday, December 8, 2022.
"Ukrainians should not forget that it is now impossible to restore 100% of our energy infrastructure to what it was before Russia launched an attack," Zelesky said in a video message. "We need time and this is why power outages are still in place in most cities and regions of Ukraine," Zelensky added.
The Russian military has been targeting Ukraine's energy infrastructure since October, days after an attack on a Crimean bridge, which Russia has blamed on Ukrainian military intelligence.
US, Russia compete to sell arms to Vietnam at first large-scale arms show in Hanoi
HANOI (Reuters) - US and Russian defense companies on Thursday showcased state-of-the-art weapons and unveiled new aircraft models at Vietnam's first large-scale weapons exhibition event as the top two countries Compete for influence and arms sales in this ASEAN country. This was released by the AFP news agency on Thursday, December 8, 2022.
The arms show, held at an air base in Vietnam's capital Hanoi, attracted a total of 174 defense companies from 30 countries, including major arms manufacturers except China. The invitation was declined.
US Ambassador to Vietnam Marc Knapper says the arms show represents a new phase in Vietnam's efforts to globalize, diversify and modernize its military, and that the United States wants to be part of its mission. This effort.
Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh has said that Hanoi is now aiming to diversify its weapons imports with the aim of defending the country. Vietnam's military diversification could be widely seen as a representation of Russia's reliance on weapons for its weapons, but analysts say that any change could be significant. Slowly.
Russia is Vietnam's largest arms supplier, accounting for about 80 percent of Hanoi's demand, but Moscow's arms attractiveness has declined significantly in recent years as the war continues. Ukraine has put pressure on exports of its defense equipment, and sanctions have made many countries reluctant to buy weapons from Russia.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth announced to provide flowers for those who wish to decorate their houses and locations.
