More than 2,400 officials and youths prepare to collect garbage during the Sea Festival in Sihanoukville
(Preah Sihanouk): More than 2,400 government officials, law enforcement, as well as people and young people or more are ready to participate in collecting garbage to clean the environment at the main sites of the 9th Sea Festival in Sihanoukville From 9-11 December 2022. This is according to Mr. Huot Rithy, Director of the Department of Clean City Protection and Promotion of the Ministry of Tourism.
His remarks were made at a workshop on improving the quality of tourism services towards the celebration of the ninth round of the 9th Sea Festival, which was held on the morning of December 8, 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Tith Chantha, Secretary of State The Ministry of Tourism represents Minister Thong Khon at the Sokha Hotel in Sihanoukville.
On that occasion, Mr. Huot Rithy mentioned about the problem of garbage that has occurred in organizing small and large programs such as Water Festival in Phnom Penh, Kandal Province, Battambang Province, Sea Festival in Koh Kong Province, Kampot Province and so on.
He said that in order to solve all these problems, the professional officers of the Ministry of Tourism have put forward a number of solutions that focus on education, training, environmental clean-up activities and practical garbage collection, and raising awareness among tourism business owners, as well as General participants.
For example, during the Sea Festival in Sihanoukville, the Ministry of Tourism received a total of 100 bins to provide more options for participants in addition to what the provincial administration has already prepared.
Mr. Huot Rithy confirmed the activities of collecting garbage and cleaning the environment on the morning of December 10, 2022 in Poy Samdech Techo with 716 participants and the tree of love with 1,699 participants in collaboration with Ministry of Tourism and Administration of Preah Sihanouk Province. On the morning of December 11, 2022, there will be activities at Ochheuteal Beach (Bathroom 1) and Otres Beach with similar participants on the 10th.
In addition, there is the 42nd VIP booth, which broadcasts educational videos related to littering and educational games, as well as prizes.
Mr. Huot Rithy called on tourists and people to participate in the Clean Cambodia Campaign on the occasion of this Sea Festival to revitalize the event to be clean, hygienic, beautiful and ensure a clean and happy environment.
Permanent Secretary of State Tith Chantha thanked Total Energy through the National Committee for Clean City Assessment, Ministry of Tourism, for donating 100 bins for sanitation, especially during the Sea Festival.
He also requested the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration, authorities at all levels and the private sector to work together to maintain security, public order and the beauty of the city on the occasion of the Sea Festival, based on Sihanoukville as the winner of the romduol flower. Three branches of the National Clean City Competition in the past and also the winner of the ASEAN Clean City in the past.
15 drug smuggling suspects shot dead by Thai border patrols
BANGKOK: Thai soldiers clashed with drug smuggling suspects in a forested area north of the Myanmar border on Thursday, killing 15 people, Thai authorities said on Thursday. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Thursday, December 8, 2022.
Thai soldiers met with a group of suspects carrying backpacks on Wednesday evening and ordered them to stop, but they refused to stop and even launched a combat operation with authorities. This is according to the military unit in charge of security in the northern border provinces of Thailand.
An investigation is ongoing into whether the suspect brought methamphetamine from Myanmar. It is a frequent drug smuggling route into Thailand. The exact amount of drugs seized was not immediately known.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, told the media that during the farewell meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the afternoon of December 8, 2022, the outgoing Ambassador congratulated Samdech Techo and the Royal Government. Successfully chairing and chairing the ASEAN Summit as well as the relevant summits. The Ambassador also congratulated the successful management of Kovid 19.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth said that in this meeting, the Ambassador also evaluated and highly appreciated the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. The leadership that the Ambassador demonstrated and admired included: Leading and building Cambodian society from the ashes of war to the stage of tremendous development over the past 30 years.
The Ambassador also praised and appreciated Samdech Techo's foreign policy on the decisions related to the Ukraine-Russia conflict and Myanmar's efforts to resolve the issue. In particular, strengthening and promoting the relationship between Cambodia and Japan to become a comprehensive strategic partner in 2023.
In this meeting, the Ambassador also informed Samdech Techo that his mission in Cambodia achieved good results with the full support of Cambodia's public and private institutions. He also informed Samdech Techo that Japan continues to support Cambodia in its development work and that Japan is currently helping to train Cambodian players for next year's SEA Games.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Ambassador for his many actions to promote relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Japan.
Regarding the Russia-Ukraine issue, Samdech Techo told the Ambassador that the decision was in line with international law. As for the Myanmar issue, Samdech Techo stressed that Cambodia has made great efforts to normalize the situation, but now it is time for Indonesia to help resolve it as the chair of ASEAN.
