Minister Sok Chenda Sophea Leads a Cambodian Delegation to the 25th Greater Mekong Subregion Ministerial Conference in Laos
(Phnom Penh): The 25th Greater Mekong Sub-region Ministerial Conference was held on December 6-8, 2022 under the theme "Accelerating Economic Recovery to Extend GMS's 30-Year Achievement Towards Sustainable Development and Environment ”in Luang Prabang Province, Lao People's Democratic Republic.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Minister in charge of the Greater Mekong Subregion Program, led the Cambodian delegation to the conference, which was attended by representatives of GMS member countries, representatives of the Asian Development Bank, representatives of development partners and the private sector, a total of about 100 people. .
The Ministerial Conference aims to review the progress of the implementation of initiatives under the GMS Cooperation Program and discuss development-related issues aimed at improving the integration, competitiveness and development of health and the environment. Local communities in the subregion.
Meanwhile, delegates from member countries also celebrated the 30th anniversary of the establishment of the GMS program, celebrating the achievements of the past, especially the implementation of investment projects under the GMS program, which has exceeded 30 billion. US $.
The projects cover agriculture, energy, environment, health, human resource development, information technology, tourism, transportation, trade facilitation and urban development, while further achievements are expected by 2030.
At the same time, the GMS Minister also expressed his satisfaction with the progress of the implementation of investment projects under the GMS framework, as of 2022, about 63% of 205 projects have been completed and / or started.
In addition, the conference also reviewed and approved the GMS Investment Framework 2023-2025, which has a total of 111 projects, including 16 projects in Cambodia (12 transport projects, 1 agricultural project, 1 environmental project, 1 health project and information). Science 1 project).
Speaking at the GMS Ministerial Conference after a two-year absence due to the Kovid-19 pandemic, Sok Chendasophea stressed the need to continue to push for closer regional cooperation to strengthen the environment. , Sustainability and resilience of development, especially in the current uncertain economic context.
In this regard, the Minister also encouraged the Asian Development Bank, other development partners and the private sector present at the conference to continue to support each other to address the challenges towards achieving the Greater Mekong Subregion vision. 2030 as directed by the GMS Head of Government at the 7th GMS Summit.
The Minister also stressed the need to improve the resilience of the regional supply chain to ensure the region's attractiveness for attracting more investment and trade flows.
This requires the region to carefully consider and identify measures to improve the investment climate by seizing the opportunities for effective digitalization in trade and investment facilitation.
