90-year-old still struggling to make ends meet
(Kampong Chhnang): A 90-year-old woman struggles to make a living on her own without relying on her children, which disrupts their education, even though she is now very old. She still struggles to survive on her own until her last breath.
Kong Yim is now 92 years old and lives alone in a small hut in Umpor village, Svay Chrum commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province. Buy food.
Her business of harvesting grass for sale Every day, she harvests 2 to 3 bags and sells them to the villagers in the village at a price of 15,000 riel per bag. She said that in the beginning, when she was still strong, she worked as a laborer, transplanting and harvesting rice, but later, as she got older, her strength decreased and she could not work far away, so she changed her job to harvest. Grass near the house for sale.
