Leaders of the Ministry of Tourism advise tourism business owners not to increase service fees excessively
(Preah Sihanouk): In order to organize the 9th Sea Festival Round 3 with the hosting of the conference of the most beautiful beach club in the world in Preah Sihanouk province, success and excellence, Mr. Tith Chantha The Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism has advised tourism business owners to pay attention to their services and not to increase the service fee excessively.
Mr. Tith Chantha said this at a seminar on improving the quality of tourism services to celebrate the 9th Sea Festival, Round 3, 2022 under the theme "Beach of Peace, Beach of Hope" accompanied by a certificate and Letter of commendation to the tour operator of the destination province at the Sokha Beach Hotel on the morning of December 8, 2022.
Mr. Tith Chantha said, "We would like to ask all businesses that have received commendation in 98 locations and receive commendation letters in 82 locations, as well as all businesses to make efforts to serve customers with good quality and not to install. Excessive service fees that can cause a bad image will not affect the tourist destination of Sihanoukville and the coast.
He also requested the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration, authorities at all levels and the private sector to work together to maintain security, public order and the beauty of the city on the occasion of the Sea Festival, based on Sihanoukville as a winner. Three branches of the National Clean City Competition Movement in the past and also the winner of the ASEAN Clean City Competition.
At the same time, Mr. Kim Sereyroth also urged all business owners when there is an increase in the price of their services to be clearly informed or have a price list closed at their business base for guests to know in advance. Those who receive the service will not have to increase the price unnecessarily and without the approval of the experts.
