Two Cambodian Blue Hat Troops Return Home After Mission in Mali
(Phnom Penh): Two Cambodian Blue Hat forces, the Airport Engineering Force and the 9th Explosive Ordnance Disposal Unit (EOD), have returned home after completing a humanitarian peacekeeping mission under the United Nations umbrella. National in Mali.
The reception ceremony of the Airport Engineering Force and the Explosive Ordnance Disposal (EOD) Force was held this morning, December 8, 2022, under the chairmanship of General Sem Sovanny, Vice Chairman of the National Coordinating Committee for sending troops to join the organization's peacekeeping mission. United Nations and Director-General of the National Peacekeeping Center at Phnom Penh International Airport.
Upon arrival at the airport, all forces were immediately screened for 19 cases of Kovid and malaria before being allowed to meet with their families.
The General emphasized that the two forces have participated in carrying out fruitful tasks with great success and more proud new results. Unexploded ordnance (UXO) crews and airport engineers worked tirelessly under the Sahara sandstorm, with temperatures reaching 53 degrees Celsius.
Taking this opportunity, the General would also like to thank the Head of the Royal Government, the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense, and the National Committee for always considering our visit to our forces on a regular basis and to strictly implement the "3 Do's and 3 Defenders" measures. The Royal Cambodian Armed Forces is a model for our family, ourselves and our society as a whole.
Unexploded ordnance (UXO) forces deployed 144 positions in GAO, MOPTI and TIMBUTU, including 11 women, clearing mines, clearing unexploded ordnance and clearing explosives and improvised explosive devices. For the airport engineering force stationed in Kidal and Tesalit with a force of 154 people, of which 15 women are in charge of airport maintenance and other construction work.
