First. Explore the possibility of creating new mechanisms and establishing an open platform to support government in education and industry, including promoting digital connectivity.
Second. Share information, experiences and best practices on the formulation and implementation of industry promotion policies 4.0.
Third. Develop an ASEAN Integration Strategy on Industrial Development 4.0, emphasizing the promotion of innovation and the technology industry.
Fourth. Strengthen cooperation in the development of legal frameworks to support ASEAN-to-Industry Transformation 4.0 through public-private dialogue, in collaboration with international organizations and development partners, with the aim of facilitating compliance and certification of digital standards, facilitating data flow. Cross-border and develop a common platform for linking industry statistics through the use of digital technology.
Fifth. Participate in solving the challenges that will arise from the growth of Industry 4.0 in ASEAN and find solutions to meet those challenges.
He also congratulated the Indonesian Engineering Institute for receiving the flag of the ASEAN Engineering Federation to host the 41st ASEAN Engineering Federation Conference 2023. Ministry of Foreign Affairs issues press release on the second bilateral consultation between Cambodia and Colombia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation this morning, December 8, 2022, issued a press release on the second bilateral consultation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Colombia.
In this regard, the two sides reviewed bilateral relations and exchanged views and updated on various topics of mutual interest, including development cooperation, national unification, trade, investment, education, tourism, agriculture. Demining and peacekeeping operations. Due to the limited trade volume between the two countries, the two sides agreed to work together to promote trade between the two countries.
In this regard, Mr. Ouch Borith informed the parties about the favorable conditions of the business environment and investment policy in Cambodia and requested the organization of a business forum following the next bilateral consultation meeting in Phnom Penh to expand active business links between the two countries. Both countries.
In the field of tourism, the two sides agreed to increase tourism cooperation and assist each other in organizing tourism promotion activities and encourage people to travel to their respective countries. In this regard, the Colombian side requested the Cambodian side to consider raising visas for ordinary passport holders.
In the field of education, the Colombian side welcomed Cambodia's request to sign a memorandum of understanding between the two countries' diplomatic institutes and pledged to continue to provide Spanish language scholarships to Cambodian officials in the coming years.
The Colombian side has also decided to provide master's and doctoral scholarships to Cambodian students from 2023 onwards.
The two sides expressed their commitment to strengthen cooperation in the agricultural sector through technology sharing, especially rice breeding, training and exchange visits by competent authorities and experts. The Colombian side also proposed a joint training project between the two countries on agriculture through the National Training Service of the Colombian Ministry of Labor.
For cooperation on demining and peacekeeping, the Colombian side thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for providing demining training to more than 180 Colombian officials since 2010.
Mr. Ouch Borith expressed the support of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the training of Colombian officials for another three years (2023-2025) within the framework of the Cambodia-Japan-Colombia trilateral cooperation.
The two sides also exchanged views on mutually beneficial regional and international issues, including geopolitical aspects, as well as support for multilateralism and the UN-based international system.
Ouch Borith noted Colombia's goodwill and commitment to strengthening its relationship with ASEAN and forging closer cooperation between ASEAN and South America.
The two sides agreed to boost bilateral ties and continue to support each other in the international arena for the common benefit of both countries and peoples.
The two sides also agreed to hold major events to mark the 50th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Colombia. Mr. Ouch Borith sincerely thanked the Colombian side for printing postage stamps as a symbol of friendship between the two countries on this precious occasion.
