General Knowledge: Which image on the US dollar bank is not the image of the President of the United States?
(Phnom Penh): "US Dollar" is an international currency that circulates around the world. On each dollar bill are portraits of important figures in history that are no different from the currencies of other countries. But do you know whose faces are on those banknotes, as some people mistakenly think they are all US presidential faces?
TOKYO (Reuters) - Japan's foreign exchange reserves hit a six-year high in November as a weaker dollar boosted asset prices, the Ministry of Finance said on Wednesday. Foreigners who are not dollars. According to Reuters.
Japan's foreign exchange reserves rose 2.65 percent from October to 1.226 trillion US dollars at the end of November, the first increase in a year, Reuters reported, citing a Japanese Finance Ministry official. Four months and the highest growth since December 2016.
Investors are scrutinizing Japan's foreign exchange reserves and interventions for clues as to how much money Japan could spend to curb the yen's depreciation despite the weakening dollar. Recently, the pressure on the Japanese currency has eased.
The dollar has fallen about 10 percent against the yen since hitting a 32-year high of nearly 152 yen in October. The dollar weakened amid rising expectations that the Fed's sharp rate hike could hit record highs and inflation could reach near record highs.
Japan's foreign exchange reserves fell in September and October, with authorities intervening to sell and buy the yen as authorities struggled to contain a sharp depreciation of the yen against the dollar. Rising foreign bond yields also reduced the value of currency reserves.
According to the Japanese Ministry of Finance, due to the fact that those factors are no longer active, other factors that drive Japan's reserves, such as interest earned on foreign bond holdings, declining bond yields abroad Rising euro against the dollar and higher gold prices boosted Japan's foreign exchange reserves in November. According to Reuters.
German authorities have arrested a total of 25 members and supporters of the right-wing terrorist group on Wednesday, German authorities said on Monday. Arrested during operations across Germany on suspicion of plotting to overthrow the government. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, December 7, 2022.
The German military intelligence agency BAMAD said that among those arrested and under investigation were a professional soldier and some reservists, while a professional soldier was a member of the headquarters. Special Forces.
The suspects have been accused of preparing for at least the end of November 2021 to act on their ideology. These activities include buying equipment, recruiting new members, and practicing shooting. Efforts to recruit members are primarily focused on German military and police officers.
The operation was carried out with the participation of more than 3,000 police officers and security forces in 11 German states.
Minister of Agriculture Assigns Dr. Yang Saing Komar to Solve Rice Problems (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, confirms that he has assigned Dr. Yang Saing Koma And Secretary of State for the Ministry of Agriculture to address the rice issue.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Dith Tina holding a talk with the press on "Agriculture in Cambodia" at the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on December 6, 2022.
Mr. Dith Tina stated, "I have assigned His Excellency Yang Saing Koma to help him work through the agricultural contract, which is a big project that he has to work with farmers and mills to prepare production plans. With the repurchase.
Mr. Dith Tina also said that the intervention to keep the price of rice stable depends on facilitating the movement of rice into the rice mill, which must be arranged to cooperate between farmers and mills. Milling rice by creating a series of harvests, not flooding at the same time.
The Minister of Agriculture stressed that the Ministry of Agriculture will cooperate with the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture to provide loans to farmers to buy rice from farmers to avoid congestion.
