Cambodia-Japan launches Cambodia-Japan digital production center with three CNC machines worth over $ 4 million
CJDM will be a training ground for Cambodian human resources to work in industry 4.0 for the advancement of science and technology in Cambodia. The CJDM comes after efforts to build bilateral relations between the Cambodian and Japanese leaders.
Mikami Masahiro said that three different types of advanced CNC machines worth about 500 million yen (US $ 4.5 million) have been provided to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports through a Japanese government grant project. Used in professional training courses at RUPP that will train highly skilled engineers in the context of Industry 4.0.
Please be informed that after the bilateral meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Mr. Kesida Fermio, Prime Minister of Japan at the Peace Palace on the evening of March 20, 2022, during the visit of the Prime Minister of Japan to Cambodia, both sides released A joint statement, which also mentions investments for the future of Asia.
With the cooperation of Japan, CJDM will train human resources using various metal components using digital technology to produce parts and components for domestic use, reduce imports.
