The Pentagon said in a statement on Tuesday evening that part of the sale would support Taiwan's F-16 fighter jets, Taiwan-made fighter jets and other aircraft. Various accessories originating in the United States. Washington has said it will help him and strengthen the capacity of the Taiwan Air Force in the face of current and future threats.
The Taiwan Defense Ministry said Wednesday that the sale is expected to take effect within a month and will serve as a major boost as China seeks to normalize its military activities in Taiwan. Near Taiwan and put pressure on Taiwan's air and sea, as well as the training capabilities and response of Taiwanese military forces.
At present, Taiwan's air force is well-equipped but older and lower than China's. Taipei has often complained that for the past three years, Chinese military aircraft have been operating daily near its territory.
The National Assembly thanked all stakeholders for successfully co-organizing the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly.
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly thanked the Armed Forces, civil servants, youth, artists, and working groups from relevant institutions for successfully co-organizing the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly. This is according to the thank you statement received by Fresh News on December 7, 2022.
"The Secretary-General of the National Assembly is very honored and very grateful and grateful to the Armed Forces, Civil Servants, Civil Servants, Youth, Artists and the team from The relevant institutions that have co-organized the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly in the past have had a glorious success.
The National Assembly appreciated and highly appreciated all the ladies and gentlemen who paid attention to the high responsibility in performing the above tasks. At the same time, there are also compliments from national and international delegations.
The National Assembly considers these noble cooperation as a great contribution to the honor and prestige of the motherland.
The announcement came after Chinese President Xi Jinping chaired a meeting of the Communist Party's Politburo on Tuesday.
Ministry of Education: All the worksheets of the candidates for the Baccalaureate have been delivered to Preah Sisowath High School (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has confirmed that as of 2 pm on December 7, In 2022, all the worksheets of the candidates of the high school diploma exam, examination period: December 5, 2022, were transported from the provinces to Preah Sisowath High School.
The Ministry confirms that all the worksheets of the candidates are kept properly and securely under the strict supervision of the National Committee of the Capital-Provincial Ministries and the Anti-Corruption Unit.
The World Bank report, obtained by Fresh News, states that in the December 2022 Cambodia Economic Update, the World Bank forecasts that Cambodia will have 4.8 percent economic growth in 2022, including a post-modern economic recovery. Epidemics are on the rise, in part due to the recovery of tourism.
Economic growth is projected to reach 5.2 percent by 2023 as employment growth will further boost domestic consumption accompanied by a slowdown in inflation. However, the prospects for faster growth still face serious risks due to the evolving situation outside of Cambodia.
Cambodia has a small economy that is open to foreign trade and foreign investment, and the outlook for global growth remains bleak. Global trade growth slowed in the second half of 2022 and is projected to slow sharply in 2023. The economies of developing countries such as Cambodia are particularly vulnerable, especially as inflation rises, global economic growth slows, energy supplies fall and interest rates rise.
Cambodia's manufacturing sector relies on export markets for growth, and it will be adversely affected as slower growth lingers in its two largest export markets, the United States and the European Union. Similarly, investment and capital inflows are likely to decline due to the gradual decline in capital from China, Cambodia's largest source of foreign direct investment to date.
In order to protect its economy from the impact of declining demand abroad, Cambodia should take steps to strengthen its fiscal position and boost the economy in the country, said Mariam Sorman, World Bank Country Director for Myanmar, Cambodia and Laos. The district, especially its attractive tourism industry for the world.
"Revenues have increased due to the economic recovery and the improvement of the administration," she said. Expanding the tax base will help ensure the resources needed to boost Cambodia's economy and to withstand the downturn among major trading partners. "Tourism and hospitality are potential sectors for future growth."
In the long run, Cambodia's economy is expected to continue to grow at a rate of about 6 percent as international and domestic tourism grow stronger. Cambodia's participation in the recently signed trade agreement could also boost the agricultural sector and the agro-processing industry.
The special section of this report examines the impact of inflation on poverty. This section highlights the need to protect the most vulnerable, along with the expansion of tentatively targeted temporary social protection programs. The Cambodia Economic Update report focuses on short- and medium-term macroeconomic developments and is published twice a year.
Minister of Information Holds the 7th Meeting of the ASEAN Senior Officials Working Group on Information in Siem Reap, Cambodia Supports the Establishment of the ASEAN Working Group on False Information
The meeting was held at the Regency Angkor Hotel, Siem Reap, from December 6-9, 2022, with the invitation of senior information officers representing each of the 10 ASEAN member countries. Through the online video system.
Minister Khieu Kanharith said this was the first time for the Cambodian Ministry of Information to host the ASEAN Media Summit after the 1919 Kovid epidemic, which changed its way of life and work and affected Economy, trade, tourism and other sectors around the world.
According to the Minister, amid the spread of Kovid 19, false information and false information have risen to a high level, affecting politics, economy, security, social and cultural order is indisputable and disturbs the unity and peace of the country. To create mistrust, divisions and violence between people, aggravate and undermine people's confidence in the media.
During the global epidemic, false information spread faster than viruses, causing great anxiety and fear in people's hearts and distrust in a community. The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, reiterated in early 2020 that "Kovid-19 is a vicious disease, but false information is more vicious."
Media literacy and media literacy have become increasingly important tools in society for combating false information, teaching people how to collect, verify and use information properly and ethically in the world of social media. Which leads to the reduction of false information.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith shared some experiences in the fight against false information in Cambodian society. In addition to the introduction of media and information literacy, the Ministry of Information also established an Anti-False Information Committee at the ministerial level in mid-2020.
The Cambodian Ministry of Information fully supports the establishment of the ASEAN TFN and highly appreciates the outcome of its first meeting in October this year. The Ministry also welcomes actions proposed by Australia to support the TFFN under the auspices of the ASEAN-Australia Political-Security Partnership.
The 7th meeting of the SOMRI Working Group on Media Information and Training is a contribution to help ASEAN journalists and media organizations take drastic measures to strengthen the quality of the media.
Cambodia deports 148 more foreigners after arrests for crossing the border and staying illegally
From December 4 to 6, 2022, the General Department of Immigration deported 148 foreigners, 10 females of 3 nationalities, including 145 Chinese and 2 Koreans. A man and an Estonian leave Cambodia in accordance with the Immigration Law at the Phnom Penh International Airport and Prek Chak International Border Police.
The statement added that the 148 foreigners were arrested in connection with the theft of residence and illegal work in violation of the law on immigration, with the eviction of the Ministry of Interior and ban. Entered Cambodia for 3 years.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth officially announces the "Vision and Strategy for the Harmonization of 3 + 1 Reform of the Royal Government"
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth stated that the vision and strategy on the harmonization of the three-plus-one reform aims to ensure the harmonization of the reforms based on past achievements and experiences leading to the achievement of policies and strategies. Of the Royal Government in response to the evolving situation of the global context.
He said that in addition to this, the Royal Government must also consider efforts to strengthen its capacity within the framework of the rapid development of technology in the era of Industrial Revolution 4.0.
In order to achieve the vision of "Harmonization of 3 + 1 Reform" and the mission of "Ensuring the consistency and efficiency of the management and coordination of the 3 + 1 Reform Program", Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth has provided four recommendations or approaches. Focus on the implementation of our reform work as follows:
First. The whole vision-keeping approach refers to the fact that one reform program is dependent and dependent on another, intertwined and indispensable in the overall context of reform. For example, the transfer of functions requires the review and preparation of a set of rules and procedures at the same time as the transfer of financial and human resources, as well as an overview of the legal and procedural framework, and the judiciary.
Second. Role-contribution approach refers to: Each reform program must complement each other individually according to their roles and responsibilities within the framework of their respective institutional functions as defined by applicable laws and regulations.
Third. The approach to maintaining ownership and supporting cooperation is to respect ownership of progress and accountability for its reform programs, and to provide support and willing cooperation with other reform programs.
Fourth. The proactive approach is to prepare to solve problems or prevent problems from occurring through the three-plus-one reform coordination mechanism, without waiting for problems to occur before taking action.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch Meets MAG Executive Director on Mine Action Cooperation in Cambodia
On that occasion, once again, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Senior Minister Ly Thuch expressed his congratulations on the 30th anniversary of the establishment of MAG in Cambodia in participating in the work of humanitarian mine action, as well as saving lives and Provide safe land to local people.
The Senior Minister appreciated and thanked all the efforts and dedication of all MAG leaders and staff and considered MAG as an important partner not only in clearing mines and unexploded ordnance. Only the field is a strategic partner for 30 years. The Royal Government of Cambodia will continue to provide support and cooperation to MAG in the Mine Action Partnership in Cambodia.
At the same time, the Senior Minister told the Executive Director of MAG that for the past 30 years, Cambodia has been among the countries in the world that carry out large-scale humanitarian demining and is recognized as a leading country and ranked No. 1 in the field. Largest demined land.
He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia has paid close attention to the work of clearing mines and unexploded ordnance, especially recently, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the occasion of the closing ceremony of the 30th anniversary of mine action in Cambodia. Accelerate demining work and reduce the Royal Government's budget of 30 million dollars to support the goal of Cambodia by 2025.
It should be noted that from 1992 to 2022, MAG cleared 124.7 square kilometers of landmines and unexploded ordnance, found and destroyed 84,188 mines, 32,171 cluster munitions and explosive remnants. From other wars, 288,049 bullets, with more than 2 million beneficiaries, and 37,710 explosive ordnance education.
